{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_149","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'tail -12 cores/bench/implementation_notes.md'","aggregated_output":"\nEX exports the value and eligibility it writes to EX/MEM, including formatted load data and jump links. The existing interlock supplies the M-use bubble. The existing clock enables hold both operand registers and their override bits through repair and denied data requests. The address predictor continues to use its original base matches.\n\nDirected tests cover simultaneous EX and MEM producers on opposite ports, a denied signed halfword load, a trapping load shadowing an older multiply, and a store that needs the product on both ports through address repair and three denied cycles. An adjacent ADD checks the single M-use bubble. The jump-target test also consumes the link on the target's first instruction.\n\nVerilator lint and all 100 cocotb tests passed. The selftest and three random instruction traces matched the ISS with and without stalls. Co-simulation validated the CoreMark CRCs. Ten CoreMark iterations took 3,234,996 bracketed cycles.\n\nGowin placements 0, 1 and 2 reached 75.421, 80.207 and 80.207 MHz. The 80.207 MHz median falls below the 85.328 MHz baseline and the 89.25 MHz target. On placement 1 the replay lookup took 17.762 ns, and the path from the rs1 M override through the integer addition to the next rs2 register took 17.760 ns.\n\nI retained the proposed two-input EX muxes. A trial combining immediate selection with M forwarding and simplifying the branch comparison reached 78.115 MHz median. Parallel ALU result masks reached 78.326 MHz median. Extending that trial to capture the register ALU operand in the immediate field and replay both source tags from distributed RAM reached 77.376 MHz median.\n\nThe local single-channel ALTOPS formal suite passed all 53 checks on the submitted RTL. I ran several instruction checks from the generated makefile in parallel with the main run. Every check produced a PASS result, and `formal/run_all.sh` exited successfully on its first run for this RTL.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
