{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_132","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"rg -n '(Top module|rvfi_order)' CLAUDE.md | head -4\nrg -n '(nret:|io_rvfi_valid_0\\\\s+=|io_rvfi_order_0\\\\s+=|io_rvfi_rd_wdata_0\\\\s+=)' cores/bench/core.yaml cores/bench/rtl/core.sv\"","aggregated_output":"11:| 1 | Top module `core` exposes an RVFI port set selected by `cores/<target>/core.yaml`'s `nret` field (default 2). **nret=1**: only `io_rvfi_*_0` ports exist; the single retirement always lands on channel 0. **nret=2**: both `io_rvfi_*_0` and `io_rvfi_*_1` exist; channel 0 carries the older of two simultaneous retirements, channel 1 the younger; single-retire cycles MUST place the retirement on channel 0 with `io_rvfi_valid_1 = 0`; all channel-1 ports MUST be driven (no X/Z, tie unused fields to `'0`). | cocotb smoke test, `riscv-formal` wrapper (`wrapper.sv` for nret=2, `wrapper_si.sv` for nret=1) |\n14:| 4 | `rvfi_order` strictly monotonic +1 per retirement across both channels combined (no gaps, no duplicates). When both channels retire in the same cycle, channel-0 order = N and channel-1 order = N+1.                                       | `riscv-formal unique` check                  |\n100:- `nret: 1` — single-issue. Top module exposes only `io_rvfi_*_0`\n107:  wider contract). Top module exposes both `io_rvfi_*_0` and\ncores/bench/rtl/core.sv:12:// CLAUDE.md invariant 1 under `nret: 1` (declared in core.yaml). The\ncores/bench/rtl/core.sv:37:  // declared via `nret: 1` in core.yaml). Channel 0 is the sole\ncores/bench/rtl/core.sv:275:    io_rvfi_valid_0     = mem_wb_w.valid;\ncores/bench/rtl/core.sv:276:    io_rvfi_order_0     = rvfi_order_q;\ncores/bench/rtl/core.sv:288:    io_rvfi_rd_wdata_0  = rd_wen ? wb_w_data   : 32'b0;\ncores/bench/core.yaml:6:nret: 1\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
