{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_133","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"git diff --check\ncat cores/bench/implementation_notes.md\nrg 'FAIL|ERROR|PREUNSAT' \\\"\"'$TMPDIR/formal-delivered.out\" | tail -1'","aggregated_output":"# Decode-stage older bypass\n\nID captures the completed MEM result or the write-first register-file value independently for each source. Both operands retain that fallback even when EX names the same destination. A registered tag match and the producer's trap-checked EX/MEM forwardable bit select the younger result in EX. MEM/WB samples the same result wire as ID, including products and divides in hardware and ALTOPS mode.\n\nTwo timing refinements qualify and prioritize address producers. Decode clears the register-write control for rd=x0, so each downstream tag match can use the producer's existing write enable. Decode also computes the EX address candidates in parallel with the source-tag comparisons. The youngest matching writer selects the candidate and its availability. A late MEM producer still requires address repair, and adjacent M dependencies still take the original interlock.\n\nThe regression exercises a multiply followed by a misaligned load to the same register, an aligned load that wins over the multiply, writes to x0, and a denied store that takes its base and data from different producers. It checks RVFI operands, the trap, and accepted bus transfers.\n\nThe direct implementation measured 76.454 MHz median in Gowin. Its placements 1 and 2 were limited by the integer result feeding back through EX. Placement 0 was limited by instruction readiness through the address predictor to data RAM. Trials that reordered the PC/immediate input muxes or moved carry-chain results to the final ALU selection produced lower frequencies than the delivered RTL.\n\nThe final Gowin placements reached 80.654, 83.766, and 83.766 MHz. The median corresponds to 258.94 CoreMark iterations/s, 1.83% below the 85.328 MHz champion at the same cycle count. It misses the 89.26 MHz acceptance threshold. All three placements were limited by the path from the instruction successor RAM through the decode address candidates to data RAM.\n\n| Placement 1 setup path | Required clock period |\n| --- | ---: |\n| Successor RAM through the decode address candidate to data RAM | 11.938 ns |\n| EX/MEM result through branch resolution to ID/EX PC | 11.937 ns |\n| Registered younger rs1 match through the ALU to the EX/MEM result | 11.908 ns |\n| EX/MEM operation through the MEM multiplier and fallback mux to ID/EX rs1 | 11.899 ns |\n\nThe final RTL passed Verilator lint and all 99 cocotb cases. The selftest matched the ISS with and without stalls. Stalled CoreMark matched all five CRCs, printed the validation message, and completed without an out-of-bounds access. The markers at cycles 11,828 and 3,246,824 bracketed exactly 3,234,996 cycles.\n\nThe ALTOPS formal suite is in progress.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
