{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_138","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'git diff --check && git status --short --ignored && cat cores/bench/implementation_notes.md && for f in cores/bench/rtl/*.sv; do cmp \"$f\" \"$TMPDIR/addi-eval/formal/riscv-formal/cores/bench-wyfDMiO1V/${f##*/}\" || exit 1; done'","aggregated_output":" M cores/bench/rtl/core.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/ex_stage.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/id_stage.sv\n M cores/bench/test/test_pipeline.py\n!! .agent.last\n!! .agent.log\n!! cores/bench/implementation_notes.md\n!! formal/riscv-formal\n# ADDI address bypass\n\nID reuses a matching EX ADDI's registered `mem_addr` when its base was available and its displacement stayed on the same 4 KiB page. The next ADDI, load, or store copies that page and adds its displacement to the low 13 bits. A younger writer owns the base even when its address is unavailable. A dependent memory instruction then spends one cycle repairing its address from forwarded rs1 before it issues a request.\n\nID reads LUI's immediate from ID/EX. The EX operand buses now stay in EX. This removes the 32-bit ADD base calculation and the three-input low-address compressor. The ALU supplies the exact ADDI result to register consumers and retirement.\n\nThe pipeline regression checks consecutive same-register writes, signed displacements, a page crossing and return, and a multiply-dependent ADDI. It checks retired values and all accepted transfers, including the full address across a denied request. The existing ADD and AUIPC tests each require one repair cycle.\n\nVerilator lint passed. Pipeline tests and five-ELF cosimulation passed, including both stall modes for the four trace programs. Stalled CoreMark validated all five CRCs. Ten iterations took 3,240,833 bracketed cycles, from 11,974 to 3,252,807.\n\nThe three Gowin placements reached 73.366, 79.724, and 79.724 MHz. The 79.724 MHz median gives 246.00 CoreMark iterations/s, below the requested acceptance point of approximately 89.4 MHz. On the median placement the critical path starts at `older_rs2_q`, passes through the forwarded branch comparison and redirect, and ends at the ID/EX PC register.\n\nThe implementation applies the ADDI certificate to the next slot's `base_available` bit. The page and low sum can be selected in parallel with this check. Gating the address mux itself with the certificate reduced the median to 77.996 MHz. A separate trial that also retimed ordinary operand forwarding reached 84.292 MHz and still missed the threshold. The delivered change retains the existing operand forwarding and repair handshake.\n\nLocal ALTOPS formal passed all 53 checks on the first run of the delivered RTL, with zero failures.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
