{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_185","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/implementation_notes.md'","aggregated_output":"# EX/MEM result partition\n\nEX/MEM captures two 16-bit banks for the low half (shift and nonshift) and three for the high half (ADD, SUB and other). Both arithmetic operations use 32-bit operands and produce a full 32-bit sum or difference before slicing. ID registers mutually exclusive integer ALU enables. Its validated load and jump controls select the formatted bus word or PC+4. Every bank shares the pipeline advance, so repair and a denied request preserve both halves of the resident bypass value.\n\nBoth EX operands, the ID memory-base predictor and MEM consume the registered banks' OR. The shifter reverses the bit order for SLL to share a barrel with SRL and SRA. The forward unit registers the source grants on the producer's transfer edge using its trap-checked write enable and late-result flag. The ID address predictor reuses the decoded ADD enable.\n\nThe directed pipeline test checks each retired destination and data word, order, PCs, bus requests and memory masks. It exercises SUB bit 25 through SRLI into address bit 4, carry and borrow at bit 16, signed and unsigned loads, signed shifts, both jump links and three consecutive denials per memory request.\n\nVerilator lint and all six cocotb runners passed. Selftest and all three random trace programs matched the ISS with both ready modes. Ten stalled CoreMark iterations ran from cycle 11,828 to 3,246,824, giving 3,234,996 bracketed cycles. The five CRCs were e9f5, e714, 1fd7, 8e3a and fcaf. UART reported “Correct operation validated.” The run completed without an out-of-bounds access.\n\nGowin placements 0, 1 and 2 reached 80.631, 81.906 and 81.906 MHz. The median missed the 89.25 MHz threshold by 7.344 MHz and gives 253.19 iterations/s. The median placement's longest setup path ran from the successor RAM through displacement selection and the ID address adder to data RAM. A second address path began at the registered rs2 forwarding grant. Neither low result bank appeared as a destination in this placement's 25 worst setup paths.\n\nThe local single-retirement ALTOPS formal suite is in progress.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
