{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_60", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'git diff -- cores/bench/test/test_pipeline.py | tail -105 && cat cores/bench/implementation_notes.md'", "aggregated_output": " \n+@cocotb.test()\n+async def branch_held_behind_store(dut):\n+    store = SW(1, 0, 0x44)\n+    program = [\n+        ADDI(1, 0, 37), ADDI(2, 0, 37), store,\n+        BEQ(1, 2, 8), store, JAL(3, 8), store, ADDI(4, 3, 7), EBREAK(),\n+    ]\n+    fetches = []\n+    store_cycles = 0\n+\n+    def bus_ready(pc, addr, ren, wen, data):\n+        nonlocal store_cycles\n+        fetches.append(pc)\n+        assert not ren\n+        if wen:\n+            # The held branch compares x2 forwarded from MEM/WB on every cycle.\n+            assert (pc, addr, wen, data) == (20, 0x44, 15, 37)\n+            store_cycles += 1\n+            if store_cycles <= 3:\n+                return 1, 0\n+            return 0, 1  # Accept the store and deny its younger branch's target.\n+        return 1, 1\n+\n+    rets, dmem = await _run(dut, program, bus_ready=bus_ready, unready_instr=store)\n+    assert store_cycles == 4 and dmem == {0x44: 37}\n+    assert fetches[:9] == [4, 8, 12] + [20] * 5 + [28]\n+    pcs = [0, 4, 8, 12, 20, 28, 32]\n+    assert [r[\"pc\"] for r in rets] == pcs\n+    assert [r[\"pc_next\"] for r in rets[:-1]] == pcs[1:]\n+    assert [r[\"insn\"] for r in rets] == [program[pc // 4] for pc in pcs]\n+    assert [r[\"order\"] for r in rets] == list(range(len(pcs)))\n+    assert all(not r[\"trap\"] for r in rets)\n+    assert rets[3][\"rs1_rdata\"] == rets[3][\"rs2_rdata\"] == 37\n+    assert rets[4][\"cycle\"] == rets[3][\"cycle\"] + 2  # one denied target fetch\n+    assert rets[5][\"cycle\"] == rets[4][\"cycle\"] + 1\n+    assert rets[4][\"rd_wdata\"] == rets[5][\"rs1_rdata\"] == 24\n+    assert rets[5][\"rd_wdata\"] == 31\n+\n+\n @cocotb.test()\n async def divider_dependencies_with_stalls(dut):\n     mask = 0xFFFFFFFF\n@@ -403,6 +443,7 @@ async def branch_taken_skips(dut):\n     assert pcs == [0, 8, 12], f\"unexpected retirement PC sequence: {pcs}\"\n     [r2] = _by_insn(rets, ADDI(2, 0, 42))\n     assert r2[\"rd_wdata\"] == 42\n+    assert r2[\"cycle\"] == rets[0][\"cycle\"] + 1\n \n \n @cocotb.test()\n@@ -422,14 +463,15 @@ async def jal_writes_pc_plus_4(dut):\n     assert rj[\"rd_wdata\"] == rj[\"pc\"] + 4\n  \n…[1831 of 4903 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:aead6de780c753a3]…\n0, 1, 1, 1, 0, 0]\n+    assert all((r[\"rd\"], r[\"rd_wdata\"]) == (0, 0) for r in rets[2:5])\n+    assert rets[5][\"rd_wdata\"] == 8\n \n \n @cocotb.test()\n# Fetch the resolved target in EX\n\nEX selects the instruction bus address for taken branches, JAL and JALR. Otherwise IF selects the resident EX PC plus four. IF records the bus address on each non-reset edge and reissues it when ID/EX is empty. A target can enter ID/EX on the edge its branch or jump advances.\n\nID/EX holds during a data-bus stall or divide wait. A denied fetch or a load/multiply dependency inserts a bubble when EX advances. Misaligned taken transfers trap and fall through, and a trapping jump suppresses its link write.\n\nThe directed tests check adjacent retirement cycles for ready targets, including a JALR with a forwarded base and an odd sum. They also check skipped fetch addresses, denied reads carrying store instructions, a branch held behind a stalled store, a denied target on the store release edge, and fall-through after misaligned transfers.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
