{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_105","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cat cores/bench/implementation_notes.md\nrg -c 'DONE \\\\(PASS' \\\"\"'$TMPDIR/formal-qual.log\"\nrg '\"'DONE \\\\((ERROR|FAIL)' \\\"\"'$TMPDIR/formal-qual.log\" | tail -n 4\ntail -n 3 \"$TMPDIR/cosim-final.log\"\ndate -u'","aggregated_output":"# EX load and store issue\n\nDecode computes two byte addresses in parallel. One sum uses the EX/MEM result or the write-first register file. The other uses the preceding LUI immediate or the raw bus word of an aligned LW. The youngest writer selects the address that enters ID/EX. An ADD base costs one bubble, and a multiply base waits until writeback.\n\nEX drives the registered address and forwarded store data. A verified, aligned request holds ID/EX, EX/MEM and the replay verification state until acceptance. MEM/WB clears its valid bit during the wait and retains the operand that may still be feeding the store. On acceptance, EX captures the formatted load for forwarding and the raw word and address for RVFI. Misaligned accesses trap with zero memory masks and suppress the destination write.\n\nThe directed tests check consecutive retirements through LUI, two dependent word loads, a taken branch and its target, including replay during denied fetches. They also check arithmetic and multiply base dependencies, byte lanes, sign extension, misalignment, and stable requests across stalls. Denying fetch when a stalled store completes exercises both an aliased successor store and a successor load whose base now points into MMIO.\n\nThe self-test and three random programs matched the reference with both buses ready and with both stall generators enabled. Ten CoreMark iterations took 3,320,238 cycles between the MMIO markers, saving 166,671 cycles from the champion. All five CRCs and the UART validation banner matched.\n\nReplay annul clears the valid bit and the controls for memory, writes, hazards and redirects. Lane selection and ALU operands can settle independently. A bubble clears the controls and validity in ID/EX and EX/MEM, allowing the wide payload registers to omit their bubble reset. MEM formats the captured raw word for writeback and computes products. The core retains its configured single RVFI channel.\n\n| Gowin placement option | Fmax (MHz) | CoreMark iterations/s |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n| 0 | 65.108 | 196.09 |\n| 1 | 65.941 | 198.60 |\n| 2 | 65.941 | 198.60 |\n\nThe median throughput is 12.49% above the champion. Placement used 3,822 logic cells. All three worst setup paths cross the divider recurrence. The measured median is 1.259 MHz below the scratch prototype.\n13\n  \"passed\": true,\n  \"elfs_tested\": 5\n}\nFri Nov 20 05:49:59 UTC 2026\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
