{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_109","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"rg -n '53 checks|97 cocotb|81.075|3,234,996|Zero-divisor' cores/bench/implementation_notes.md; tail -n 2 \\\"\"'$TMPDIR/div-final-formal.log\"'","aggregated_output":"7:**Zero-divisor handling** uses the radix-8 path. Setup seeds the quotient with 14 ones and the remainder with the high 14 dividend bits. All seven trials fit on each step, so the quotient becomes all ones and the remainder recovers the entire dividend magnitude. This eliminates a separate saved-dividend register.\n12:- Local formal passed all 53 checks with zero failures using `formal/run_all.sh` and the bench core's single-retire configuration. The preprocessed ALTOPS token stream for `alu.sv` matched the baseline exactly. The integer-reference vectors and ISS comparisons exercise the real arithmetic.\n13:- All 97 cocotb cases passed across six pytest runners, including the divider integer-reference and stalled pipeline tests. Added vectors cover every narrow digit threshold, the four low-bit suffixes at shared thresholds, the mode boundary, the largest wide quotient, signed operands and zero divisors. The tests also exercise alternating modes, reset during either mode, delayed consume and held MEM results.\n14:- Selftest and all three random ELF traces matched the ISS with and without bus stalls. Stalled CoreMark passed all five CRC checks and printed the validation message. The ten iterations ran from marker cycle 11,828 to 3,246,824, or 3,234,996 bracketed cycles.\n18:Gowin placement options 0, 1 and 2 reached 77.777, 81.075 and 81.075 MHz. The **81.075 MHz median yields 250.62 CoreMark iterations/s**, a 10.44% gain over 226.92. The netlist uses 4,443 logic cells, 939 registers, six BSRAMs and five DSPs. The worst setup path in each placement starts at the instruction successor RAM and ends on the data-memory address path.\n\nFormal: 53 passed, 0 failed\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
