{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_205","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"rg -n 'TESTS=|testsuite' cores/bench/test/*.xml | cut -c1-160 | head -8; git diff --check; cat cores/bench/implementation_notes.md\"","aggregated_output":"cores/bench/test/test_reg_file_runner.result.xml:1:<testsuites name=\"results\">\ncores/bench/test/test_reg_file_runner.result.xml:2:  <testsuite name=\"all\" package=\"all\">\ncores/bench/test/test_reg_file_runner.result.xml:9:  </testsuite>\ncores/bench/test/test_reg_file_runner.result.xml:10:</testsuites>\ncores/bench/test/test_imm_gen_runner.result.xml:1:<testsuites name=\"results\">\ncores/bench/test/test_imm_gen_runner.result.xml:2:  <testsuite name=\"all\" package=\"all\">\ncores/bench/test/test_imm_gen_runner.result.xml:12:  </testsuite>\ncores/bench/test/test_imm_gen_runner.result.xml:13:</testsuites>\n# M-result interlock at EX\n\nThe forwarding unit samples the producer's effective M-result control on the same edge as the candidate's two source matches. The existing comparisons exclude x0. A divide holds those registers until its transfer edge.\n\nThe core combines the registered dependency with the successor-address annul. A rejected slot clears EX validity and the controls for memory operations, redirects and register writes. IF selects the saved retry PC and the producer advances toward WB. The hazard unit now flushes ID only for an invalid fetch when EX can advance.\n\nThe initial implementation reached 76.783 MHz. Its timing report showed the replayed rs1 field on the path to the ID address calculation. The implementation stores those five bits in a separate distributed RAM with the same read and write enables and the same collision check. It also registers the trap-checked bypass selects on the producer's transfer edge to shorten the path from tag matching to the EX operands.\n\nThe pipeline regression trains a cached store after a divide, denies fetch through the next divide's transfer and its first retry, and checks the store address, data, issue count, retirement order and cycle spacing.\n\nVerilator lint, pipeline cocotb tests and cosimulation passed. The stalled CoreMark run completed ten iterations in 3,234,996 bracketed cycles with the expected CRCs. Gowin placement options 0, 1 and 2 reached 81.519, 80.185 and 80.185 MHz, respectively. That median gives 247.87 iterations per second and falls short of the requested 84.80 MHz. The median placement's longest path runs from a registered forwarding select to the EX/MEM result register. Gowin reports 5,006 logic cells and 96 LUT-RAMs, including the replay bank.\n\nThe first implementation passed all 53 local formal checks. On this RTL, 52 checks have passed and the register consistency check is running.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
