{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_9", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"cat cores/bench/LESSONS.md; rg --files cores/bench/test; sed -n '1,260p' tools/eval/gowin.py\"", "aggregated_output": "- 2026-11-20 hyp-20261120-001-r1s0 (regression, +471.20%): Eight serial trial subtractions on the `partial_q` feedback path limited median Fmax to 31.094 MHz versus 41.649 MHz for six steps per clock, while CoreMark executed no DIV/REM between markers to benefit from the shorter divide latency.\n- 2026-11-20 hyp-20261120-002-r1s1 (improvement, +665.10%): Moving combinational `/` and `%` off the shared EX result path into a six-cycle restoring divider raised median Fmax from 5.442 to 41.649 MHz without adding divider stalls because CoreMark issued no DIV/REM between its markers.\n- 2026-11-20 hyp-20261120-003-r1s2 (regression, +6.19%): Predicting branches by displacement bias and taking JAL in fetch saved 302,818 CoreMark cycles by avoiding EX redirects, while the combinational DIV/REM path still limited median Fmax to 5.392 MHz.\n- 2026-11-20 hyp-20261120-001-r2s0 (regression, +10.91%): Replacing six serial trials with three radix-4 stages that test divisor multiples in parallel raised median Fmax from 41.649 to 46.194 MHz, exposing the path from the register file through hazard logic to ID/EX as the new timing limit.\n- 2026-11-20 hyp-20261120-002-r2s1 (improvement, +12.46%): Registering 3D, 5D and 7D let two radix-8 stages replace six serial trial subtractions, raising median Fmax from 41.649 to 46.838 MHz at the same 4,491,485 CoreMark cycles, with the single-cycle multiplier limiting both median-frequency placements.\n- 2026-11-20 hyp-20261120-003-r2s2 (regression, +10.77%): Predicting branches and JAL in fetch avoided EX redirects and saved 302,818 CoreMark cycles, but the six-step divider’s `remainder_q` feedback path limited median Fmax to 43.026 MHz, leaving throughput below the radix-8 core (102.72 vs 104.28 iterations/s).\n- 2026-11-20 hyp-20261120-001-r3s0 (regression, +18.45%): Registering four multiply partial products at EX/MEM raised median Fmax from 46.838 to 55.927 MHz, while registering the forwarded operands and doing the full multiply in MEM reached 62.078 MHz with the same 0.81% CoreMark cycle pena\n…[15979 of 19051 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:902fff6f367ae4ae]…\n:\n            print(f\"place_option {r['place_option']}: FAILED ({r.get('reason')})\")\n            continue\n        print(f\"place_option {r['place_option']}: Fmax {r['fmax_mhz']} MHz, {r['levels']} logic levels; \"\n              f\"logic {r['logic']}, registers {r['regs']}, LUT-RAM {r['lutram']}, BSRAM {r['bsram']}, DSP {r['dsp']}\")\n        tr = (wt / \"cores\" / a.target / \"generated\" / \"timing\" / f\"gowin_p{r['place_option']}\" / \"impl/pnr/core_bench.tr\")\n        for i, p in enumerate(critical_paths(tr.read_text(errors=\"replace\"), a.paths), 1):\n            print(f\"  path {i}: {p['arrival_ns']} ns, {p['logic_cells']} cells, {p['from']} -> {p['to']}\")\n            print(f\"          through: {' > '.join(p['modules'])}\")\n        print(f\"  full report: {tr}\")\n    if len(res) > 1 and all(not r[\"placement_failed\"] for r in res):\n        print(f\"score Fmax (median): {summarize(res)['fmax_mhz']} MHz\")\n    return 0 if all(not r[\"placement_failed\"] for r in res) else 1\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    raise SystemExit(main())\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
