{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_199","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'git diff --stat && git diff --check && cat cores/bench/implementation_notes.md'","aggregated_output":" cores/bench/rtl/alu.sv            | 37 ++++++++++++++++++------------\n cores/bench/rtl/core.sv           | 17 +++++++++-----\n cores/bench/rtl/core_pkg.sv       | 16 +++++++++++--\n cores/bench/rtl/ex_stage.sv       | 30 +++++++++++++++++++------\n cores/bench/rtl/id_stage.sv       | 28 +++++++++++++----------\n cores/bench/rtl/mem_stage.sv      |  3 ++-\n cores/bench/test/test_alu.py      | 24 +++++++++++++++++++-\n cores/bench/test/test_pipeline.py | 47 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++\n 8 files changed, 160 insertions(+), 42 deletions(-)\n# Carry-select forwarding\n\nEX computes the 16-bit low sum and carry alongside two 16-bit upper sums for ADD, ADDI, AUIPC and SUB. SUB complements the second operand and seeds the low adder with one. EX/MEM holds the carry and both upper candidates. MEM selects the upper half once for forwarding, address prediction and writeback. Loads, jump links and other integer results use the primary half with a clear carry select.\n\nID reuses the EX sum for the ADD base page and computes the low 13 address bits independently from the two operands and the displacement. ID/EX holds both candidate upper halves until EX drives the request. An address repair overwrites the primary address and clears its carry select. A denied request holds the entire representation.\n\nTen CoreMark iterations took 3,234,996 bracketed cycles, matching the champion. Gowin reported 81.296, 78.937 and 78.937 MHz for placement options 0, 1 and 2. The 78.937 MHz median gives 244.01 iterations/s, 7.49% below the champion. Acceptance required 89.26 MHz. In the median placement the registered carry fed a critical path through operand forwarding and the shifter into low result bit 10. In placement 0 the carry-to-successor-PC path was worst.\n\nTwo forwarding experiments also preserved the cycle count. Giving the shifter direct access to rs1 and preparing RF and WB address candidates in parallel yielded a 77.409 MHz median. Registering separate upper forwarding enables for each consumer reached 79.602 MHz with 5,047 logic cells and 984 registers. I retained the requested shared MEM selection for both operands, ID and writeback. It uses 5,010 logic cells and 978 registers.\n\nVerilator lint and all 100 cocotb cases passed. Selftest and three random programs matched the ISS with and without bus stalls. CoreMark passed CRC validation. The directed pipeline test checks a carried ADD base, a denied store, a repaired load, consecutive branch and JALR forwarding, and AUIPC-to-load forwarding across bit 16.\n\nLocal formal has passed 52 of 53 checks on the retained RTL. The register-consistency check (`reg_ch0`) is still solving its depth-20 assertion and has produced no counterexample. A discarded forwarding variant hit a Yosys frontend error on assignments to individual fields of a function return. Returning the packed value as one assignment resolved the elaboration error.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
