{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_78","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cat cores/bench/implementation_notes.md; git status --porcelain=v1 | cut -c1-110; rg -n '\"'^[ '\"\\\\t]*Path1\"'$'\"' \\\"\"'$TMPDIR/split-final-timing\"/gowin_p1/impl/pnr/core_bench.tr | head; date -u'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_78","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cat cores/bench/implementation_notes.md; git status --porcelain=v1 | cut -c1-110; rg -n '\"'^[ '\"\\\\t]*Path1\"'$'\"' \\\"\"'$TMPDIR/split-final-timing\"/gowin_p1/impl/pnr/core_bench.tr | head; date -u'","aggregated_output":"# Split integer sums and dependent replay\n\nEX computes the exact low 16 bits of ADD, ADDI, SUB and AUIPC. A second adder starts at bit 12 with the sign of effective B as its carry-in. Its bits 31 through 16 form the provisional upper half. Subtraction complements B and seeds the exact low sum with one. Both the EX bypass and the ADD address predictor use the provisional result. The true low carry and the predicted bit-16 carry cross the EX/MEM boundary in separate registers.\n\nMEM corrects the provisional upper half with parallel bit toggles for an increment or decrement. A single exact result feeds the register-file write, the same-edge ID read and the WB retirement record. ID uses direct array reads for its address candidates and schedules EX repair for a corrected MEM base.\n\nAn admitted consumer with a registered raw source match replays on a carry disagreement. Its producer drains to WB, its matched operands capture the exact value, and its bypass selectors clear. A matched base loses its precomputed address. The replay edge suppresses bus strobes, redirect and divide issue. An independent successor advances in the ordinary pipeline.\n\nThe core keeps its declared single RVFI channel. The standalone register file retains write-first reads and shares its storage module with the core. The standalone ALU retains exact ADD and SUB. A Verilator-only `+split_stats` option counts replay and repair edges between accepted marker writes.\n\n## Local verification\n\n- Verilator `--lint-only -Wall -Wno-MULTITOP` passed.\n- Selftest and all three random ELFs passed full RVFI cosimulation at zero wait and with both stall generators enabled. The stalled ten-iteration CoreMark run reached EBREAK, reported `Correct operation validated.`, and matched all five expected CRCs.\n- The start and stop writes occurred at cycles 11,877 and 3,249,030. The 3,237,153 measured cycles included 2,002 dependent replays and 693 address repairs. This adds 2,157 cycles to the supplied baseline.\n- Directed pipeline tests cover both carry-error directions, independent and raw-tag-only dependencies, shift, branch, store, divide, AUIPC, x0, fetch denial and data backpressure.\n- The single-channel ALTOPS formal suite and the three final Gowin placements are running.\n M cores/bench/rtl/alu.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/core.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/core_pkg.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/ex_stage.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/forward_unit.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/id_stage.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/mem_stage.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/reg_file.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/wb_stage.sv\n M cores/bench/test/test_pipeline.py\nrg: /srv/hwebench/tmp/3c491641/a63cff08/split-final-timing/gowin_p1/impl/pnr/core_bench.tr: IO error for operation on /srv/hwebench/tmp/3c491641/a63cff08/split-final-timing/gowin_p1/impl/pnr/core_bench.tr: No such file or directory (os error 2)\nFri Nov 20 17:44:15 UTC 2026\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
