k. 2nd column (where present) is the k-induction prove\n# depth. Keep depths matched to the current pipeline so bugs within ~20\n# cycles of any symbolic instruction stream are exposed.\ninsn          20\nreg       10  20\npc_fwd    10  20\npc_bwd    10  20\ncausal    10  20\n# unique   — no two retirements share rvfi_order (catches double-retire)\n# cover    — sanity that the CPU r\n…[2029 of 5101 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:c78b53e3549f54bd]…\n\":\ntools/eval/formal.py:113:                the subprocess environment so run_all.sh picks up that\ntools/eval/formal.py:125:    run_script = worktree_path / \"formal\" / \"run_all.sh\"\ntools/eval/formal.py:128:                'detail': f'formal/run_all.sh missing in {worktree}'}\ntools/eval/formal.py:134:    env = {**env, \"FORMAL_WORK_ID\": work_id}\ntools/eval/formal.py:169:                'detail': (f'run_all.sh exceeded {e.timeout}s wall-clock'\ntools/eval/formal.py:175:        # run_all.sh prints a final \"Formal: <N> passed, <M> failed\" tally line.\ntools/eval/formal.py:182:                # `no_checks_generated` is run_all.sh's fallback when the\ntools/eval/gowin.py:22:GOWIN_HOME = Path(os.environ.get(\"GOWIN_HOME\", \"/opt/gowin\"))\ntools/eval/gowin.py:23:GOWIN_VERSION = \"1.9.11.03 Education\"\ntools/eval/gowin.py:35:    libs = [GOWIN_HOME / \"deps/root/usr/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu\", GOWIN_HOME / \"IDE/lib\"]\ntools/eval/gowin.py:133:        proc = subprocess.Popen([str(GOWIN_HOME / \"IDE/bin/gw_sh\"), \"build.tcl\"], cwd=outdir,\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
