{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_94","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"git status --short; git diff --check; cat cores/bench/implementation_notes.md | tail -9; python3 -c 'from pathlib import Path; import xml.etree.ElementTree as E; print([(p.stem, len(E.parse(p).findall(\\\".//testcase\\\"))) for p in sorted(Path(\\\"cores/bench/test\\\").glob(\\\"*result.xml\\\"))])'\"","aggregated_output":" M cores/bench/rtl/core.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/core_pkg.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/ex_stage.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/id_stage.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/mem_stage.sv\n M cores/bench/test/test_pipeline.py\nThe pipeline tests cover back-to-back load and replayed branch retirement, stale-store suppression at loop exit, base producer priority, misaligned accesses, subword extension and stable store data during a five-cycle denial.\n\nVerilator lint and the cocotb suite passed. All four short ELFs matched the reference in both bus modes. Ten CoreMark iterations took 3,235,202 bracketed cycles with both stall generators enabled, saving 251,707 cycles. The run reached EBREAK, stayed within bounds and passed the canonical UART and CRC checks.\n\nGowin placement options 0, 1 and 2 reached 62.247, 62.236 and 62.236 MHz. The median gives 192.37 iterations/s, 8.96% above 176.55. Option 0 used 4,107 logic cells and 974 registers. The design matched the prototype's cycle count and fell short of its reported 64.712 MHz median. The critical path on options 1 and 2 runs from the WB destination through register-file forwarding and address generation to dmem.\n\nA separate 12-cycle BMC passed with symbolic instruction words, read data and both ready inputs. It checked the byte address of every valid EX memory operation against forwarded rs1 plus the decoded immediate. It also checked that address, read enable, write mask and write data stay stable across a denied request.\n\nThe 53 standard single-channel formal checks are running on the final RTL.\n[('test_alu_runner.result', 23), ('test_decoder_runner.result', 30), ('test_imm_gen_runner.result', 8), ('test_mul_product_runner.result', 2), ('test_pipeline_runner.result', 27), ('test_reg_file_runner.result', 5)]\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
