X as the new timing limit.\n- 2026-11-20 hyp-20261120-002-r2s1 (improvement, +12.46%): Registering 3D, 5D and 7D let two radix-8 stages replace six serial trial subtractions, raising median Fmax from 41.649 to 46.838 MHz at the same 4,491,485 CoreMark cycles, with the single-cycle multiplier limiting both median-frequency placements.\n- 2026-11-20 hyp-20261120-003-r2s2 (regression, +10.77%): Predi\n…[4009 of 7081 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:352f02653c0cf29a]…\ngistering both producer tag matches in decode took the comparisons off the EX operand path and raised prototype median Fmax from 68.274 to 76.825 MHz, while `ex_mem_w.forwardable` kept a trapping younger writer from masking the older value.\n- 2026-11-20 hyp-20261120-002-r7s1 (regression, +10.13%): With forwarding matches registered in ID, splitting at divisor magnitude 2^17 limited divider feedback to two 20-bit radix-8 stages for small divisors or one full-width stage for large divisors, yielding 222.86 CoreMark iterations/s versus 226.92 for the design that forwarded DIV/REM from MEM/WB.\n- 2026-11-20 hyp-20261120-003-r7s2 (regression, +6.03%): Reading a 512-row table in ID let EX replay denied RAM loads when the tag matched and all requested byte lanes were valid, saving 132,870 cycles over ten CoreMark iterations, too few to offset the higher Fmax of the retimed divider and forwarding design (214.58 vs 226.92 iterations/s).\n-rwxr-xr-x 1 nobody nogroup 24968 Jul 10  2025 /opt/gowin/IDE/bin/gw_sh\n/opt/gowin\n", "exit_code": 1, "status": "failed"}}
