{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_56","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/implementation_notes.md'","aggregated_output":"# Registered rs1 in successor replay\n\nThe implementation follows the proposed split. A 512 × 5 distributed RAM stores instruction bits 19 through 15. Its five output flip-flops capture the same lookahead index on the same edge as the successor block RAM. Both banks share the write enable, stall, collision guard and row validity, including the reset and FENCE.I sweep. A ready fetch supplies the entire live instruction. A replay uses the five registered bits and the rest of the block RAM row.\n\nThe full-PC comparison clears validity and the branch, jump, JALR, memory-read, memory-write, register-write and late-result enables for a rejected replay. EX can select operands and calculate its discarded result in parallel with the comparison.\n\n## Measurements\n\n| Gowin placement option | Fmax |\n| --- | ---: |\n| 0 | 75.641 MHz |\n| 1 | 85.328 MHz |\n| 2 | 85.328 MHz |\n\nWith both stall generators, ten CoreMark iterations took 3,234,996 cycles between the MMIO markers. The median gives **263.77 iterations/s**, 5.25% above 250.62. The median clears the 84.805 MHz threshold by 0.523 MHz. Option 0 falls below that threshold. Its design uses 4,965 logic cells and 944 registers, increases of 522 cells and five registers.\n\n## Verification\n\n- The standard single-channel formal suite passed all 53 checks on its first run using `wrapper_si.sv` and `checks_si.cfg`.\n- Verilator lint passed with all requested warnings enabled. All 98 cocotb cases passed.\n- The new pipeline case trains a four-instruction loop for two iterations, then denies every loop fetch for four iterations while driving a store on imem. Each load waits through three data-bus denials. The test checks the held and accepted addresses, retired instruction stream, x1 and x30 operand values, destination data and absence of store strobes.\n- Selftest and all three random ELF retirement traces matched the reference with and without stalls. CoreMark reported all five expected CRCs and the validation banner.\n- A separate induction check passed for an arbitrary replay index. Both banks contain the last written rs1 at that index. A noncolliding read captures that value in both outputs, which retain it through stalls.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
