{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_125", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/implementation_notes.md; ls -lh cores/bench/implementation_notes.md'", "aggregated_output": "# Middle-carry prediction\n\nEX splits integer addition and subtraction at bit 16. An exact 17-bit low operation supplies the low result and boundary carry. A second carry chain starts at bit 12 with the sign guess and keeps result bits 31 through 16. A generate or kill in bits 15 through 12 makes the upper result exact. Only a fully propagating nibble can require repair.\n\nADD and SUB use separate carry chains to keep the operation select off the forwarded B inputs. SUB uses the equivalent borrow representation, where borrow equals the complement of the two's-complement carry. On a miss EX saves the exact carry. Injecting it at bit 12 on retry supplies it at bit 16 because all four intervening bits propagate.\n\nOnly valid ADD, ADDI, AUIPC and SUB instructions writing nonzero rd can interlock. A miss holds ID/EX, EX/MEM, fetch replay state and forwarding selects. MEM/WB retires once and retains its data. EX/MEM and the dependent address predictor take the same ADD result on the transfer edge. ID keeps its independent three-input low displacement sum and the existing memory-address repair. The core uses the single RVFI channel declared by its `nret: 1` configuration.\n\nThe directed pipeline tests cover both miss directions, a SUB borrow, an AUIPC miss, a discarded x0 write, an annulled ADDI replay, and an immediately dependent store denied three times. They check retirement order, PCs, source and destination values, memory masks and every accepted transaction. The ALU test sweeps all 256 pairs of prediction nibbles for ADD and SUB.\n\n## CoreMark\n\nTen iterations took **3,239,407 bracketed cycles** with both random bus stalls enabled. The start and stop writes occurred at cycles 11,877 and 3,251,284. This is 4,411 cycles above the champion's 3,234,996 (+0.136%). All five canonical CRCs matched and CoreMark printed `Correct operation validated.`\n\nA simulator probe counted **3,532 carry-miss clocks and 3,532 retry clocks** between the markers. The arithmetic retirement trace independently accounts for 2,010 ADDI repairs, 1,010 ADD repairs and 512 SUB repairs. Each pair of miss and retry clocks adds one clock to its producer's execution.\n\n## Gowin timing\n\n| Placement option | Fmax (MHz) | Critical path |\n| --- | ---: | --- |\n| 0 | 76.098 | Older rs2 forwarding select through carry verification to the data-memory address |\n| 1 | 77.287 | MEM/WB result bit 14 through carry verification and divider start to quotient bit 20 |\n| 2 | 77.287 | Same endpoints as placement 1 |\n\nThe **77.287 MHz median** gives **238.58 CoreMark iterations/s**, 9.55% below the champion's 263.77. The carry check and its fanout to pipeline enables limit timing. Placement 0 used 5,015 logic cells, 946 registers, 96 LUT RAMs, six block RAMs and five DSPs.\n\nThe first implementation used a separate nibble comparator, selected the carry at bit 16, and shared the adder with a conditionally complemented B. That version reached 66.899 MHz median. Putting the four prediction bits on the upper carry chains shortened the forwarded-sign path. A separate trial checking the carry into bit 12 and folding PC/immediate selection into the forwarding muxes reached 75.867 MHz median.\n\n## Local verification\n\nVerilator lint passed with `-Wall`. All 101 cocotb cases passed across six pytest runners. A separate combinational SAT proof checked the predicted result, miss flag, exact carry and repaired result for every 32-bit operand pair under ADD and SUB. Co-simulation passed for selftest and all three random programs, each with and without bus stalls. CoreMark passed its CRC and bounds checks with both stalls enabled.\n\nThe single-channel ALTOPS run of `formal/run_all.sh` passed **53 of 53 checks**, including register consistency, liveness and retirement order. The final RTL passed on its first full run and required zero formal fixes.\n-rw-rw----+ 1 hwebench hwebench 3.8K Nov 20 13:20 cores/bench/implementation_notes.md\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
