{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_111","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"git check-ignore cores/bench/implementation_notes.md && git diff --check && cat cores/bench/implementation_notes.md && rg -n 'waiting for solver' formal/last_run-wFFWmhOkH.log | tail -3\"","aggregated_output":"cores/bench/implementation_notes.md\n# Denied-load replay\n\nReady loads use the external bus and retain the same-cycle LW base bypass into ID. A denied, address-checked, naturally aligned load in the first MiB probes a 1,024-row table indexed by byte address bits 11 through 2. Each row stores the word, eight physical tag bits and four valid lanes. Accepted RAM reads fill every lane. Accepted RAM stores replace the row with the replicated store data and the written lanes. A 1,024-cycle reset sweep clears validity and blocks probes.\n\nThe synchronous block RAM reads on the falling edge of the load's EX cycle. The next rising edge captures the formatted candidate and raw row with the MEM slot. MEM checks the physical tag and requested lanes in parallel with the younger instruction's use of the candidate. A denial arriving after the read edge forces a miss. A ready load always takes live data on its accepting edge.\n\nA miss holds both forwarding sources, inhibits repair and divider launch, suppresses redirects and gives the older load exclusive bus ownership. The detection edge saves the younger address and puts the older address into the existing bus address register. The refill acceptance edge captures the returned word and restores the younger address. This adds one acquisition cycle per miss and preserves Gowin block-RAM inference for the external data memory.\n\nThe simulator accepts `+load_replay_stats` to count probes, verified hits, cycles held for refill (including acquisition and acceptance), and immediate dependent address repairs between the benchmark markers.\n\n## Local measurements\n\nThe ten-iteration run took 3,101,251 bracketed cycles. Of 119,386 denied-load probes, 116,859 hit (97.88%). The 2,527 misses held the pipeline for 5,773 cycles. Immediate dependent addresses needed 12,936 repairs.\n\nGowin placement options 0, 1 and 2 produced 62.228, 60.190 and 60.190 MHz. The median gives 194.08 iterations/s, below the acceptance target. The two median placements were limited by the half-cycle path from block RAM through subword formatting to the candidate register. Placement 0 was limited by tag verification through the pipeline hold logic to the external data RAM address. The replay table used three block RAMs. The timed design used nine in total.\n\nVerilator lint passed with `-Wall`. All six cocotb runners passed, including 35 pipeline scenarios. Co-simulation passed selftest and the three random programs with and without stalls. Stalled CoreMark produced all five expected CRCs, the validation message, both timing markers and a clear out-of-bounds flag.\n\nThe final local RVFI run is in progress with the single-retirement wrapper. That wrapper holds the data bus ready. The directed pipeline tests and stalled co-simulation exercise the denied-load behavior.\n756:SBY 16:09:39 [reg_ch0] engine_0: ##   0:05:24  waiting for solver (1 minute)\n834:SBY 16:09:53 [cover] engine_0: ##   0:05:42  waiting for solver (1 minute)\n1169:SBY 16:13:39 [reg_ch0] engine_0: ##   0:09:24  waiting for solver (5 minutes)\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
