{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_8", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'rg --files cores/bench; cat cores/bench/core.yaml; cat cores/bench/rtl/{if_stage,ex_stage,hazard_unit}.sv'", "aggregated_output": "cores/bench/rtl/decoder.sv\ncores/bench/rtl/forward_unit.sv\ncores/bench/rtl/imm_gen.sv\ncores/bench/rtl/mem_stage.sv\ncores/bench/rtl/alu.sv\ncores/bench/rtl/if_stage.sv\ncores/bench/rtl/reg_file.sv\ncores/bench/rtl/hazard_unit.sv\ncores/bench/rtl/id_stage.sv\ncores/bench/rtl/ex_stage.sv\ncores/bench/rtl/wb_stage.sv\ncores/bench/rtl/core.sv\ncores/bench/rtl/core_pkg.sv\ncores/bench/core.yaml\ncores/bench/test/test_imm_gen.py\ncores/bench/test/conftest.py\ncores/bench/test/test_pipeline.py\ncores/bench/test/_helpers.py\ncores/bench/test/test_decoder.py\ncores/bench/test/test_reg_file.py\ncores/bench/test/test_alu.py\ncores/bench/CORE_PHILOSOPHY.md\ncores/bench/experiments/progress.png\ncores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\nname: bench\ndescription: Frozen LLM-benchmark fixture core. Identical RTL to baseline at the bench-fixture-v1\n  freeze point. The benchmark matrix clones from the bench-fixture-v1 orphan branch\n  and operates only on this directory.\nisa: rv32im\nnret: 1\ntarget_fpga: tang-nano-20k\ntargets:\n  fmax_mhz: 135\n  lut4: 10000\n  coremark_iter_s: 300\n  coremark_per_mhz: 2.2\ncurrent:\n  fmax_mhz: 5.442\n  lut4: 12312\n  ff: 460\n  coremark_iter_s: 2.0e-06\n  coremark_per_mhz: 0.0\n  source_id: baseline-bench-ec4e0d6\n  updated: '2026-11-20T02:35:27.887001Z'\n// rtl/if_stage.sv\n//\n// Instruction fetch stage. Holds the PC register; the IF/ID payload\n// (pc + instr + valid) is *combinational* — there is no separate IF/ID\n// flop in this microarchitecture, the next-stage's ID/EX register\n// captures everything one cycle later.\n//\n// On flush or redirect, the instruction emitted to ID is forced to NOP\n// (`0x00000013` = ADDI x0,x0,0). This prevents the hazard unit from\n// observing a real rs1/rs2 from a wrong-path instruction and inserting\n// a spurious load-use stall the cycle after a taken branch.\n//\n// Latency:        PC-reg update is synchronous; output is combinational.\n// RVFI fields:    feeds pc_rdata (via ID/EX/MEM/WB) and pc_wdata (via\n//                 EX-stage redirect).\nmodule if_stage (\n  input  logic              clock,\n  input  l\n…[9966 of 13038 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:581112dee980ab80]…\ndirect || imem_stall;\n    // ID/EX register:\n    //   - dmem_stall  -> hold        (preserve in-flight pipeline state)\n    //   - load_use    -> bubble      (1-cycle stall between LOAD + use)\n    //   - redirect    -> bubble      (kill wrong-path)\n    //   - otherwise   -> capture\n    // dmem_stall takes precedence over load_use's bubble: re-evaluate\n    // load_use next cycle when the bus unblocks. flush_id is 1 only when\n    // we want bubble (not hold).\n    stall_id      = dmem_stall || load_use_hazard;\n    flush_id      = (load_use_hazard || redirect) && !dmem_stall;\n    // EX/MEM register: holds on dmem_stall (LOAD waits in MEM until the\n    // bus delivers).\n    stall_ex_mem  = dmem_stall;\n    // MEM/WB register: on dmem_stall the previously-retired instruction's\n    // data fields stay alive for forwarding (e.g. a held BNE needs the\n    // LOAD's load_data via fwd_mem_wb), but valid is cleared so we don't\n    // double-retire / double-write the regfile.\n    hold_mem_wb   = dmem_stall;\n  end\n\nendmodule\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
