{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_36","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'git diff --check && git status --short --untracked-files=all && verilator --lint-only -Wall -Wno-MULTITOP -sv +incdir+cores/bench/rtl cores/bench/rtl/*.sv && cat cores/bench/implementation_notes.md'","aggregated_output":" M cores/bench/rtl/core.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/core_pkg.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/ex_stage.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/id_stage.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/if_stage.sv\n M cores/bench/test/test_pipeline.py\n- V e r i l a t i o n   R e p o r t: Verilator 5.047 devel rev v5.046-331-g2cd9b8df6 (mod)\n- Verilator: Built from 0.613 MB sources in 14 modules, into 0.217 MB in 4 C++ files needing 0.000 MB\n- Verilator: Walltime 0.028 s (elab=0.004, cvt=0.016, bld=0.000); cpu 0.028 s on 1 threads; allocated 23.152 MB\n# Direct branch and JAL prediction on the radix-8 core\n\nThe measured median is **47.920 MHz**. Ten CoreMark iterations took **4,188,667 bracketed cycles** with both stall generators active, yielding **114.40 iterations/s**, up **9.71%** from the parent’s 104.28.\n\n## Implementation\n\nFetch uses a 256-entry, two-bit LUT-RAM indexed by PC[9:2]. At configuration each entry weakly favors backward-taken and forward-not-taken. A shared B/J displacement adder supplies word-aligned speculative targets below 0x00100000. Direct JAL takes that target on an accepted fetch. JALR resolves in EX.\n\nDecode and load-use detection consume the raw fetch word. ID/EX holds its entire payload during a downstream stall. On a bubble, its control bundle and valid bit clear while the operand and instruction registers capture raw inputs. Each advancing legal conditional branch trains once from its saved counter. An EX miss installs the recovery PC even when instruction memory stalls on the release edge of an older data access.\n\nEX selects the alternate address from the saved direction in parallel with the branch comparison. The comparison enables recovery, and the resolved outcome independently selects the architectural successor for RVFI.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Verilator lint passed with `-Wall`.\n- Fast single-retire formal passed on the first run, **53 passed, 0 failed**.\n- All five cocotb suites passed. Pipeline tests cover hit and exit timing, simultaneous read and write to an aliased counter, direct JAL, JALR, traps, target bounds, retirement order and suppression of a wrong-path store across overlapping bus stalls.\n- Five-ELF cosim passed. Selftest and three random programs matched the ISS with and without stalls. Stalled CoreMark reported all five canonical CRCs and “Correct operation validated.” The start and stop markers occurred on cycles 14,946 and 4,203,613.\n\n## Placement\n\n| Gowin placement option | Fmax (MHz) |\n| --- | ---: |\n| 0 | 45.588 |\n| 1 | 47.920 |\n| 2 | 47.920 |\n\nOption 0 fell 0.102 MHz below the 45.69 MHz threshold. The scored median cleared it by 2.230 MHz. Its worst setup path passes through forwarding and the signed multiplier. Gowin reports 3,590 logic units, 667 flip-flops and 24 LUT-RAMs, increases of 161 logic units, three flip-flops and 16 LUT-RAMs over the parent.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_37","type":"agent_message","text":"**114.40 CoreMark iterations/s**, up **9.71%**, with 10 iterations in 4,188,667 bracketed cycles.\n\nGowin placements reached 45.588, 47.920 and 47.920 MHz. The **47.920 MHz median** cleared the 45.69 MHz threshold by 2.230 MHz.\n\nVerilator lint, all 53 formal checks, all five cocotb suites and five-ELF cosim passed. All five CoreMark CRCs matched.\n\n[Implementation notes](/srv/hwebench/clones/gpt-6_2-astra_xhigh-v2-rep2/cores/bench/worktrees/hyp-20261120-003-r3s2/cores/bench/implementation_notes.md)"}}
