{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_41", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"ls -l cores/bench/experiments; rg -n 'successors|critical_path|median' cores/bench/experiments -g '*.jsonl' | tail -c 3000; rg -n '\"'^#|'\"\\\\.tmp|implementation_notes' .gitignore | tail -38\"", "aggregated_output": "total 216\n-rw-rw----+ 1 nobody nogroup 145297 Nov 20 07:39 log.jsonl\n-rw-rw----+ 1 nobody nogroup  71242 Nov 20 07:39 progress.png\nair, redirect or access memory.\\nKeep the architectural rs1 and rs2 captures independent of the\\npredicted address.\\n\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Carry the predicted address, crossing flag and base-source status\\nwith ID/EX. Carry the serviced byte address and raw accepted read\\nword alongside the normal result in EX/MEM.\\n\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Gate bus enables with the registered prediction status and alignment.\\nOn a miss, latch a repaired flag while writing the corrected address\\nback into the address register. Clear that flag when the slot leaves.\\nFormat accepted loads for the EX/MEM result bypass. Use forwarded\\nstore data and preserve misalignment traps and suppressed writes.\\n\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Hold ID/EX, EX/MEM and forwarding data during a repair or an EX\\nmemory request denied by dmemReady. Clear MEM/WB valid on a hold.\\nInterlock products and allow a dependent successor to advance with\\nan accepted load. Apply the same hold to successor replay metadata.\\n\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/mem_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Build RVFI memory fields and writeback from the registered serviced\\naddress, raw word, width and store data. Preserve the MEM multiplier\\nand the single-channel retirement boundary.\\n\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Check back-to-back load-to-branch retirement on a hit. Exercise\\n0x0ffc + 4 and 0x1000 - 4, an unsupported base producer, a misaligned