{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_12", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/LESSONS.md'", "aggregated_output": "- 2026-11-20 hyp-20261120-001-r1s0 (regression, +471.20%): Eight serial trial subtractions on the `partial_q` feedback path limited median Fmax to 31.094 MHz versus 41.649 MHz for six steps per clock, while CoreMark executed no DIV/REM between markers to benefit from the shorter divide latency.\n- 2026-11-20 hyp-20261120-002-r1s1 (improvement, +665.10%): Moving combinational `/` and `%` off the shared EX result path into a six-cycle restoring divider raised median Fmax from 5.442 to 41.649 MHz without adding divider stalls because CoreMark issued no DIV/REM between its markers.\n- 2026-11-20 hyp-20261120-003-r1s2 (regression, +6.19%): Predicting branches by displacement bias and taking JAL in fetch saved 302,818 CoreMark cycles by avoiding EX redirects, while the combinational DIV/REM path still limited median Fmax to 5.392 MHz.\n- 2026-11-20 hyp-20261120-001-r2s0 (regression, +10.91%): Replacing six serial trials with three radix-4 stages that test divisor multiples in parallel raised median Fmax from 41.649 to 46.194 MHz, exposing the path from the register file through hazard logic to ID/EX as the new timing limit.\n- 2026-11-20 hyp-20261120-002-r2s1 (improvement, +12.46%): Registering 3D, 5D and 7D let two radix-8 stages replace six serial trial subtractions, raising median Fmax from 41.649 to 46.838 MHz at the same 4,491,485 CoreMark cycles, with the single-cycle multiplier limiting both median-frequency placements.\n- 2026-11-20 hyp-20261120-003-r2s2 (regression, +10.77%): Predicting branches and JAL in fetch avoided EX redirects and saved 302,818 CoreMark cycles, but the six-step divider’s `remainder_q` feedback path limited median Fmax to 43.026 MHz, leaving throughput below the radix-8 core (102.72 vs 104.28 iterations/s).\n- 2026-11-20 hyp-20261120-001-r3s0 (regression, +18.45%): Registering four multiply partial products at EX/MEM raised median Fmax from 46.838 to 55.927 MHz, while registering the forwarded operands and doing the full multiply in MEM reached 62.078 MHz with the same 0.81% CoreMark cycle pena\n…[3382 of 6454 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:0b4daf2e8cd2b948]…\nyp-20261120-001-r7s0 (improvement, +12.13%): With DIV/REM forwarded from MEM/WB, registering both producer tag matches in decode took the comparisons off the EX operand path and raised prototype median Fmax from 68.274 to 76.825 MHz, while `ex_mem_w.forwardable` kept a trapping younger writer from masking the older value.\n- 2026-11-20 hyp-20261120-002-r7s1 (regression, +10.13%): With forwarding matches registered in ID, splitting at divisor magnitude 2^17 limited divider feedback to two 20-bit radix-8 stages for small divisors or one full-width stage for large divisors, yielding 222.86 CoreMark iterations/s versus 226.92 for the design that forwarded DIV/REM from MEM/WB.\n- 2026-11-20 hyp-20261120-003-r7s2 (regression, +6.03%): Reading a 512-row table in ID let EX replay denied RAM loads when the tag matched and all requested byte lanes were valid, saving 132,870 cycles over ten CoreMark iterations, too few to offset the higher Fmax of the retimed divider and forwarding design (214.58 vs 226.92 iterations/s).\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_11", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'cat Makefile'", "aggregated_output": ".PHONY: help lint test test-infra cosim formal fpga timing next loop report bench clean\n.DEFAULT_GOAL := help\n\n# Resolve OSS CAD Suite path so commands work even when the user hasn't\n# sourced .toolchain/oss-cad-suite/environment in this shell.\nTOOLCHAIN_DIR := $(CURDIR)/.toolchain\nOSS_BIN       := $(TOOLCHAIN_DIR)/oss-cad-suite/bin\nLOCAL_BIN     := $(TOOLCHAIN_DIR)/bin\nexport PATH := $(OSS_BIN):$(LOCAL_BIN):$(PATH)\n\n# Orchestrator knobs (pass-through to tools.orchestrator):\n#   N        — number of rounds for `make loop` (default 10).\n#   K        — tournament size, slots per round (default 1 = sequential).\n#   AGENT    — codex (default) or claude. Honors a pre-existing\n#              AGENT_PROVIDER env var if AGENT isn't set on the make\n#              command line.\n#   BASE     — when forking a new TARGET, copy from cores/<BASE>/.\n#              Default: baseline (orchestrator-side default).\n#   COREMARK — target CoreMark iterations/sec (e.g. '370').\n#   LUT      — target LUT count (e.g. '3000').\n#   WORKTREE — default ON. `make loop` first creates a dedicated git worktree\n#              at .worktrees/<TARGET>/ on branch core-<TARGET> and re-execs\n#              itself there. Lets two `make loop` invocations for different\n#              TARGETs run in parallel without git index/merge collisions.\n#              To opt out (run directly on the current branch + cwd) pass\n#              an explicit empty value: `make loop TARGET=v1 WORKTREE=`.\nN        ?= 10\nK        ?= 1\nAGENT    ?= $(or $(AGENT_PROVIDER),codex)\nBASE     ?=\nCOREMARK ?=\nLUT      ?=\nWORKTREE ?= 1\n\n# Compose optional CLI flags for the orchestrator. Empty vars produce\n# empty strings so the orchestrator falls back to its defaults.\nORCH_FLAGS  = --iterations $(N) --tournament-size $(K)\nifneq ($(strip $(BASE)),)\n  ORCH_FLAGS += --base $(BASE)\nendif\nifneq ($(strip $(COREMARK)),)\n  ORCH_FLAGS += --coremark-target $(COREMARK)\nendif\nifneq ($(strip $(LUT)),)\n  ORCH_FLAGS += --lut-target $(LUT)\nendif\n\n# Multi-core: TARGET selects the core under cores/<TARGET>\n…[4585 of 7657 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:5e81c709f2609edb]…\nree add \"$(WT_PATH)\" $(WT_BRANCH); \\\n\t  else \\\n\t    git worktree add -b $(WT_BRANCH) \"$(WT_PATH)\"; \\\n\t  fi; \\\n\t  [ -e \"$(WT_PATH)/formal/riscv-formal\" ] || ln -s \"$(CURDIR)/formal/riscv-formal\" \"$(WT_PATH)/formal/riscv-formal\"; \\\n\tfi\n\t@$(MAKE) -C \"$(WT_PATH)\" loop \\\n\t  WORKTREE= \\\n\t  TARGET=$(TARGET) N=$(N) K=$(K) AGENT=$(AGENT) \\\n\t  $(if $(strip $(BASE)),BASE=$(BASE),) \\\n\t  $(if $(strip $(COREMARK)),COREMARK=$(COREMARK),) \\\n\t  $(if $(strip $(LUT)),LUT=$(LUT),)\nelse\n\tAGENT_PROVIDER=$(AGENT) python3 -m tools.orchestrator $(ORCH_FLAGS) $(ORCH_TARGET_FLAG)\nendif\n\nreport:\n\tpython3 -m tools.orchestrator --report $(ORCH_TARGET_FLAG)\n\nclean:\n\trm -rf test/cosim/sim_build sim_build out\n\trm -rf experiments/worktrees\n\trm -f bench/programs/*.elf\n\trm -f test/*.result.xml\n\tfind test -name __pycache__ -prune -exec rm -rf {} + 2>/dev/null || true\n\tfind tools -name __pycache__ -prune -exec rm -rf {} + 2>/dev/null || true\nifneq ($(strip $(TARGET)),)\n\trm -rf $(OBJ_DIR)\n\trm -rf $(GEN_DIR)\n\trm -rf cores/$(TARGET)/sim_build\nendif\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
