"}}\n{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_146\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/bash -c 'date -u; checks=$(echo \\\"$TMPDIR/check/formal/riscv-formal/cores/\\\"bench-*/checks); rg --files --no-ignore \\\"$checks\\\" -g PASS | wc -l; rg --files --no-ignore \\\"$checks\\\" -g FAIL -g ERROR; for x in reg_ch0 insn_or_ch0 insn_sra_ch0; do tail -n 1 \\\"$checks/$x/logfile.txt\\\"; done; uptime'\",\"aggregated_output\":\"Fri Nov 20 13:56:56 UTC 2026\\n22\\nSBY 14:56:26 [reg_ch0] engine_0: ##   0:08:46  waiting for s\n…[10428 of 13500 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:0927448a4c27288e]…\nyp-20261120-001-r12s0/cores/bench/implementation_notes.md\",\"kind\":\"update\"}],\"status\":\"in_progress\"}}\n{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_154\",\"type\":\"file_change\",\"changes\":[{\"path\":\"/srv/hwebench/clones/gpt-6_2-astra_xhigh-v2-rep2/cores/bench/worktrees/hyp-20261120-001-r12s0/cores/bench/implementation_notes.md\",\"kind\":\"update\"}],\"status\":\"completed\"}}\n{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_155\",\"type\":\"agent_message\",\"text\":\"Implemented exact byte carry lookahead for ADD/SUB, bytewise comparisons, and reuse of the EX sum for dependent addresses.\\n\\nLint, all 100 cocotb tests, all 53 formal checks, and co-simulation passed. CoreMark matched the expected **3,234,996 cycles**. Median Gowin Fmax was **80.378 MHz**, below the **89.25 MHz** acceptance threshold.\\n\\n[Implementation notes](./cores/bench/implementation_notes.md)\"}}\n{\"type\":\"turn.completed\",\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":15183082,\"cached_input_tokens\":15008768,\"cache_write_input_tokens\":0,\"output_tokens\":46992,\"reasoning_output_tokens\":24003}}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'tail -c 13500 cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/.agent.hyp-20261120-001-r12s0.log'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/.agent.hyp-20261120-001-r12s0.last cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261120-001-r12s0.yaml'","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20261120-001-r12s0\ntitle: Shorten forwarded integer arithmetic with exact byte carry lookahead\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  Gowin traced two paths within 8 ps of each other on the champion's\n  85.328 MHz placement. One ran from a forwarding select to EX/MEM result\n  bit 27. The other ran from writeback through the EX branch comparison\n  to ID/EX.pc. Round 11's predicted carry shortened the nominal addition\n  but put carry verification on the pipeline hold path. Both original\n  endpoints can use exact arithmetic on small groups of bits in parallel.\nhypothesis: |\n  Partition the 32-bit forwarded arithmetic into four bytes. For addition,\n  each byte computes its carry-out assuming carry-in zero and whether it\n  propagates an incoming carry. Form the three boundary carries with a\n  balanced group lookahead. Select each upper byte's sum for carry-in\n  zero or one with its exact boundary carry. Apply the same construction\n  to subtraction with complemented B and initial carry one. Supply ID's\n  ADD-produced base page from the same exact EX sum. This keeps a second\n  full-width carry chain off the dependent load/store address path.\n\n  Use the equivalent borrow lookahead for comparisons. In parallel each\n  byte computes unsigned less-than and equality. The most significant\n  unequal byte determines the result. Signed compares override that result\n  when operand signs differ. Use these predicates for branch resolution\n  on forwarded rs1/rs2 and for SLT/SLTU on their actual ALU inputs.\n  The network computes the exact result in the original EX cycle, so every\n  ready successor can still issue and the expected bracket is 3,234,996\n  cycles. At that count acceptance requires a median above 89.25 MHz.\n  The principal timing risk is extra routing for the upper-byte selects.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 6\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: Define synthesizable fixed-width helpers for exact grouped addition and lexicographic comparison with explicit byte carry and equality terms.\n  - file: rtl/alu.sv\n    description: Use grouped arithmetic for integer ADD/SUB and SLT/SLTU. Expose the ADD candidate for the existing dependent-address calculation.\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: Use the byte comparison on raw forwarded branch operands, invert the selected predicate for BNE/BGE/BGEU, and pass the ALU sum to ID.\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: Wire the exact EX sum to the address generator alongside the existing operands used for the three-input displacement sum.\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: Take the ADD producer's page from the exact EX sum. Keep the existing independent low displacement sum, base priority, and page-cross repair.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: Exercise carries and borrows across one and several byte boundaries, signed branch comparisons with opposite signs, and an immediately dependent load using a carried ADD result. Check retirement and the accepted byte address.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
