{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261120-001-r13s0.yaml'","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20261120-001-r13s0\ntitle: \"Reuse the address computed in ID as an ADDI base bypass\"\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  A load following ADDI currently takes its base page from a 32-bit sum\n  of two forwarded EX operands. ID also puts both operands through a\n  carry-save compressor to obtain the low effective-address bits. This\n  loads the same EX operand buses that limit the champion's ALU and branch\n  paths. A scratch run retaining only ADDI in this arithmetic base bypass\n  took 3,240,833 cycles versus 3,234,996 for the champion. That small cost\n  makes it practical to remove the general three-input address path.\nhypothesis: |\n  ID already computes a tentative memory address for every incoming word.\n  For ADDI, opcode bit 5 is zero, so the displacement extracted by ID is\n  exactly the signed I-immediate. If base_available is set and page_cross\n  is clear, the ADDI's own ID/EX.mem_addr therefore equals its exact\n  architectural result. Reuse that registered value as the base for the\n  next memory instruction. Its upper bits supply the page directly and\n  a single 13-bit addition supplies the low address and page-cross check.\n  This removes both forwarded EX operands from the arithmetic base bypass.\n\n  Apply the same rule when the next word is itself ADDI. It can carry a\n  verified address through a chain of pointer increments. An unavailable\n  base or a page crossing invalidates the candidate. The youngest writer\n  retains ownership even when its candidate is invalid. A dependent memory\n  access then uses the existing one-cycle repair from its exact forwarded\n  rs1 before asserting a bus request. Register-register ADD and AUIPC\n  producers take this repair path. Integer ADDI execution, forwarding to\n  ordinary consumers, and retirement still use the exact ALU result.\n\n  Measure bracketed cycles and the three-placement Gowin median. Around\n  3.24 million cycles, acceptance requires approximately 89.4 MHz. The\n  timing risk is that an EX operand-to-branch path still sets the clock\n  after its address-generation fanout falls.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Qualify the arithmetic base candidate with an admitted, matching ADDI writer. Keep the existing youngest-writer priority, accepted LW, LUI, MEM and RF source rules.\"\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: \"Use the resident reg_q.mem_addr as the ADDI candidate, with reg_q.base_available and !reg_q.page_cross as its certificate. Add the incoming displacement to its low 13 bits and copy the page. Read the LUI immediate directly from reg_q.imm. Drop the EX operand inputs and the ADD base adder and compressor.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Keep the forwarded ALU operands local to EX once ID no longer consumes them. Preserve exact results and the existing memory repair handshake.\"\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: \"Exercise back-to-back ADDIs followed by a load or store, negative offsets, an ADDI that crosses a page and a successor that crosses back. Include a competing writer, an unavailable M base and a denied request. Check retired results, the full accepted address and exactly one transfer.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
