{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_10", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261120-001-r5s0.yaml'", "aggregated_output": "id: hyp-20261120-001-r5s0\ntitle: Register effective addresses in decode so loads can forward from EX/MEM\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  The champion issues data requests in MEM, one cycle too late for a dependent\n  instruction to use a load through the EX/MEM bypass. An instruction trace\n  of the ten timed iterations contains 544,852 loads. A branch immediately\n  follows 135,320 loads with a matching source field. Moving address generation\n  one stage earlier can remove that bubble and keep the FPGA RAM address\n  registered. The latter matters because the champion's reported option-zero\n  critical path crosses the shared EX ALU on its way to data memory.\nhypothesis: |\n  Compute the full byte address as a memory instruction enters ID/EX. Drive\n  the data bus from this register during EX. On acceptance, latch the raw\n  read word for RVFI and the formatted load value in EX/MEM for ordinary EX\n  forwarding. Stores use the forwarded rs2 in EX. A stalled request holds\n  its address, data, enables and producer operands through the accepting edge.\n\n  To handle a newly produced base, compare the incoming rs1 against the\n  youngest writers. For ADD, ADDI and AUIPC in EX, their operands A and B\n  are already available. With displacement D, compute P = A XOR B, then\n  (P XOR D) + (((A AND B) OR (P AND D)) << 1) modulo 2^32. This gives\n  A+B+D with one carry-propagate adder. Compute it in parallel with the normal\n  base-plus-displacement path. A preceding LUI supplies its immediate and an\n  aligned, accepted LW can supply the raw bus word. Use the EX/MEM value for\n  older available writers and the write-first register file otherwise.\n  Interlock unavailable bases, including pending products. Suppress x0 and\n  trapped writes. Keep the multiply-use interlock for ordinary EX consumers.\n\n  A scratch prototype completed ten iterations in 3,967,605 bracketed cycles\n  versus 4,171,092 for the champion, with all canonical CRCs. Gowin placement\n  options 0, 1 and 2 reached 61.552, 66.658 and 66.658 MHz respectively.\n  The median gives 168.01 iterations/s, 9.44% above the champion. The\n  prototype passed all 53 standard single-channel formal checks. The selftest\n  and three random programs matched the reference with and without bus stalls.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 9\n  confidence: high\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: Carry the effective address in ID/EX, then carry the serviced address and raw load word in EX/MEM alongside the forwarded result.\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: Select the youngest available base and register the address on issue. Compute the ordinary, LW/LUI-bypassed and carry-save three-input candidate addresses in parallel with the producer checks.\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: Drive the registered address, alignment-qualified enables and replicated store data in EX. On transfer, capture the raw read word, effective address and extended load result. Expose the forwarded arithmetic operands for address generation.\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: Connect the EX bus, classify eligible base producers, permit EX/MEM load forwarding and derive dmem backpressure from the resident ID/EX memory operation.\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: Interlock address bases that cannot yet be bypassed and retain the multiply-use check. Hold the resident request and forwarding state on data waits, including simultaneous instruction waits.\n  - file: rtl/mem_stage.sv\n    description: Format the captured raw word and byte address into the existing MEM/WB read_data path for register writeback, alongside the earlier EX/MEM copy used for bypass. Use the captured access for aligned RVFI masks, memory data and traps. Preserve the MEM multiplier.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: Assert back-to-back load-to-branch and LW-to-address timing. Check dependent ADDI addresses with carries, stale-base interlocks, misaligned requests and a stalled store accepted exactly once. Adjust stage-specific cycle expectations while retaining architectural checks.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
