{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261120-001-r9s0.yaml'","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20261120-001-r9s0\ntitle: \"Move the M-result interlock off the replay-to-decode control path\"\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  The champion's 18.152 ns reported path starts at the successor instruction\n  RAM and crosses hazard and decode logic on its way to data memory. ID\n  compares both fields of a fetched word with the late producer's rd, then\n  uses that decision to clear every control in ID/EX. The forwarding unit\n  already registers both younger-producer matches on the same edge.\nhypothesis: |\n  Use those registered matches to recognize the M-result dependency at\n  the entrance to EX. Capture a fetched candidate on the producer's\n  transfer edge. If the preceding instruction was a valid M writer and\n  either captured match is set, annul the candidate in EX and fetch it\n  again from retry_pc. The producer advances to WB and the retry gets\n  its result through the existing bypass. This places a register between\n  the RAM word's source fields and suppression of decoded side effects.\n  A dependent pair still costs one bubble and an independent pair can\n  issue on consecutive clocks. At 3,234,996 cycles per ten iterations,\n  acceptance requires a median clock above 84.80 MHz.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 6\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/forward_unit.sv\n    description: |\n      Capture the advancing producer's effective late-result qualifier\n      with the existing younger_rs1_q and younger_rs2_q matches. Expose\n      their registered dependency indication. Preserve x0 exclusion,\n      stall holds and the priority of the original forwarding muxes.\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: |\n      Combine the resident dependency indication with the existing replay\n      annul before any EX side effect, redirect, FENCE.I, training or\n      retirement. Reset or an invalid candidate cannot generate a retry\n      side effect. Feed IF the effective ex_valid so it uses retry_pc on\n      the bubble, including when the producer itself has just finished a divide.\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: |\n      Remove the same-cycle fetched rs1/rs2 versus late rd test from\n      flush_id. Keep the invalid-fetch bubble and the existing divide,\n      data-bus and address-repair hold priorities.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
