{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_20","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor line in open('.tmp/agent-logs/impl.hyp-20261120-001-r9s0.log'):\n try: item=json.loads(line).get('item',{})\n except ValueError: continue\n if item.get('type')=='agent_message': print(item.get('text'))\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_20","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor line in open('.tmp/agent-logs/impl.hyp-20261120-001-r9s0.log'):\n try: item=json.loads(line).get('item',{})\n except ValueError: continue\n if item.get('type')=='agent_message': print(item.get('text'))\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"I’ll check the worktree layout and pipeline controls, then implement the EX interlock and run the requested verification.\nThe interlock now uses the existing registered M-result bit in EX/MEM and the two registered source matches. Verilator lint passes. I’ll run formal, cosim, and all three Gowin placements to check correctness and measure the median clock.\nCosim passed and CoreMark took 3,234,996 bracketed cycles. Two placements measured 76.783 MHz, below the 84.80 MHz target. The timing report points to the replayed source field feeding the ID address calculation. I’ll test a narrower EX annul that gates side effects while leaving operand selection off that path.\nMoving the replayed `rs1` field into a separately registered RAM bank brought one placement to 79.339 MHz. Its longest path now starts at the forwarding select, so I’ll test resolving bypass priority on the producer’s transfer edge and check that version against formal and cosim.\nThe best completed three-placement run so far is 80.185 MHz, with the expected CoreMark cycle count and CRCs. I’ll compare the remaining timing results and record the formal status for the RTL left in the worktree.\nMoved the M-result interlock to EX. Dependent pairs retain one bubble, and independent pairs can issue on consecutive clocks.\n\nMedian Gowin Fmax was **80.185 MHz**, below the **84.80 MHz** acceptance threshold. CoreMark completed ten iterations in **3,234,996 bracketed cycles** with matching CRCs.\n\nVerilator lint, all 53 formal checks, all six cocotb suites, and cosimulation passed. [Implementation notes](/srv/hwebench/clones/gpt-6_2-astra_xhigh-v2-rep2/cores/bench/worktrees/hyp-20261120-001-r9s0/cores/bench/implementation_notes.md)\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
