{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'ls -A .tmp && cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261120-002-r2s1.yaml | head -80'","aggregated_output":"agent-logs\nenv.json\norchestrator.log\nriscv-formal-eval\nsandbox-probe\nid: hyp-20261120-002-r2s1\ntitle: Resolve six quotient bits with two radix-8 divider stages\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  The champion's worst Gowin path runs from divisor_q to remainder_q through\n  six dependent trial subtractions. Eight trials per clock reached 31.094 MHz\n  and six reached 41.649 MHz. CoreMark executed zero DIV or REM instructions\n  in its 4,491,485 bracketed cycles, so the divider limits the clock even\n  when it contributes no stalls.\nhypothesis: |\n  Keep the six iteration clocks and change the quotient-digit datapath.\n  On the first clock after issue, divide the dividend's top two bits by the\n  registered divisor magnitude D. Only D values 1, 2 and 3 can yield a\n  nonzero digit for a nonzero divisor. In parallel, register 3D, 5D and 7D\n  using shifts and adds or subtracts. The other multiples are wires or shifts.\n  On each of the next five clocks, compute two radix-8 digits in series.\n  Each digit appends three dividend bits to the remainder and tries the seven\n  nonzero divisor multiples in parallel. Borrow bits select the largest\n  multiple that fits and its already-computed difference. This produces all\n  32 quotient bits with two dependent subtract/select levels per feedback\n  cycle. The existing EX issue, result transfer and retirement schedule apply.\n\n  Predict the same bracketed cycle count and a median Fmax near 50 MHz,\n  giving about 111 CoreMark iterations/s. At that cycle count the acceptance\n  threshold is just above 43.56 MHz. Compare the measured cycles and median\n  Gowin Fmax with these predictions. Wide digit-selection muxes or the\n  single-cycle multiplier could limit the gain.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 20\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/alu.sv\n    description: |\n      Replace the six binary trial steps with the two-bit initialization\n      and five pairs of radix-8 steps. Size each multiple and shifted trial\n      remainder to 35 unsigned bits and retain a separate subtraction borrow.\n      Register each pair's remainder and dividend/quotient shift register.\n      For D=0, append all-one quotient digits and pass each dividend prefix\n      through as the remainder. Use the existing magnitude and sign logic\n      for signed results, including INT_MIN / -1. Use the same counter,\n      held result-valid handshake and reset behavior for real and ALTOPS\n      execution.\n  - file: test/test_alu.py\n    description: |\n      Add directed DIVU and REMU vectors at k*D-1, k*D and k*D+1 for\n      k=1 through 7 wherever the dividend fits in 32 bits. Exercise each\n      possible two-bit dividend prefix with D=0,1,2,3,4 and divisors near\n      2^32 to catch truncation of large multiples. Check both results with\n      the existing six-clock handshake and integer reference.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
