{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_10", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261120-002-r8s1.yaml && tail -65 cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/.agent.hyp-20261120-002-r8s1.log'", "aggregated_output": "id: hyp-20261120-002-r8s1\ntitle: \"Replace divider feedback with reciprocal interpolation and one exact correction\"\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  Gowin traces the champion's 74-cell critical path from quotient_q to remainder_q through two serial digit selections. CoreMark issues zero DIV/REM between the markers, so shortening this path benefits the entire timed loop. The fixed retirement bound matters even for these infrequent instructions. A nine-clock radix-16 prototype failed liveness when a FENCE.I bubble preceded a divide and a younger store needed address repair.\nhypothesis: |\n  Build a fixed-latency divider from a synchronous reciprocal ROM and a registered multiplier used twice. For dividend magnitude A and nonzero divisor magnitude D, normalize V = D << s into [2^31, 2^32). Use i = V >> 20 and x = the low 20 bits of V. A 2048-by-45-bit ROM returns the intercept C = floor(2^42/i) and slope S = ceil(2^34/i²). Round the residual up to t = ceil(x/32768). A six-by-thirteen-bit product gives R = C - ((t*S) << 3). This makes the interpolation term an integer and removes the fractional carry from its subtraction. The shared unsigned multiplier first forms A*R. Extract q0 by shifting this full product right by 62-s, then reuse the multiplier to form P = q0*D.\n  \n  R is a lower bound on 2^62/V because the reciprocal curve is convex and rounding the slope and residual upward makes the subtracted term larger. For 4096 <= D < 131072, s >= 15, so x is already a multiple of 32768. The curvature and coefficient rounding errors total less than 770 reciprocal units and A/2^(62-s) is below 1/2048. For D >= 131072 residual rounding adds at most 32768 units and the scale is below 1/65536. For D < 4096 the residual is zero, C has less than one unit of error, and D=1 is exact. Thus q0 is either the exact quotient or one short. Register A-D with its borrow early. On consume select q0+1 and A-D-P if A >= D and P <= A-D, otherwise q0 and A-P. Sign-correct the registered final magnitude for MEM.\n  \n  An isolated prototype us\n…[68880 of 71952 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:cbf24e2cbb298dd4]…\nlace('The remaining timing limit runs','The six-bit interpolation is an unmeasured refinement targeting 78 MHz through lower logic and routing demand. The prototype timing limit runs')\\ns=s.replace('fitness_delta_pct: 4','fitness_delta_pct: 6').replace('confidence: medium','confidence: low')\\ns=s.replace('Compute t from bits [19:8] and a sticky OR of [7:0]. Use ((C << 4) - t*S) >> 4 at sufficient width.', 'Compute t from bits [19:15] plus a sticky OR of [14:0]. Retain all six bits, including t=32. Zero-extend the product before shifting left three bits and subtracting it from C.')\\ns=s.replace('the 4095/4096 boundary','the 4095/4096 and 131071/131072 boundaries')\\np.write_text(s)\\njsonschema.validate(yaml.safe_load(s),json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\\nprint('schema valid')\\nPY\\ndate -u\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"schema valid\\nFri Nov 20 07:32:32 UTC 2026\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\nsudo: cannot execute '/usr/local/sbin/hwe-agent-scope': Broken pipe (os error 32)\nKilled\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
