{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261120-003-r10s2.yaml'","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20261120-003-r10s2\ntitle: Predict the fetch PC from the successor replay table on live control transfers\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  The champion already knows the last successor PC and instruction at each of\n  512 predecessor indices. It uses the word on a denied fetch, but every live\n  branch and JALR still routes forwarded EX operands through the comparison or\n  target adder and back to the fetch PC. Round 9 exposed this feedback path\n  on two placements reported in the experiment log. The champion takes\n  3,234,996 bracketed cycles for ten iterations at a median 85.328 MHz.\nhypothesis: |\n  Use the saved destination as the fetch PC for a valid branch or jump with a\n  usable successor row, including when instruction memory is ready. Predict\n  PC+4 for a cold row and for ordinary instructions. Only select an aligned\n  in-range speculative destination. Fetch and decode that address while EX\n  independently resolves the architectural successor with forwarded operands\n  and the existing trap rules. Register the comparison and the recovery\n  address at the transfer edge. A wrong prediction costs one retry on a ready\n  bus. A correct prediction removes the EX operand-to-fetch dependency on\n  both the direction and the target without adding a stage to replay.\n\n  Train the predecessor with the instruction fetched at its resolved\n  destination. On a miss, retain the predecessor index across recovery until\n  a live response at that destination can train it. This lets cold taken\n  branches and indirect calls learn their targets. Check marker-to-marker\n  cycles and all three Gowin placements. At a 2% cycle increase the median\n  must exceed 91.04 MHz to clear the tournament margin.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 6\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Predict the live fetch address from the registered successor row. On\n      every advancing valid EX transfer, record the selected direction of\n      recovery and the exact target and fall-through PCs in parallel. On a\n      mismatch issue the registered correct PC even if the speculative fetch\n      was denied or ID took a bubble. Qualify replay separately by the PC of\n      its stored word. Freeze related metadata over holds, reject read/write\n      collisions and clear pending training and row validity on reset/FENCE.I.\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: |\n      Supply IF with the resident branch/jump classification. Apply the\n      registered miss to the existing EX annul enables before a provisional\n      instruction can issue memory or division, redirect, write or retire.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: |\n      Train a taken branch and a JALR, then change the outcome and the\n      indirect target with a forwarded operand. Run with both bus stalls.\n      Check exact retirement PCs, absence of a wrong-path MMIO store, and\n      eventual recovery after a denied correction fetch. Cover a misaligned\n      target and FENCE.I with a pending table update.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
