{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_11", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nwith open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl') as f:\n rec=json.loads(list(f)[-1])\nprint(str(rec)[:10500])\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "{'id': 'hyp-20261120-002-r10s1', 'title': 'Resolve operand sources in parallel for live and replayed instructions', 'category': 'structural', 'motivation': \"Ten iterations take 3,234,996 cycles on the champion. Gowin's placement\\n0 path starts at older_rs1_q and ends at EX/MEM. On placement 1 both\\nWB-to-branch-PC and bypass-select-to-ALU-result paths approach the\\n85.328 MHz limit. The data-address generator also waits for the live\\nversus replay instruction choice before reading rs1 and adding the offset.\\n\", 'hypothesis': {'motivation': \"Ten iterations take 3,234,996 cycles on the champion. Gowin's placement\\n0 path starts at older_rs1_q and ends at EX/MEM. On placement 1 both\\nWB-to-branch-PC and bypass-select-to-ALU-result paths approach the\\n85.328 MHz limit. The data-address generator also waits for the live\\nversus replay instruction choice before reading rs1 and adding the offset.\\n\", 'hypothesis': \"Retime operand selection across ID/EX. Form the final youngest,\\nolder and local grants for each source while its instruction is in ID.\\nFor the ALU, group the two forwarded values on one arm of a mux and\\nthe local register value and PC or immediate on the other. Capture the\\ngrants alongside the consumer. This keeps the branch-selected PC out\\nof the D input of a combined local operand register.\\n\\nA scratch implementation of that EX routing reached 85.338, 85.574\\nand 85.574 MHz across the three placements. It retained 3,234,996\\nbracketed cycles with both buses stalling, the five canonical CRCs\\nand the validation banner. That yields 264.53 iterations/s. The\\nmedian placement's worst path then ran from imem_ready through the rs1\\nread and address adder to a data-address register. Apply the same\\nlate selection to the ID address operand. Use the live rs1 tag and the\\nregistered replay rs1 tag as independent asynchronous RF read addresses.\\nForm each RF-based address candidate with its own instruction's displacement.\\nSelect the completed candidates with imem_ready. A denied fetch still\\nneeds the existing \n…[5215 of 8287 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:0688abc9b34fb31d]…\nome': 'regression', 'fitness': 259.25, 'delta_pct': -1.71, 'vs_baseline': 2039.03, 'fmax_mhz': 83.868, 'ipc_coremark': 3e-06, 'cycles': 3234996, 'iterations': 10, 'lut4': 5311, 'ff': 950, 'seeds': [83.796, 83.868, 83.868], 'perturbations': [[0, 83.796, 13], [1, 83.868, 13], [2, 83.868, 13]], 'lutram': 112, 'bsram': 6, 'dsp': 5, 'critical_path': {'from': 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu/triple_q_0_s0', 'to': 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu/quotient_q_1_s1', 'slack_ns': -6.934, 'arrival_ns': 17.228, 'logic_cells': 43, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu']}, 'logic_levels': 13, 'formal_passed': True, 'cosim_passed': True, 'error': None, 'implementation_notes': '', 'timestamp': '2026-11-20T11:31:23.634944Z', 'slot': 1, 'round_id': 10, 'lesson': '- 2026-11-20 hyp-20261120-002-r10s1 (regression, -1.71%): Computing live and replay addresses in parallel took `imem_ready` off the critical path, but the path from `rs1_grants.older` through EX to the successor PC in ID/EX limited median Fmax to 83.868 MHz at the same 3,234,996 CoreMark cycles.'}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
