{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261120-003-r11s2.yaml'","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20261120-003-r11s2\ntitle: Predict the middle carry for integer adds and their dependent addresses\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  The champion takes 3,234,996 cycles for ten iterations. Its reported placement-0\n  path starts at older_rs1_q and ends at EX/MEM.alu_result[23]. ID also computes\n  a full-width sum from the same forwarded EX operands to obtain the page of a\n  dependent memory address. Predicting the live fetch PC in round 10 added\n  41,750 cycles. Arithmetic carry prediction can shorten these two uses of the\n  forwarded operands while retaining same-cycle fetch at the resolved PC.\nhypothesis: |\n  Split a 32-bit integer sum at bit 16. Compute the low result and exact carry\n  with a 17-bit adder. Start the upper adder independently using a predicted\n  carry from bits 15 through 12 of the two operands. For subtraction complement\n  B and use a low carry-in of one. If those four bits all propagate, use the\n  effective B sign as the carry guess. This costs one short carry chain before\n  the upper sum and handles common additions of small signed displacements.\n  Use the same predicted sum for the integer EX result and the ADD-produced\n  base page that ID needs for an immediately dependent load or store.\n\n  Verify the carry before the producer transfers. On a mismatch hold the\n  producer, its forwarding sources and its successor for one clock, save the\n  exact boundary carry, then use it for the high sum on the retry. Qualify the\n  interlock with a valid, effectful arithmetic operation so annulled slots and\n  irrelevant default ALU_ADD decodes cannot hold the pipeline. The check only\n  compares one bit and can run alongside upper-result generation. A key risk is\n  moving the limiting path to carry verification and the pipeline enables.\n  Measure repair cycles and bracketed cycles as well as the three-placement\n  median. At a 0.5% cycle cost acceptance requires about 89.70 MHz.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 6\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/alu.sv\n    description: Form predicted split ADD and SUB results, export the predicted and exact middle carry, and accept a registered carry override for the repair cycle.\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: Register the exact carry on a miss, qualify misses for valid integer ADD, ADDI, AUIPC and SUB writers to nonzero rd, and expose the selected arithmetic sum for the ID base-page bypass. Hold repair state through any concurrent backpressure.\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: Source the ADD producer's base page from the shared split sum. Keep the independent low displacement sum and existing effective-address repair.\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: Hold ID/EX and EX/MEM on the initial carry miss and retain MEM/WB forwarding data while allowing its older instruction to retire once.\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: Connect the carry-miss interlock and the EX sum to ID. Keep carry repair independent of the memory-address repair write enable.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: Force both directions of carry misprediction, include SUB borrow and an ADD immediately feeding a stalled store, and check full RVFI values, retirement order and each accepted address and write.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
