{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_15", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport json\np=Path('.tmp/agent-logs/impl.hyp-20261120-003-r11s2.log')\nfor line in p.open():\n try: it=json.loads(line).get('item',{})\n except ValueError: continue\n if it.get('type')=='agent_message': print(it.get('text',''))\n out=it.get('aggregated_output','')\n if ('77.287' in out or '4,411' in out) and len(out)<4500: print(it.get('id'),out[:2200])\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "I’ll inspect the worktree and available checks, then implement the split adder and test its retry behavior under stalls.\nCo-simulation passed on five programs. CoreMark took 3,239,407 bracketed cycles, with 3,532 carry repairs counted from the retirement trace. The first timing reports put the forwarded operand sign on the critical path, so I’ll adjust how the predictor feeds the upper adder and rerun placement.\nA simulator probe confirmed 3,532 miss cycles and 3,532 retry cycles between the CoreMark markers. The directed store test also passed with three bus denials. Placement now shows the carry check feeding pipeline enables as a limiting path.\nitem_99 Fri Nov 20 12:14:15 UTC 2026\n  1     clock        200.000(MHz)   77.287(MHz)   11      TOP     \n[80%] Routing Phase 2 completed\n...{\n  \"passed\": true,\n  \"elfs_tested\": 5\n}\n25\n\nitem_67 [(77.287, [{'from': 'cpu/u_mem/reg_q.alu_result_14_s0', 'to': 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu/quotient_q_20_s1', 'slack_ns': -7.939, 'arrival_ns': 18.233, 'logic_cells': 11, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_ex', 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu', 'cpu/u_ex', 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu']}]), (77.287, [{'from': 'cpu/u_mem/reg_q.alu_result_14_s0', 'to': 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu/quotient_q_20_s1', 'slack_ns': -7.939, 'arrival_ns': 18.233, 'logic_cells': 11, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_ex', 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu', 'cpu/u_ex', 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu']}])]\n\nitem_100 gowin_v3 {'fmax_mhz': 76.098, 'levels': 12, 'logic': 5015, 'regs': 946, 'lutram': 96, 'bsram': 6, 'dsp': 5} [{'from': 'cpu/u_fwd/older_rs2_q_s0', 'to': 'dmem_0_dmem_0_0_0_s', 'slack_ns': -8.141, 'arrival_ns': 18.436, 'logic_cells': 21, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_ex', 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu', 'cpu/u_ex', 'cpu/u_id']}]\ngowin_p2 {'fmax_mhz': 77.287, 'levels': 11, 'logic': 5015, 'regs': 946, 'lutram': 96, 'bsram': 6, 'dsp': 5} [{'from': 'cpu/u_mem/reg_q.alu_result_14_s0', 'to': 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu/quotient_q_20_s1', 'slack_ns': -7.939, 'arrival_ns': 18.233, 'logic_cells': 11, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_ex', 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu', 'cpu/u_ex', 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu']}]\ngowin_p1 {'fmax_mhz': 77.287, 'le\n…[2062 of 5134 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:623168f085151f2b]…\nLU test sweeps all 256 pairs of prediction nibbles for ADD and SUB.\n\n## CoreMark\n\nTen iterations took **3,239,407 bracketed cycles** with both random bus stalls enabled. The start and stop writes occurred at cycles 11,877 and 3,251,284. This is 4,411 cycles above the champion's 3,234,996 (+0.136%). All five canonical CRCs matched and CoreMark printed `Correct operation validated.`\n\nA simulator probe counted **3,532 carry-miss clocks and 3,532 retry clocks** between the markers. The arithmetic retirement trace independently accounts for 2,010 ADDI repairs, 1,010 ADD repairs and 512 SUB repairs. Each pair of miss and retry clocks adds one clock to its producer's execution.\n\n## Gowin timing\n\n| Placement option\nLint, co-simulation, all 101 cocotb tests and all 53 formal checks passed.\n\nCoreMark recorded **3,532 carry repairs** in **3,239,407 bracketed cycles**. Median Fmax was **77.287 MHz**, yielding **238.58 iterations/s**, 9.55% below the champion. [Implementation notes](./cores/bench/implementation_notes.md)\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
