slot, then release it through the normal bypass.\n  Authorize younger bus strobes, redirects, divider launch and pipeline\n  transfer only after the older result is verified. A refused candidate\n  must never drive a speculative JALR fetch address onto imem.\n\n  The experiment suc\n…[1837 of 4909 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:cd6e6323e95b0ba2]…\neld slot.\n      Keep the predicted load value off the bus until verification\n      authorizes a younger access or fetch redirect.\n  - file: rtl/mem_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Format the returned raw word using the resident load's width,\n      signedness and byte offset. Use the same verified word for\n      RVFI memory data and architectural writeback. Retire once.\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: |\n      Allow a denied load chosen for local service to leave EX. Hold\n      the younger instruction, EX/MEM metadata and older WB forwarding\n      data on a failed probe through refill capture. Give this hold\n      priority over younger repair, division and fetch activity.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: |\n      Warm a RAM word, deny its load and follow it with a dependent\n      branch or address. Exercise a conflicting tag, partial-store\n      lane miss, wrong-candidate JALR and prolonged refill before a\n      younger store. Check bus ownership, PCs, load values and RVFI order.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
