{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_16", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'tail -c 6500 cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'", "aggregated_output": "he EX operands from ID address generation at a cost of 5,837 cycles over ten CoreMark iterations, but the path from `older_rs2_q` through branch comparison and redirect to `ID/EX.pc` limited median Fmax to 79.724 MHz versus the champion's 85.328 MHz.\"}\n{\"id\": \"hyp-20261120-002-r13s1\", \"title\": \"Carry both upper sums across EX/MEM for exact integer forwarding\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The 85.328 MHz champion takes 3,234,996 cycles for ten iterations. Gowin traced a path from older_rs1_q through EX to bit 23 of the EX/MEM result. The same forwarded operands feed a second full-width ADD in ID to form the page of an immediately dependent memory access. Round 12 kept the whole carry-select operation before the register and reached 80.378 MHz. Round 11 put speculative carry verification on pipeline enables and reached 77.287 MHz.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The 85.328 MHz champion takes 3,234,996 cycles for ten iterations. Gowin traced a path from older_rs1_q through EX to bit 23 of the EX/MEM result. The same forwarded operands feed a second full-width ADD in ID to form the page of an immediately dependent memory access. Round 12 kept the whole carry-select operation before the register and reached 80.378 MHz. Round 11 put speculative carry verification on pipeline enables and reached 77.287 MHz.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Split ADD, ADDI, AUIPC and SUB at bit 16. In EX, compute the low half and its unsigned carry-out alongside two upper halves for carry-in zero and one. For subtraction complement the second operand and seed the low adder with one. Register all three data slices and the carry at EX/MEM. Fold ordinary ALU, link and formatted load results into the same representation using their exact low and high halves and a zero select. Select the correct registered upper half on the MEM side for forwarding and writeback. A dependent instruction can issue on the following clock, including a branch or JALR that reads the full result.\\n\\nApply the same register cut to the ID address path that consumes th\n…[3428 of 6500 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:9d5ab16c3766b095]…\negister writes and RVFI.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 244.01, \"delta_pct\": -7.49, \"vs_baseline\": 1913.28, \"fmax_mhz\": 78.937, \"ipc_coremark\": 3e-06, \"cycles\": 3234996, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 5010, \"ff\": 978, \"seeds\": [81.296, 78.937, 78.937], \"perturbations\": [[0, 81.296, 11], [1, 78.937, 13], [2, 78.937, 13]], \"lutram\": 96, \"bsram\": 6, \"dsp\": 5, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_ex/reg_q.result.carry_s0\", \"to\": \"cpu/u_id/reg_q.pc_27_s0\", \"slack_ns\": -7.301, \"arrival_ns\": 17.595, \"logic_cells\": 21, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_if\"]}, \"logic_levels\": 11, \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-20T15:24:43.332820Z\", \"slot\": 1, \"round_id\": 13, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-11-20 hyp-20261120-002-r13s1 (regression, -7.49%): Registering both upper sums kept CoreMark at 3,234,996 cycles, but the next EX shifter had to wait for `EX/MEM.result.carry` to select its forwarded operand, cutting median Fmax from 85.328 to 78.937 MHz.\"}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
