ial products at EX/MEM raised median Fmax from 46.838 to 55.927 MHz, while registering the forwarded operands and doing the full multiply in MEM reached 62.078 MHz with the same 0.81% CoreMark cycle penalty from multiply-use stalls.\n- 2026-11-20 hyp-20261120-002-r3s1 (improvement, +31.48%): Bubbling invalid fetches at ID/EX let the load/multiply interlock compare raw `rs1` and `rs2` with the producer’s `rd` in parallel with EX redirect resolution, raising prototype median Fmax from 46.286 to 60.355 MHz with the same MEM multiplier.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
