{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_6", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg -n --hidden --glob '\"'!**/.git/**'\"' '114\\\\.40|hyp-20261120-003-r3s2|4,188,667|4188667' cores/bench\"", "aggregated_output": "cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl:4:{\"id\": \"hyp-20261120-003-r1s2\", \"title\": \"Predict direct control flow with a displacement-biased agree predictor\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"Fetch advances to PC+4 even at a hot loop backedge or a direct call. Because\\nIF/ID is combinational, a correct next-PC prediction saves one fetch opportunity\\non a ready cycle. Backward loop branches and forward exit branches can share\\nthe same counter constructively if it records agreement with their respective\\ndisplacement biases.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"Fetch advances to PC+4 even at a hot loop backedge or a direct call. Because\\nIF/ID is combinational, a correct next-PC prediction saves one fetch opportunity\\non a ready cycle. Backward loop branches and forward exit branches can share\\nthe same counter constructively if it records agreement with their respective\\ndisplacement biases.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Predict backward conditional branches taken and forward branches fall-through.\\nUse the high bit of a 256-entry table of two-bit saturating counters to invert\\nthat prediction at sites that repeatedly disagree with the bias. Predict JAL\\ntaken and leave JALR sequential until EX. Decode direct targets from the\\ncurrent instruction, so aliases affect direction alone. On the prototype,\\nstalled CoreMark took 4,188,667 bracketed cycles versus 4,491,485 at baseline\\nand passed all five CRCs. Gowin reported 5.236, 5.528 and 5.528 MHz. The\\nmedian gives 13.20 iterations/s versus 12.12. The cycle improvement alone\\ngives 7.23% more iterations per cycle. The prototype used 16 additional\\nLUTRAMs and three additional flip-flops. It passed all 53 single-retire\\nfast formal checks.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 9, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Implement a 256 x 2 distributed RAM indexed by PC[9:2], with one\\nasynchronous fetch read and one synchronous EX update. Initialize words\\nto 01 (weak agreement) at FPGA configuration and retain them on warm\\nreset. On\n…[12504 of 15576 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:d54f1609d79b28b3]…\ns\": 102.72, \"delta_pct\": 10.77, \"vs_baseline\": 747.52, \"fmax_mhz\": 43.026, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4188667, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 2953, \"ff\": 569, \"seeds\": [42.023, 43.026, 43.026], \"perturbations\": [[0, 42.023, 36], [1, 43.026, 35], [2, 43.026, 35]], \"lutram\": 24, \"bsram\": 6, \"dsp\": 6, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu/remainder_q_0_s0\", \"to\": \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu/remainder_q_2_s0\", \"slack_ns\": -18.796, \"arrival_ns\": 29.091, \"logic_cells\": 188, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu\"]}, \"logic_levels\": 36, \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-20T03:43:10.708462Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 2, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-11-20 hyp-20261120-003-r2s2 (regression, +10.77%): Predicting branches and JAL in fetch avoided EX redirects and saved 302,818 CoreMark cycles, but the six-step divider\\u2019s `remainder_q` feedback path limited median Fmax to 43.026 MHz, leaving throughput below the radix-8 core (102.72 vs 104.28 iterations/s).\"}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
