{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'tail -c 3400 cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'","aggregated_output":"pair, register writes, M issue and interlocks. Leave\\nalu_op, alu_src, is_auipc and the other payload fields available\\nto EX. Preserve full-PC verification for denied instruction fetches.\\n\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Train a four-instruction loop containing loads through x1 and x30\\nwith different addresses and data. Deny every loop fetch for the\\nfinal four iterations, put a store on the denied instruction bus,\\nand hold each load for three data-bus denials. Check the sequence\\nof accepted addresses, the retired rs1 values and load results,\\nand the absence of stores. This exercises the two replay banks'\\nshared read, hold and advance behavior.\\n\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"The prototype used logic [19:15] insn_fast [0:511] with\\nsyn_ramstyle=\\\"distributed_ram\\\" and ram_style=\\\"distributed\\\", plus\\nlogic [19:15] early_q. On write_enable write train_insn_q[19:15]\\nat write_index. On !stall register insn_fast[read_index] into\\nearly_q. Keep the original live/replay instruction mux\\nand source bits [19:15] from the live word or the registered rs1\\nfield using the same imem_ready select. The unused five payload\\nbits in the block RAM can be removed by synthesis. Share the row\\nvalidity, read/write collision guard, reset and FENCE.I sweep.\\n\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Keep the default id_ex_w copy of id_ex_q. On annul clear valid\\nand the is_branch, is_jump, is_jalr, mem_read, mem_write, reg_write\\nand late_result bits individually. These suppress redirects, memory\\nstrobes and repair, register writes, M issue and interlocks. Leave\\nalu_op, alu_src, is_auipc and the other payload fields available\\nto EX. Preserve full-PC verification for denied instruction fetches.\\n\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Train a four-instruction loop containing loads through x1 and x30\\nwith different addresses and data. Deny every loop fetch for the\\nfinal four iterations, put a store on the denied instruction bus,\\nand hold each load for three data-bus denials. Check the sequence\\nof accepted addresses, the retired rs1 values and load results,\\nand the absence of stores. This exercises the two replay banks'\\nshared read, hold and advance behavior.\\n\"}], \"outcome\": \"improvement\", \"fitness\": 263.77, \"delta_pct\": 5.25, \"vs_baseline\": 2076.32, \"fmax_mhz\": 85.328, \"ipc_coremark\": 3e-06, \"cycles\": 3234996, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 4965, \"ff\": 944, \"seeds\": [75.641, 85.328, 85.328], \"perturbations\": [[0, 75.641, 15], [1, 85.328, 13], [2, 85.328, 13]], \"lutram\": 96, \"bsram\": 6, \"dsp\": 5, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_fwd/older_rs1_q_s0\", \"to\": \"cpu/u_ex/reg_q.alu_result_23_s0\", \"slack_ns\": -8.22, \"arrival_ns\": 18.515, \"logic_cells\": 31, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_id\", \"cpu/u_ex\"]}, \"logic_levels\": 15, \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-20T09:28:28.870941Z\", \"slot\": 1, \"round_id\": 9, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-11-20 hyp-20261120-002-r9s1 (improvement, +5.25%): Registering a distributed-RAM copy of replay `rs1` bypassed BSRAM delay on the path from `rs1` to the address adder, and annulling only validity and operation enables kept the replay PC check off the EX operand muxes, raising median Fmax from 81.075 to 85.328 MHz.\"}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
