{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_17","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261120-003-r9s2.yaml'","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20261120-003-r9s2\ntitle: \"Predict the instruction two successors ahead to register replay before decode\"\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  The champion takes 3,234,996 cycles for ten CoreMark iterations. Its\n  reported worst path starts at the successor instruction RAM, crosses\n  hazard and decode logic, and ends at data memory. The RAM already\n  covers taken backedges during instruction-bus stalls. Reading it one\n  instruction earlier would give its output a dedicated register before\n  the instruction drives register selection, interlocks and address generation.\nhypothesis: |\n  Train each of the 512 predictor rows on a pair of successive control-flow\n  transitions. For the executed sequence B, C, D, row B learns the full\n  destination word PC and instruction of D from a ready bus fetch. While A\n  executes, use the existing short lookahead index for its likely successor B\n  to launch that row's synchronous read. While B executes, copy the complete\n  returned row into a replay register. While C executes, that register can\n  supply D on a denied fetch. A ready fetch always supplies the live word.\n  This adds a clock boundary between the RAM read and the ID address logic\n  while retaining one issue per cycle on a warm stable path.\n\n  Pair the training key with consecutive admitted instructions. Invalidate\n  broken chains across bubbles, retries or annuls. Freeze the read and replay\n  pipeline together across EX holds. Carry row validity and read/write\n  collision handling through the extra register. On a denied fetch keep the\n  existing full-PC checks against fall-through and aligned redirect target.\n  A mismatch cancels every EX side effect and retries the resolved PC. Flush\n  pending reads and training on reset or FENCE.I. The tradeoff is reduced\n  replay coverage after unpredictable branches. With a 1% cycle penalty the\n  median must exceed 85.66 MHz to clear the 4.6% acceptance margin.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 6\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Delay the training predecessor by one advancing instruction. Read its\n      two-successor prediction through a synchronous block RAM and a separate\n      output register, carrying a usable bit with the word and destination.\n      Handle simultaneous read/write explicitly so tight loops can replay.\n      Preserve live-bus priority, full destination validation, retry and\n      FENCE.I invalidation.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: |\n      Exercise a warm loop through consecutive denials, then change the\n      middle branch outcome so a predicted store has the wrong destination.\n      Check exact retirement PCs and accepted stores through a data hold,\n      a read/write collision, and a FENCE.I with a prediction in flight.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
