{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_103","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cat > 'cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261120-001-r10s0.yaml' <<'YAML'\nid: hyp-20261120-001-r10s0\ntitle: Capture fully forwarded source values at the ID/EX edge\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  On the champion's 85.328 MHz placement, the path from MEM/WB result bit 1\n  through the EX branch comparison to ID/EX.pc[16] arrives at 17.014 ns.\n  The path from older_rs1_q through the ALU to EX/MEM.alu_result[27] arrives\n  at 17.006 ns. Both paths begin by reconstructing an operand in EX. A trial\n  that registered only the bypass selects reached 78.497 MHz median.\nhypothesis: |\n  Move the bypass data mux across the ID/EX boundary. For each incoming\n  source, compute three mutually exclusive enables during decode. The\n  youngest eligible producer supplies the outgoing EX result, including\n  formatted load data on an accepting edge and PC+4 for a legal jump.\n  The next older writer supplies the final combinational MEM result,\n  including MUL or DIV/REM. Otherwise use the write-first register file.\n  Capture the selected 32-bit value directly in the existing ID/EX source\n  register. EX can then start its branch comparison, ALU and address\n  repair from register outputs. An immediately dependent ADD still issues\n  every clock. The timing tradeoff is the return path from the outgoing\n  ALU result to the next operand register. Compute source ownership in\n  parallel with the result so only the data selection follows arithmetic.\n  Qualify the youngest writer with its actual trap-checked write enable.\n  A denied load holds issue until acceptance. An M producer retains its\n  current interlock until its result is available from MEM. A held consumer\n  keeps its captured operands through repair or data-bus backpressure.\n  At 3,234,996 cycles for ten iterations the acceptance target is a\n  three-placement median above 89.25 MHz.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 6\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/forward_unit.sv\n    description: Compute combinational one-hot producer ownership for both ID source tags, including x0 exclusion, youngest-writer priority and suppression of a trapping EX writer.\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: Export the exact data and eligibility entering EX/MEM. Drive both architectural EX operands from the captured ID/EX values for execution, stores and RVFI.\n  - file: rtl/mem_stage.sv\n    description: Expose the existing final writeback value at the input of MEM/WB for the older bypass, including multiply and divide results.\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: Capture the masked OR of the eligible EX, MEM and register-file values separately for rs1 and rs2 when ID advances. Retain both values on every hold.\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: Connect both producer buses and source enables to ID. Preserve the address generator's existing base matches and the late-result issue interlock.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: Exercise different producers for both operands, competing writes to one rd with a younger misaligned load, a held store, and an M result consumed after its interlock.\nYAML\npython - <<'PY'\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\nd=yaml.safe_load(open('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261120-001-r10s0.yaml'))\njsonschema.validate(d,json.load(open('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json')))\nprint(d['title'])\nPY\ngit status --short\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
