{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_8", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nrows=[json.loads(s) for s in open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl')]\nprint(rows[-1].keys())\nfor i in (17,21,26,28,29,30,31,32,33):\n r=rows[i]\n print(r['id'],r['hypothesis'], str(r.get('notes',''))[:6000])\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "dict_keys(['id', 'title', 'category', 'motivation', 'hypothesis', 'expected_impact', 'changes', 'outcome', 'fitness', 'delta_pct', 'vs_baseline', 'fmax_mhz', 'ipc_coremark', 'cycles', 'iterations', 'lut4', 'ff', 'seeds', 'perturbations', 'lutram', 'bsram', 'dsp', 'critical_path', 'logic_levels', 'formal_passed', 'cosim_passed', 'error', 'implementation_notes', 'timestamp', 'slot', 'round_id', 'lesson'])\nhyp-20261120-002-r6s1 {'motivation': \"Successor replay brings ten CoreMark iterations down to 3,486,909 cycles,\\nbut its load-use interlock still bubbled 197,861 available fetches in\\nthat interval. On 38,301 of those cycles the bus denied the fetch and\\nthe successor table supplied a candidate. Each bubble also leaves EX\\nwithout the valid predecessor that enables replay on the retry. Moving\\ndata access into EX previously saved 203,487 cycles on the pre-replay\\ncore. The champion's option-zero timing path crosses the shared EX ALU\\non its way to data memory.\\n\", 'hypothesis': 'Generate the effective address while a live or replayed memory instruction\\nenters ID/EX. Drive the data port from that register in EX. At the\\naccepting edge, clock the extended load value and the integer ALU result\\ninto separate EX/MEM fields. Select between the registered values at\\nthe bypass source. This takes the load mux off the ALU register input\\nand lets the next instruction consume a load, including a branch issued\\nfrom replay. Only the admitted EX slot owns the data port. A replay\\naddress mismatch must squash both bus strobes before the edge.\\n\\nBypass available base producers into address generation. For an immediately\\npreceding ADD, ADDI or AUIPC, fold its two operands and the displacement\\nwith a carry-save compressor and one final adder. An accepted aligned LW\\ncan supply a pointer directly from the bus. Retry an instruction whose\\nyoungest base producer is unavailable. Preserve a single registered\\nbyte address on dmem across backpressure.\\n\\nA scratch prototype completed ten iterations in 3,235,202 bracketed\\ncycles, \n…[30314 of 33386 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:042cd4ded3999cdb]…\nct carry on a miss, qualify misses for valid integer ADD, ADDI, AUIPC and SUB writers to nonzero rd, and expose the selected arithmetic sum for the ID base-page bypass. Hold repair state through any concurrent backpressure.'}, {'file': 'rtl/id_stage.sv', 'description': \"Source the ADD producer's base page from the shared split sum. Keep the independent low displacement sum and existing effective-address repair.\"}, {'file': 'rtl/hazard_unit.sv', 'description': 'Hold ID/EX and EX/MEM on the initial carry miss and retain MEM/WB forwarding data while allowing its older instruction to retire once.'}, {'file': 'rtl/core.sv', 'description': 'Connect the carry-miss interlock and the EX sum to ID. Keep carry repair independent of the memory-address repair write enable.'}, {'file': 'test/test_pipeline.py', 'description': 'Force both directions of carry misprediction, include SUB borrow and an ADD immediately feeding a stalled store, and check full RVFI values, retirement order and each accepted address and write.'}]} \n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
