{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_10", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor line in open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'):\n r=json.loads(line)\n if r['id'].endswith(('r9s1','r10s0','r10s1','r11s0','r11s1','r12s0','r11s2','r12s2')):\n  print(r['id'],r.get('hypothesis'),\\\"\\\\n\\\",r['changes'])\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "hyp-20261120-002-r9s1 {'motivation': \"On the champion's 81.075 MHz placement, Gowin traces the worst path\\nfrom successor BSRAM output bit 15 through rs1 selection, register-file\\nwrite bypass and the address adder to the data-address register. The\\nRAM's clock-to-output delay alone is 2.260 ns. Another path with almost\\nidentical slack runs from the replay target-match register through the\\nannul mask and the EX operand mux to the ALU result. Both paths arise\\nwhen issuing a replayed instruction.\\n\", 'hypothesis': 'Partition the replay entry by when its fields are needed. Give the five\\nrs1 bits a 512-by-5 distributed RAM with an asynchronous read feeding\\nfive flip-flops. Read it at the same lookahead index and on the same\\nedge as the synchronous successor BSRAM. The flip-flops supply rs1\\nearly enough in the next cycle for the register read and address sum.\\nThe BSRAM supplies the saved destination PC, valid bit and remaining\\ninstruction bits. Both reads have the original one-cycle latency.\\n\\nLimit replay annulment to the controls that authorize an operation.\\nA rejected entry can still select ALU inputs and compute a discarded\\nresult while its invalid bit and cleared enables suppress every effect.\\nThis takes the full-PC replay check off the arithmetic operand selects.\\n\\nA scratch implementation ran ten iterations in 3,234,996 bracketed cycles\\nwith both stall generators, the five expected CRCs and the validation\\nbanner. Gowin placement options 0, 1 and 2 gave 75.641, 85.328 and\\n85.328 MHz. The median yields 263.77 iterations/s, 5.25% above 250.62.\\nAcceptance at this cycle count requires more than 84.805 MHz. The\\nmargin is 0.523 MHz, so a fresh three-placement median matters.\\nThe prototype adds 522 logic cells and five registers on placement 0.\\nThe register-tag path alone reached 76.264 MHz on placement 1, and\\nlimiting annulment alone reached 74.043 MHz on that same placement.\\nThe cocotb suite and all 53 standard single-channel formal checks\\npassed. Selftest and all three random ELF traces match\n…[34859 of 37931 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:7daf5027ecc04616]…\nthe load result and dependent LW address bypass. Send misses and stores through the existing bus interface.'}, {'file': 'test/test_pipeline.py', 'description': 'Exercise both read ports under denied reads, partial stores, index aliases and repair. Check every retired load value and accepted store.'}]} \n [{'file': 'rtl/id_stage.sv', 'description': 'Expose independent RF and forwarded word indices alongside the existing architectural address candidate.'}, {'file': 'rtl/load_replay.sv', 'description': 'Replicate the coherent table, register source and collision metadata, and verify the selected row against the resolved load address and lane mask.'}, {'file': 'rtl/core.sv', 'description': 'Connect verified replay to the load result and dependent LW address bypass. Send misses and stores through the existing bus interface.'}, {'file': 'test/test_pipeline.py', 'description': 'Exercise both read ports under denied reads, partial stores, index aliases and repair. Check every retired load value and accepted store.'}]\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
