t\t\t\tassume(!rvfi_halt[`RISCV_FORMAL_CHANNEL_IDX]);\n\t\t\t\tassume(insn_order == rvfi_order[64*`RISCV_FORMAL_CHANNEL_IDX +: 64]);\n\t\t\tend\n\t\t\tif (check) begin\n\t\t\t\tassert(found_next_insn);\n\t\t\tend\n\t\tend\n\tend\nendmodule\n594:    rets, _ = await _run(dut, program, memory, startup_wait=512, bus_ready=bus_ready,\n621:    store_wait = 0\n625:        nonlocal jalr_fetches, target_fetches, store_wait\n630:                if store_wait < 4:\n631:                    store_wait += 1\n632:                    return store_wait % 2, 0\n642:    rets, _ = await _run(dut, program, bus_ready=bus_ready, startup_wait=512,\n646:    assert jalr_fetches == 2 and target_fetches == 2 and store_wait == 4\n660:    store_wait = 0\n\n…[2204 of 5276 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:da8618be63aa5ba4]…\nixed-latency restoring divider. At issue, register the\nmagnitudes of the forwarded operands and the signs needed for the result.\nProcess six quotient bits per clock for six clocks using a 36-bit dividend\npadded with four leading zeros. Each bit uses the borrow from a trial\nsubtraction to select the next remainder. After the sixth clock, select and\nsign-correct the quotient or remainder for the ordinary EX/MEM result slot.\nThis bounds the divider feedback path to six subtract/select steps and\npreserves single-cycle EX for integer ALU operations and all multiplies.\nOnly a valid divide or remainder holds younger instructions. Older operations\ndrain, and the completed result uses the existing forwarding and retirement\npath. The instruction mix predicts zero divider stalls in the measured\nloop. At the baseline cycle count, a median Fmax of 8.17 MHz would deliver\nthe projected 50% gain. Check both median Fmax and marker-to-marker cycles\nbecause a change in stall-generator phase at entry can shift the cycle count.\n\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
