{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_40","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor l in open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'):\n r=json.loads(l)\n if r['id'].endswith(('r7s2','r12s1','r5s0','r6s2','r10s1')):print(r['id'],r['motivation'])\nPY\ncat /srv/hwebench/tmp/3c491641/31941f3e/rv32-r13-pi6iPR/k7/cm.json\"","aggregated_output":"hyp-20261120-001-r5s0 The champion issues data requests in MEM, one cycle too late for a dependent\ninstruction to use a load through the EX/MEM bypass. An instruction trace\nof the ten timed iterations contains 544,852 loads. A branch immediately\nfollows 135,320 loads with a matching source field. Moving address generation\none stage earlier can remove that bubble and keep the FPGA RAM address\nregistered. The latter matters because the champion's reported option-zero\ncritical path crosses the shared EX ALU on its way to data memory.\n\nhyp-20261120-003-r6s2 The champion already replays instructions across taken backedges. Ten\niterations took 3,486,909 cycles with both stalls and 3,353,265 with\ninstruction stalls disabled, a 4.0% throughput difference at equal Fmax.\nThe acceptance margin is 4.6%. A prior trace counted 135,320 loads\nimmediately followed by a branch with a matching source field. An\naddress predictor can make those load values available a cycle earlier.\n\nhyp-20261120-003-r7s2 A ready instruction already issues across a taken branch, and the successor\npredictor covers many denied instruction reads. The champion takes 3,234,996\ncycles with both stall generators. With data memory always ready, the same\npipeline takes 3,043,747 cycles. A load's predicted effective address is\nalready available in ID, one edge before EX needs the data.\n\nhyp-20261120-002-r10s1 Ten iterations take 3,234,996 cycles on the champion. Gowin's placement\n0 path starts at older_rs1_q and ends at EX/MEM. On placement 1 both\nWB-to-branch-PC and bypass-select-to-ALU-result paths approach the\n85.328 MHz limit. The data-address generator also waits for the live\nversus replay instruction choice before reading rs1 and adding the offset.\n\nhyp-20261120-002-r12s1 The champion takes 3,234,996 cycles at 85.328 MHz. Its ID stage calculates\nfive candidate addresses so an EX load can forward to the next instruction.\nBoth round-eleven forwarding experiments reported paths from successor RAM\nthrough ID to data memory. A scratch design with a registered external\nrequest slot and local load service took 3,074,760 marker cycles with both\nbuses stalling and all five CRCs correct. Its median was only 72.449 MHz.\nIt still launched the local RAM read from the speculative ID address and\nfed the hit decision back into EX admission.\n\n{\"completed\": true, \"iter_per_cycle\": 3.0745060421729993e-06, \"cycles\": 3252555, \"iterations\": 10, \"bracketed_cycles\": true}","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_41", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"cat > /srv/hwebench/tmp/3c491641/31941f3e/rv32-r13-pi6iPR/early.py <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport sys,shutil\nsc=Path(__file__).parent\nname=sys.argv[1]; opts=sys.argv[2:]\nd=sc/name/'rtl';shutil.copytree('cores/bench/rtl',d,dirs_exist_ok=True)\ndef ref(file,a,b):\n p=d/(file+'.sv');s=p.read_text();assert s.count(a)==1,(file,a);p.write_text(s.replace(a,b))\nref('mem_stage','  output mem_wb_t out','  output logic [31:0] commit_data,\\\\n  output mem_wb_t out')\na=\\\"in.ctrl.late_result ? (in.instr[14] ? div_result : product)\\\\n                                              : in.alu_result\\\"\nref('mem_stage','reg_q.alu_result <= '+a+';', 'reg_q.alu_result <= commit_data;')\nref('mem_stage','  mem_wb_t reg_q;', '  assign commit_data = '+a+';\\\\n  mem_wb_t reg_q;')\nref('core','  logic        wb_w_en;', '  logic [31:0] commit_data;\\\\n  logic        wb_w_en;')\nref('core','    .out        (mem_wb_w)', '    .commit_data (commit_data),\\\\n    .out        (mem_wb_w)')\nref('core','    .w_en     (wb_w_en),\\\\n    .w_addr   (wb_w_addr),\\\\n    .w_data   (wb_w_data)','''    .w_en     (ex_mem_w.valid && ex_mem_w.ctrl.reg_write && \"'!hold_mem_wb),\n    .w_addr   (ex_mem_w.rd),\n    .w_data   (commit_data)'\"''')\nif 'mwb' in opts:\n ref('reg_file','  input  logic [4:0]  w_addr,','''  input  logic        bypass_en,\n  input  logic [31:0] bypass_data,\n  input  logic [4:0]  w_addr,''')\n ref('reg_file','  assign bypass1 = write_reg','  assign bypass1 = bypass_en && w_addr \"'!= 0'\"')\n ref('reg_file','  assign bypass2 = write_reg','  assign bypass2 = bypass_en && w_addr \"'!= 0'\"')\n ref('reg_file','{32{bypass1}} & w_data','{32{bypass1}} & bypass_data')\n ref('reg_file','{32{bypass2}} & w_data','{32{bypass2}} & bypass_data')\n ref('core','    .w_addr   (ex_mem_w.rd),','''    .bypass_en (ex_mem_w.forwardable),\n    .bypass_data (ex_mem_w.alu_result),\n    .w_addr   (ex_mem_w.rd),''')\n ref('core','.ex_mem_reg_write   (ex_mem_w.ctrl.reg_write)', '.ex_mem_reg_write   (ex_mem_w.ctrl.reg_write && ex_mem_w.ctrl.late_result)')\n # older_rs1_match drives mem_writes_base in core, must stay real for every writer\n ref('core','    .older_rs1_match    (mem_writes_base),','    .older_rs1_match    (),')\n ref('core','  assign use_rf ', '  assign mem_writes_base = ex_mem_w.ctrl.reg_write && ex_mem_w.rd \"'!= 0 && ex_mem_w.rd == rs1_addr_w;'\"\\\\n  assign use_rf ')\nelse:\n # Simply deregister the younger match qualification as in champion, no older EX data bypass\n ref('forward_unit','older_rs1_q && \"'!fwd_rs1[0]'\"', \\\"1'b0\\\")\n ref('forward_unit','older_rs2_q && \"'!fwd_rs2[0]'\"', \\\"1'b0\\\")\n # Write-through integer result already available on the read port\nif 'base' in opts:\n # Direct AGU read from raw array because bypassed base has separate fast path.\n ref('reg_file','  output logic [31:0] rs2_data,','  output logic [31:0] rs2_data,\\\\n  output logic [31:0] rs1_raw,')\n ref('reg_file','  assign rs1_data', '  assign rs1_raw = regs[rs1_addr] & {32{written[rs1_addr]}};\\\\n  assign rs1_data')\n ref('core','  logic [31:0] rs1_data_w;', '  logic [31:0] rs1_data_w, rs1_raw;')\n ref('core','    .rs1_data (rs1_data_w),\\\\n    .rs2_data (rs2_data_w),\\\\n    .w_en', '    .rs1_data (rs1_data_w),\\\\n    .rs1_raw (rs1_raw),\\\\n    .rs2_data (rs2_data_w),\\\\n    .w_en')\n ref('core','    .use_rf   (use_rf),','    .rs1_raw (rs1_raw),\\\\n    .use_rf   (use_rf),')\n ref('id_stage','  input  logic              use_rf,','  input logic [31:0]        rs1_raw,\\\\n  input  logic              use_rf,')\n ref('id_stage','rs1_data[12:0] + disp','rs1_raw[12:0] + disp')\n ref('id_stage','& rs1_data[31:12]', '& rs1_raw[31:12]')\nPY\npython /srv/hwebench/tmp/3c491641/31941f3e/rv32-r13-pi6iPR/early.py memearly base\npython /srv/hwebench/tmp/3c491641/31941f3e/rv32-r13-pi6iPR/early.py memearlym base mwb\nPYTHONPATH=. python /srv/hwebench/tmp/3c491641/31941f3e/rv32-r13-pi6iPR/time_rtl.py memearly 1\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
