{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_10", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"command -v gw_sh; command -v verilator; ls -al /opt; sed -n '1,230p' tools/eval/gowin.py\"", "aggregated_output": "/srv/hwebench/toolchain/oss-cad-suite/bin/verilator\ntotal 20\ndrwxr-xr-x  5 nobody nogroup 4096 Sep 28 05:13 .\ndrwxr-xr-x 20 nobody nogroup 4096 Sep 28 01:00 ..\ndrwxr-xr-x  5 nobody nogroup 4096 Sep 28 05:13 gowin\ndrwxr-xr-x  4 nobody nogroup 4096 Sep 28 02:57 hwe-python\ndrwxr-xr-x  5 nobody nogroup 4096 Sep 28 02:44 hwe-toolchain\n\"\"\"Vendor place-and-route and timing for the FPGA fitness (HWE Bench V2).\n\nV2 times designs with Gowin EDA (the FPGA vendor's own synthesis, place and\nroute and static timing analysis) instead of Yosys + nextpnr, whose timing\nmodel for this part misses whole classes of paths. The vendor flow is also\ndeterministic and insensitive to circuit-neutral netlist changes.\n\nFmax is the median over Gowin's placement algorithms (PLACE_OPTIONS), each\na full build of the same RTL; results are deterministic for a given input.\n\"\"\"\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nfrom concurrent.futures import ThreadPoolExecutor\nimport os\nimport re\nimport shutil\nimport statistics\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nfrom tools.eval._subprocess import remove_path\n\nGOWIN_HOME = Path(os.environ.get(\"GOWIN_HOME\", \"/opt/gowin\"))\nGOWIN_VERSION = \"1.9.11.03 Education\"\nPART = \"GW2AR-LV18QN88C8/I7\"      # Tang Nano 20K\nDEVICE_VERSION = \"C\"\nPLACE_OPTIONS = (0, 1, 2)\nCST = \"fpga/constraints/Tang_Nano_20K.cst\"\nSDC = \"fpga/constraints/clock.sdc\"\nSTALL_GEN = \"fpga/bench_stall_gen.sv\"\nBUILD_TIMEOUT_SEC = 2700\n\n\ndef gowin_env(base: dict | None, workdir: Path) -> dict:\n    env = dict(os.environ if base is None else base)\n    libs = [GOWIN_HOME / \"deps/root/usr/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu\", GOWIN_HOME / \"IDE/lib\"]\n    env[\"LD_LIBRARY_PATH\"] = \":\".join(map(str, libs))\n    env[\"QT_QPA_PLATFORM\"] = \"offscreen\"\n    xdg = workdir / \".xdg\"\n    xdg.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n    os.chmod(xdg, 0o700)\n    env[\"XDG_RUNTIME_DIR\"] = str(xdg)\n    return env\n\n\ndef rtl_sources(rtl_dir: Path) -> list[Path]:\n    srcs = sorted(rtl_dir.glob(\"*.sv\"))\n    pkg = rtl_dir / \"core_pkg.sv\"\n    return ([pkg] if pkg in srcs else []) + [p for p in srcs if p != pkg]\n\n\ndef \n…[7557 of 10629 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:86f7cb084335bf71]…\nopts)\n    for r in res:\n        if r[\"placement_failed\"]:\n            print(f\"place_option {r['place_option']}: FAILED ({r.get('reason')})\")\n            continue\n        print(f\"place_option {r['place_option']}: Fmax {r['fmax_mhz']} MHz, {r['levels']} logic levels; \"\n              f\"logic {r['logic']}, registers {r['regs']}, LUT-RAM {r['lutram']}, BSRAM {r['bsram']}, DSP {r['dsp']}\")\n        tr = (wt / \"cores\" / a.target / \"generated\" / \"timing\" / f\"gowin_p{r['place_option']}\" / \"impl/pnr/core_bench.tr\")\n        for i, p in enumerate(critical_paths(tr.read_text(errors=\"replace\"), a.paths), 1):\n            print(f\"  path {i}: {p['arrival_ns']} ns, {p['logic_cells']} cells, {p['from']} -> {p['to']}\")\n            print(f\"          through: {' > '.join(p['modules'])}\")\n        print(f\"  full report: {tr}\")\n    if len(res) > 1 and all(not r[\"placement_failed\"] for r in res):\n        print(f\"score Fmax (median): {summarize(res)['fmax_mhz']} MHz\")\n    return 0 if all(not r[\"placement_failed\"] for r in res) else 1\n\n\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor r in map(json.loads,open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl')):\n if any(r['id'].endswith(s) for s in ['r12s0','r13s0','r11s2','r14s1','r10s2','r8s0']):\n  print(r['id'],r['hypothesis']['hypothesis'])\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_11", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor r in map(json.loads,open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl')):\n if any(r['id'].endswith(s) for s in ['r12s0','r13s0','r11s2','r14s1','r10s2','r8s0']):\n  print(r['id'],r['hypothesis']['hypothesis'])\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "hyp-20261120-001-r8s0 Use one 32-bit remainder R and one 32-bit dividend/quotient shift\nregister Q. For a nonzero divisor magnitude D below 2^14, R fits in 14\nbits. Resolve the top two dividend bits during setup, then consume 30\nbits in six radix-32 digits. For D >= 2^14, the high 14 dividend bits\nalready form a legal remainder. Seed R with them and Q with the low\n18 dividend bits followed by 14 zeros. Six radix-8 digits then give\nthe complete quotient.\n\nShare the trials for every fourth radix-32 candidate. Write T8 as\n8*R + Q[31:29] and T32 as 4*T8 + Q[28:27]. For j=1..7, T32 >= 4*j*D\nexactly when T8 >= j*D. Seven 35-bit unsigned subtractors supply these\nfit bits to both modes. When digit 4*j wins, its narrow residual is\nthe wide difference with Q[28:27] appended, truncated to 14 bits.\nThe other 24 narrow candidates need only 19-bit trials. Adjacent fit\nflags select the largest fitting digit and its residual in each mode.\nBoth banks read the shared registers directly. The registered mode\nselects the next Q and R on the write side of the recurrence.\n\nAn isolated implementation reached 77.284, 81.254 and 81.254 MHz on\nthe three Gowin placements, versus the champion's 73.409 MHz median.\nThe same digit widths with independent remainder and quotient registers\nreached 75.559 MHz median. The shared implementation used 4,472 logic\ncells, 972 registers, six BSRAMs and five DSPs. With both buses stalled\nby the standard generators, it passed the CoreMark CRC and UART checks\nin 3,234,996 bracketed cycles for ten iterations. Its median gives\n251.17 iterations/s, a 10.69% gain over 226.92. Acceptance at that\ncycle count needs 76.79 MHz.\n\nThe ALU integer-reference vectors and the stalled pipeline tests passed.\nSelftest and all three random ELF traces matched the reference both\nwith and without bus stalls. Preprocessing the prototype and champion\nRTL under RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS produced identical token streams.\n\nhyp-20261120-003-r10s2 Use the saved destination as the fetch PC for a valid branch or jump with a\nusable successor row\n…[6753 of 9825 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:b75a7d2e78024626]…\n.I invalidation for instruction replay.\n\nA scratch scalar-only split completed the canonical CoreMark run in\n3,323,883 bracketed cycles with both stalls, all five CRCs and the\nvalidation banner. Its 77.066 MHz median fell below the champion. The\nleading path started at WB and ended at the prepared first operand, whose\nPC input still depended on EX branch resolution. Capture PC separately\nfrom the register operand and select it locally for AUIPC.\nDeferring operand-dependent control transfers is the proposed timing\nchange. It cuts the forwarded-data-to-compare-to-successor path while\nkeeping the common ALU recurrence off those same buses. At 3.35 million\ncycles the three-placement median must exceed 92.43 MHz for acceptance.\nA median of 95 MHz at that count would yield 284 iterations/s. Measure\ndeferred control transfers, wrong successors and address repairs between\nmarkers. The principal risk is a new critical path from MEM validation\nto a younger bus strobe or from the register file to ID address formation.\n\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
