{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_83","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'cat > \"$TMPDIR/flagtrial/current.yaml\" <<'\"'YAML'\nid: hyp-20261120-001-r15s0\ntitle: Move the upper result mux across EX/MEM and forward low bits directly\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  The champion's timing report traces an older rs1 forwarding decision to\n  EX/MEM.alu_result[23]. The upper bits of an ADD or SUB wait for carry\n  propagation and then for the result mux. The low bits finish earlier, and\n  the next instruction needs them first for a displacement sum or shift count.\nhypothesis: |\n  Split the integer result selector by bit position. Capture result bits\n  12:0 in one EX/MEM register after selecting the complete architectural\n  result for that slice, including formatted loads and jump links. For\n  bits 31:13, capture three parallel slices. One receives the exact upper\n  bits of the ADD result, one the exact upper bits of SUB, and one the\n  selected upper bits for other producers. Generate operation enables in\n  ID. On EX transfer, synchronously zero each unused slice. The OR of the\n  three registered upper slices concatenated with the registered low bits\n  supplies the full result to forwarding, ID address generation and MEM.\n  Compute ADD and SUB over the full operand width so carries across bit 13\n  are included on the producing edge. The split changes only mux placement.\n  \n  In a scratch design that used three banks for all 32 bits, ten canonical\n  iterations took 3,234,996 bracketed cycles and passed the CRC checks.\n  Gowin reported 78.154, 85.345 and 85.345 MHz. On the median placement,\n  ADD bank bit 3 passed through the bank merge and rs2 forwarding into ID's\n  three-input address sum. The direct low slice removes that merge from\n  all 13 bits used in the address calculation. The competing risk is that\n  upper-bit forwarding to a branch becomes critical. At this cycle count,\n  acceptance requires a three-placement median above 89.25 MHz.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 6\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: Carry result-class enables in the ID/EX payload.\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Decode mutually exclusive result enables for ADD, SUB, each remaining\n      integer ALU operation, loads and jump links. Qualify ADD with the\n      decoded result class so a link or load whose ALU defaults to ADD\n      selects its own result. Capture the enables with the resident slot.\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Register the common low slice and the three masked upper slices on\n      the same EX/MEM advance. Hold all slices on address repair and bus\n      denial. Publish their reconstructed word as EX/MEM.alu_result using\n      the existing trap-checked forwarding, late-result and retirement\n      controls. Clear the externally visible result on reset.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: |\n      Alternate ADD, SUB, shift, signed byte load and jump-link producers.\n      Exercise a carry and a borrow across the split, then consume each\n      result as a branch operand or memory base. Check full retired values\n      and accepted addresses through a denied request and a rejected replay.\nYAML\npython - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport os,yaml,json,jsonschema\np=Path(os.environ['TMPDIR'])/'flagtrial/current.yaml'\ns=p.read_text().replace('  \\\\n','\\\\n')\nh=yaml.safe_load(s)\njsonschema.validate(h,json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\n(Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses')/(h['id']+'.yaml')).write_text(s)\nPY\npython \\\"\"'$TMPDIR/flagtrial/results.py\" resqsel restwo resdual resthree resshift resdualq m8 m13 m16 r8 r13 r16'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
