{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_100", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261120-001-r15s0.yaml')\ns=\\\"\\\"\\\"id: hyp-20261120-001-r15s0\ntitle: Partition the EX/MEM result mux by operation and bit position\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  ADD and SUB produce their upper bits late in EX. A right shift can also\n  produce a low bit late because its input comes from anywhere above it in\n  the forwarded word. The result mux puts both paths through the same logic\n  before EX/MEM. The next memory address calculation is especially sensitive\n  to the delay of forwarded bits 12:0.\nhypothesis: |\n  Give EX/MEM two masked result banks for bits 15:0 and three for bits 31:16.\n  In the low half, put SLL, SRL and SRA in one bank. Put all other results\n  in the second bank, using one-hot enables decoded in ID to combine ADD,\n  SUB, Boolean results, comparisons, LUI, the formatted load and PC+4.\n  OR the two registered low halves. In the high half, give ADD and SUB one\n  bank each and put all remaining results in the third. An inactive bank\n  captures zero on transfer. Compute ADD and SUB at full width before\n  slicing so every forwarded bit includes the exact carry or borrow.\n  Both EX bypass ports, the ID base bypass and MEM use the resulting word\n  on the usual cycle.\n  \n  A scratch implementation with three full-width banks completed ten stalled\n  CoreMark iterations in 3,234,996 bracketed cycles with the five canonical\n  CRCs. Its Gowin placements reached 78.154, 85.345 and 85.345 MHz. On the\n  median placement the longest path began at ADD bank bit 3 and crossed the\n  bank merge en route to the dependent address adder. A second trial merged\n  all low 16 bits before EX/MEM. Placement 1 reached 84.887 MHz, with a path\n  from SUB bank bit 25 to low-result bit 4 through forwarded rs1, and another\n  from the rs2 grant through arithmetic and the result mux to bit 14.\n  \n  The proposed two-bank low half removes the final nonshift-result selection\n  from the barrel shifter output and reduces the next low-operand merge to\n  two inputs. That asymmetric partition is unmeasured. The experiment should\n  preserve the bracketed cycle count. It needs a three-placement median above\n  89.25 MHz to clear acceptance. Check both low-result endpoints and the path\n  into the next data address, since the added read-side OR costs timing there.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 6\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: Carry the one-hot result enables in the ID/EX register payload.\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Decode exclusive result enables and hold them with the slot. Use the\n      validated load and jump controls to select formatted data or PC+4 in\n      preference to their incidental default ALU_ADD decode.\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Form the five result slices and capture them together on EX/MEM advance.\n      Keep disabled banks zero and freeze them together on repair or bus hold.\n      Publish the concatenated low and high OR reductions as out.alu_result.\n      Use the existing trap-checked forwardability and M-result qualification.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: |\n      Forward a SUB result with bit 25 set into a right shift by 21 and use\n      bit 4 in a dependent address. Exercise ADD carry and SUB borrow across\n      bit 16, signed shifts, formatted loads, jump links and repeated data\n      denials. Check each full-width retirement and accepted memory request.\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\ns=s.replace('  \\\\n','\\\\n')\nh=yaml.safe_load(s)\njsonschema.validate(h,json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nassert h['id']==p.stem and h['category']=='micro_opt'\nassert all((Path('cores/bench')/x['file']).is_file() for x in h['changes'])\np.write_text(s)\nassert yaml.safe_load(p.read_text())==h\nprint('Validated',p)\nPY\npython \\\"\"'$TMPDIR/flagtrial/results.py\" r8 dedicatedmux flatone flatmux'", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
