{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_6", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor line in open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'):\n d=json.loads(line)\n if d['id'].endswith('r3s1'):\n  for k,v in d.items():print(k,v)\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "id hyp-20261120-002-r3s1\ntitle Execute multiplies in MEM from registered, forwarded operands\ncategory structural\nmotivation The champion's two 46.838 MHz Gowin placements were multiplier-limited.\nEX currently puts register forwarding, multiplication and result selection\nin one cycle. EX/MEM already captures both forwarded source values, and\na multiply leaves the data bus idle in MEM. In the reference trace, only\n35,640 of 93,960 multiplies had an immediate consumer between the markers.\n\nhypothesis {'motivation': \"The champion's two 46.838 MHz Gowin placements were multiplier-limited.\\nEX currently puts register forwarding, multiplication and result selection\\nin one cycle. EX/MEM already captures both forwarded source values, and\\na multiply leaves the data bus idle in MEM. In the reference trace, only\\n35,640 of 93,960 multiplies had an immediate consumer between the markers.\\n\", 'hypothesis': \"Move the four RV32M products into MEM. Feed one signed 33-by-33 multiplier\\nfrom the EX/MEM operands, extending each input by one sign or zero bit\\naccording to the instruction. Register bits 31:0 for MUL or 63:32 for\\na high-half operation in the existing MEM/WB ALU-result field. The EX/MEM\\nboundary then separates the forwarding muxes from the DSP. Independent\\ninstructions, including multiplies, can still issue on successive cycles.\\nGive loads and multiplies one late-result interlock. Compare the fetched\\nrs fields directly with the producer rd in parallel with EX branch\\nresolution. An adjacent consumer takes one bubble and receives the result\\nfrom MEM/WB. Handle invalid fetches at the ID/EX register, since masking\\nthe instruction to a NOP upstream serializes redirect and hazard detection.\\n\\nA scratch prototype with this interlock measured 4,527,760 bracketed cycles\\nfor ten iterations with both bus stalls enabled, 0.81% above the champion.\\nIt reproduced all five CRCs and the validation banner. The self-test and\\nthree randomized RVFI traces matched the reference with and without stalls.\\nGowin's placement option\n…[4948 of 8020 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:87a3005c7fd7aaf2]…\nand values,\\nresults and single retirement on RVFI.\\n'}]\noutcome improvement\nfitness 137.11\ndelta_pct 31.48\nvs_baseline 1031.27\nfmax_mhz 62.078\nipc_coremark 2e-06\ncycles 4527760\niterations 10\nlut4 3329\nff 799\nseeds [58.852, 62.078, 62.078]\nperturbations [[0, 58.852, 14], [1, 62.078, 14], [2, 62.078, 14]]\nlutram 8\nbsram 6\ndsp 2\ncritical_path {'from': 'cpu/u_rf/regs_regs_0_0_s0', 'to': 'cpu/u_id/id_ex_w.rs2_val_28_s1', 'slack_ns': -11.992, 'arrival_ns': 22.286, 'logic_cells': 16, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_id', 'cpu/u_ex', 'cpu/u_id', 'cpu/u_ex', 'cpu/u_id']}\nlogic_levels 14\nformal_passed True\ncosim_passed True\nerror None\nimplementation_notes \ntimestamp 2026-11-20T04:04:36.131021Z\nslot 1\nround_id 3\nlesson - 2026-11-20 hyp-20261120-002-r3s1 (improvement, +31.48%): Bubbling invalid fetches at ID/EX let the load/multiply interlock compare raw `rs1` and `rs2` with the producer’s `rd` in parallel with EX redirect resolution, raising prototype median Fmax from 46.286 to 60.355 MHz with the same MEM multiplier.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
