{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_35","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cat > cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261120-001-r4s0.yaml <<'YAML'\nid: hyp-20261120-001-r4s0\ntitle: Fetch the resolved target in the EX redirect cycle\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  On every aligned taken branch, JAL or JALR, IF presents the fall-through\n  address for the entire EX cycle and discards the bus response. The target\n  is already available from EX and the instruction bus accepts a combinational\n  address. Serving the target in that slot can recover a cycle even for\n  indirect jumps, without a predictor or a new pipeline stage.\nhypothesis: |\n  Drive the fetch address and the PC accompanying the fetched word from the\n  resolved target whenever EX asserts redirect. Decode that response on the\n  normal ready/advance handshake. Register the address presented and a bit\n  indicating that ID accepted it. On the next cycle, issue the saved address\n  plus four after acceptance, or retry the saved address after a stall. A new\n  EX redirect takes priority over either choice. This puts the increment\n  after the address register and keeps it off the redirect-to-register path.\n  Suppress the redirect bubble because the bus now carries the target word.\n  An unready fetch still bubbles ID/EX, an older stalled data access holds\n  it, and the existing EX logic handles JALR alignment and misaligned traps.\n  A scratch prototype completed ten iterations with both bus stalls in\n  4,171,092 bracketed cycles, down from 4,527,760. All five CRCs matched.\n  At that cycle count a median Fmax above 59.83 MHz clears the acceptance\n  threshold. Gowin placement option 1 reached 60.569 MHz.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 6\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Mux the live redirect target onto imem_addr and out.pc. Record the\n      presented address and acceptance (\"'!stall) each clock. Reset both to\n      zero so the first request is PC zero. On a cycle without a redirect,\n      select the registered address or its successor with the acceptance bit.\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: |\n      Remove redirect from the ID/EX bubble condition. Preserve the fetched\n      operand interlock, fetch-valid bubble and data/divider hold priorities.\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: |\n      Remove the redundant redirect input on the hazard instance. Keep EX\n      resolution wired to IF and keep the fetch acceptance tied to stall_if.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: |\n      Check adjacent branch and target retirements on a ready bus, including\n      a JALR that consumes a forwarded base. Update the wrong-path store test\n      to expect zero fetches of skipped PCs and drive a store on a denied\n      target fetch. Check target retry, link value, absence of store strobes\n      and consecutive RVFI order, including a redirect held by an older\n      stalled data request.\nYAML\nPYTHONPATH=. PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 python -u \"$TMPDIR/microprobe/time.py\" prev 0 2 > \"$TMPDIR/microprobe/prev/others\"'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_36","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'cat > \"$TMPDIR/microprobe/select.py\" <<'\"'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport os,shutil\np=Path(os.environ['TMPDIR'])/'microprobe'\nfor name in ('onehot','muxredir','separate'):\n rtl=p/name/'rtl'\n shutil.copytree(p/'prev'/'rtl',rtl,dirs_exist_ok=True)\n f=rtl/'ex_stage.sv'\n s=f.read_text()\n decl='  output logic               redirect,\\\\n  output logic [31:0]        redirect_target\\\\n'\n if name\"'!='\"'muxredir':\n  s=s.replace(decl,'''  output logic               take_direct,\n  output logic               take_indirect,\n  output logic [31:0]        direct_target,\n  output logic [31:0]        indirect_target\n''')\n i=s.index('  assign redirect ')\n j=s.index('  // ── EX/MEM register',i)\n sel='''  assign take_direct = (branch_taken || (in.ctrl.is_jump && \"'!in.ctrl.is_jalr))\n                     && branch_target[1:0] == 2'\"'b00;\n  assign take_indirect = in.ctrl.is_jalr && \"'!jalr_sum[1];\n  assign direct_target = branch_target;\n  assign indirect_target = {jalr_sum[31:1], 1'\"'b0};\n'''\n if name=='muxredir':\n  sel=\\\"\\\"\\\"  assign redirect = ((branch_taken || (in.ctrl.is_jump && \"'!in.ctrl.is_jalr)) && branch_target[1:0] == 0)\n                  || (in.ctrl.is_jalr && !jalr_sum[1]);\n  assign redirect_target = in.ctrl.is_jalr ? {jalr_sum[31:1], 1'\"'b0} : branch_target;\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\n f.write_text(s[:i]+sel+'\\\\n'+s[j:])\n if name=='muxredir':continue\n f=rtl/'if_stage.sv'\n s=f.read_text()\n a=s.index('  input  logic              redirect,')\n b=s.index('  output logic [31:0]       imem_addr,',a)\n s=s[:a]+'''  input  logic              take_direct, take_indirect,\n  input  logic [31:0]       direct_target, indirect_target,\n'''+s[b:]\n line=\\\"  assign imem_addr = redirect ? redirect_target : last_accepted ? last_fetch + 32'd4 : last_fetch;\\\"\n if name=='onehot':\n  which='''  logic [31:0] sequential;\n  assign sequential = last_accepted ? last_fetch + 32'd4 : last_fetch;\n  assign imem_addr = ({32{take_direct}} & direct_target)\n                   | ({32{take_indirect}} & indirect_target)\n                   | ({32{\"'!take_direct && !take_indirect}} & sequential);'\"'''\n else:\n  which='''  assign imem_addr = take_direct ? direct_target :\n                     take_indirect ? indirect_target :\n                     last_accepted ? last_fetch + 32'd4 : last_fetch;'''\n assert line in s\n f.write_text(s.replace(line,which))\n f=rtl/'core.sv'\n s=f.read_text().replace('  logic        redirect;\\\\n  logic [31:0] redirect_target;','  logic take_direct, take_indirect;\\\\n  logic [31:0] direct_target, indirect_target;')\n ports=\\\"\\\"\\\".take_direct     (take_direct),\n    .take_indirect   (take_indirect),\n    .direct_target   (direct_target),\n    .indirect_target (indirect_target)\\\"\\\"\\\"\n s=s.replace('.redirect        (redirect),\\\\n    .redirect_target (redirect_target)',ports)\n f.write_text(s)\nPY\npython \\\"\"'$TMPDIR/microprobe/select.py\"'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
