g PC with retry_pc. Reset it to zero\n      and otherwise register imem_addr unconditionally. Drive imem_addr as\n      redirect ? redirect_target : ex_valid ? ex_pc + 4 : retry_pc. Use\n      imem_addr for out.pc and imem_ready for out.valid. This keeps target\n      plus four off the redirect path and preserves the PC across bubbles.\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Form the fetch redirect enable from two parallel conditions. Take an\n      aligned PC-relative target for branch_taken or a direct jump. Take a\n      decoded JALR when jalr_sum[1] is clear. Use is_jalr to select the\n      bit-zero-cleared JALR sum or the PC-relative target. Preserve the\n      existing misalignment trap, link write suppression and RVFI pc_next.\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: |\n      Remove the redirect input and stall_if output. Bubble ID/EX on a\n      late-use match or invalid fetch when EX can advance. Keep the ID/EX\n      hold for an older data-bus stall or divide wait. The instruction\n      presented on a redirect now belongs to the target PC.\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: |\n      Wire id_ex_w.valid and id_ex_w.pc to IF along with the resolved EX\n      redirect and target. Remove the obsolete stall_if and hazard redirect\n      connections. Preserve the single-channel retirement interface.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: |\n      Assert consecutive retirement cycles for a ready branch or JALR and\n      its target, including a forwarded JALR base. Update the wrong-path\n      store test to assert zero fetches of skipped PCs and drive a store\n      on denied target fetches. Hold a branch behind an older stalled\n      store, deny imem on the release edge, and check the target retries,\n      one accepted store, link data and consecutive RVFI order. Check that\n      misaligned taken targets trap and continue at the fall-through PC.\nYAML\npython - <<'PY'\nimport json, yaml, jsonschema\nfrom pathlib import Path\nroot=Path('cores/bench')\np=root/'experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261120-001-r4s0.yaml'\nd=yaml.safe_load(p.read_text())\njsonschema.validate(d, json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nassert d['id']==p.stem and d['category']=='micro_opt'\nassert all((root/c['file']).is_file() for c in d['changes'])\nassert type(d['expected_impact']['fitness_delta_pct']) is int\nprint(f'{p.name} passes schema and target path checks')\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "hyp-20261120-001-r4s0.yaml passes schema and target path checks\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
