{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_43", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor l in open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'):\n d=json.loads(l)\n if 'r4s1' in d['id']:\n  print(d['hypothesis'])\nPY\nsed -n '118,181p' test/cosim/main.cpp && sed -n '108,144p' test/cosim/reference.py\"", "aggregated_output": "{'motivation': 'The champion spends 4,527,760 cycles on ten CoreMark iterations. A taken\\nbranch spends one fetch opportunity on fall-through even though EX knows\\nthe target that cycle. A backend hold can also discard a ready instruction\\nand force decode to wait for the bus a second time.\\n', 'hypothesis': 'Give IF one fall-through buffer holding an instruction and its PC. When\\nempty, drive the instruction address from the registered fetch cursor or\\nthe aligned redirect resolved by EX. Decode can accept the target on the\\nsame edge that the branch advances. If a redirect stalls, retain the\\nexact target for retry. On a sequential fetch, buffer a ready word when\\ndecode is blocked and advance the bus cursor. Decode can later issue\\nthat word even when imemReady is low.\\n\\nRecord whether the buffered instruction permits refill. When issuing a\\nbuffered branch, JAL, JALR or fence, leave the buffer empty for its\\nsuccessor. For an ordinary instruction, dequeue and refill on the same\\nedge if the bus is ready. Thus a buffered word and an EX redirect cannot\\ncoexist. The registered full bit selects the instruction presented to\\ndecode, keeping EX branch comparison off the register-file address path.\\n\\nThe guarded buffer completed ten iterations in 4,051,673 bracketed\\ncycles with both bus stalls enabled, a 10.51% reduction. It reproduced\\nall five CRCs and the validation banner. Gowin placement options 0, 1\\nand 2 reached 60.269, 60.507 and 60.507 MHz, giving 149.34 iterations/s\\nagainst the 137.11 champion. The prototype passed all 53 standard\\nsingle-channel formal checks. A separate induction check with symbolic\\nbus backpressure proved that full and redirect cannot coincide.\\n', 'expected_impact': {'fitness_delta_pct': 9, 'confidence': 'high'}, 'changes': [{'file': 'rtl/if_stage.sv', 'description': \"Store the word, its PC, a full bit and a refill-permitted bit.\\nDisable refill for instr[6:4] == 3'b110 and opcode 7'b0001111.\\nAccept a bus word when ready and either empty or issuing a\\nrefill-permitted head. On \n…[5319 of 8391 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:6d87a1f180d3f506]…\nlegal).\"\"\"\n        if trap:\n            wrd = wval = 0\n            mem_addr = mem_rmask = mem_wmask = 0\n            mem_rdata = mem_wdata = 0\n            npc = (pc + 4) & MASK\n        if wrd:\n            self.regs[wrd] = wval\n        self.regs[0] = 0\n        self.pc = npc\n        out = {\n            'order': self.retired, 'pc': pc, 'npc': npc, 'insn': instr,\n            'rd': wrd, 'rd_wdata': wval if wrd else 0,\n            'rs1': rs1, 'rs1_rdata': rs1_rdata_pre,\n            'rs2': rs2, 'rs2_rdata': rs2_rdata_pre,\n            'mem_addr': mem_addr, 'mem_rmask': mem_rmask, 'mem_rdata': mem_rdata,\n            'mem_wmask': mem_wmask, 'mem_wdata': mem_wdata,\n            'trap': trap, 'halt': 0, 'intr': 0, 'mode': 3, 'ixl': 1,\n        }\n        self.retired += 1\n        return out\n\n    def step(self) -> Optional[dict]:\n        instr = self.rw(self.pc)\n        op  = instr & 0x7F\n        rd  = (instr >> 7)  & 0x1F\n        fn3 = (instr >> 12) & 0x7\n        rs1 = (instr >> 15) & 0x1F\n        rs2 = (instr >> 20) & 0x1F\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
