{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_5", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor n,l in enumerate(open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl')):\n d=json.loads(l)\n if n==15:\n  for k,v in d.items():\n   print(k, ':', str(v)[:12500])\n elif n in (10,13,14):\n  for k in ('id','hypothesis','implementation_notes','worst_path','seeds','fitness','cycles'):\n   print(k,':',str(d.get(k))[:1300])\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "id : hyp-20261120-001-r4s0\nhypothesis : {'motivation': 'The champion spends 4,527,760 cycles on ten CoreMark iterations. On a\\ntaken branch, JAL or JALR, IF presents the fall-through address while EX\\nresolves the target, then discards that fetch. The combinational imem\\ninterface can serve the resolved target during the same cycle. This also\\nworks for indirect jumps because EX already has the forwarded JALR base.\\n', 'hypothesis': 'Let the resident EX instruction select the fetch address. Give its aligned\\nredirect target first priority. Otherwise issue ID/EX.pc + 4 when ID/EX\\nis valid. When ID/EX is empty, issue a retry address held in a 32-bit IF\\nregister. Reset this register to zero and capture the actual bus address\\non every other rising edge. Send the same address to ID as the fetched PC.\\nA held EX instruction keeps selecting its successor. A bubble from an\\nunready fetch or a late-result dependency retries the address on the next\\ncycle. A ready target can enter ID/EX on the edge its branch leaves EX.\\nThis uses the existing branch decision and requires no prediction state.\\n\\nA scratch RTL prototype completed ten iterations in 4,171,092 bracketed\\ncycles with both stall generators enabled, saving 356,668 cycles (7.88%).\\nAll five CRCs and the UART validation banner matched. The self-test and\\nthree randomi\nimplementation_notes : \nworst_path : None\nseeds : [62.465, 64.034, 64.034]\nfitness : 153.52\ncycles : 4171092\nid : hyp-20261120-001-r5s0\nhypothesis : {'motivation': \"The champion issues data requests in MEM, one cycle too late for a dependent\\ninstruction to use a load through the EX/MEM bypass. An instruction trace\\nof the ten timed iterations contains 544,852 loads. A branch immediately\\nfollows 135,320 loads with a matching source field. Moving address generation\\none stage earlier can remove that bubble and keep the FPGA RAM address\\nregistered. The latter matters because the champion's reported option-zero\\ncritical path crosses the shared EX ALU on its way to data memory.\\n\", 'hypothesis': 'Co\n…[9635 of 12707 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:98a24b460c17fedd]…\n\noutcome : improvement\nfitness : 176.55\ndelta_pct : 15.0\nvs_baseline : 1356.68\nfmax_mhz : 61.563\nipc_coremark : 3e-06\ncycles : 3486909\niterations : 10\nlut4 : 3540\nff : 866\nseeds : [62.145, 61.563, 61.563]\nperturbations : [[0, 62.145, 15], [1, 61.563, 15], [2, 61.563, 15]]\nlutram : 8\nbsram : 8\ndsp : 2\ncritical_path : {'from': 'cpu/u_rf/regs_regs_0_0_s0', 'to': 'dmem_1_dmem_1_0_0_s', 'slack_ns': -11.091, 'arrival_ns': 21.386, 'logic_cells': 20, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_id', 'cpu/u_ex', 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu', 'cpu/u_ex']}\nlogic_levels : 15\nformal_passed : True\ncosim_passed : True\nerror : None\nimplementation_notes : \ntimestamp : 2026-11-20T05:02:04.433223Z\nslot : 2\nround_id : 5\nlesson : - 2026-11-20 hyp-20261120-003-r5s2 (improvement, +15.00%): Replaying the successor instruction from a table indexed by predecessor PC kept CoreMark issuing across taken loop backedges with `io_imemReady` low, while parallel checks of the saved successor PC against `fallthrough_pc` and `redirect_target` let EX annul mismatches.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
