{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_82", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261120-001-r6s0.yaml && python - <<'PY'\ns=672000000/3320238; print(s,(s/176.55-1)*100,3486909-3320238,100*(1-3320238/3486909),'MHz min',176.55*1.046*3320238/1e7)\nPY\nrg -c 'DONE \\\\(PASS' \\\"\"'$TMPDIR/clean/formal.out\" && rg '\"'TESTS=' \\\"\"'$TMPDIR/clean/pipeline.out\"'", "aggregated_output": "id: hyp-20261120-001-r6s0\ntitle: \"Issue memory requests from a registered address one stage earlier\"\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  The champion takes 3,486,909 cycles for ten CoreMark iterations. Its\n  successor replay can supply the next instruction during a fetch stall,\n  but a load-use interlock still discards that slot. The previous trace\n  counted 135,320 loads immediately followed by a branch with a matching\n  source. On the pre-replay core, early address generation saved 203,487\n  cycles and moved the reported worst path away from the data RAM.\nhypothesis: |\n  Compute a load or store's byte address as it enters ID/EX and present\n  that register to dmem during EX. On the accepting edge, put the formatted\n  load in EX/MEM. The next instruction can use the existing registered\n  bypass, including a branch that must select its successor in that cycle.\n  Compute addresses for adjacent ADD/ADDI-produced bases using a carry-save\n  sum of the producer operands and the displacement. Interlock an address\n  whose youngest producer cannot supply its value in time.\n\n  A replayed instruction may have entered ID/EX provisionally. Qualify\n  every early request and data wait with the resident slot's verified\n  controls and alignment. A rejected prediction must retry the resolved\n  PC without issuing a store, reading MMIO or blocking EX on dmemReady.\n  Keep address, store data and replay verification aligned across waits.\n  A scratch prototype completed ten iterations in 3,235,202 bracketed\n  cycles with both stall generators, saving 251,707 cycles. All five CRCs\n  and the UART validation banner matched. Gowin placement options 0, 1\n  and 2 gave 54.866, 60.688 and 60.688 MHz. The median gives 187.59\n  iterations/s against the champion's 176.55. Selftest and the three\n  random instruction traces matched the reference with and without stalls.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 6\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: Carry the byte address in ID/EX and the serviced address and raw read word in EX/MEM for RVFI.\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: Compute the incoming memory address from the youngest available base. Select the carry-save ADD/ADDI address, a bypassable producer plus displacement, or the write-first register-file base plus displacement. Capture only on issue.\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: Present the registered address, qualified strobes and forwarded store data. On transfer, capture the accepted read word and extended load result with the address. Expose operands for dependent address generation.\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: Replace the blanket load-use bubble with an address-base interlock. Retain the multiply-use interlock. Hold a verified EX request and its forwarding sources until data acceptance.\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: Wire the data port to EX behind the existing replay annul mask. Resolve base dependencies by producer age, exclude x0 and trapped writes, and make the accepted load available through EX/MEM forwarding.\n  - file: rtl/mem_stage.sv\n    description: Use the captured address, raw word, lane masks and store data for the retirement record. Pass the formatted load value to writeback and keep product generation in MEM.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: Check consecutive load and dependent branch retirements on ready buses, dependent address carries, subword results, and misalignment. Force a denied replay with a stale store or MMIO load and verify zero spurious requests, then stall a verified request and check exactly one acceptance.\n202.3951295057764 14.63898584297727 166671 4.779906788505239 MHz min 61.315266776940014\n15\n                                                        ** TESTS=24 PASS=24 FAIL=0 SKIP=0                                         40004.02           0.07     598035.53  **\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
