{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_86", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"cat > cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261120-001-r8s0.yaml <<'YAML'\nid: hyp-20261120-001-r8s0\ntitle: \\\"Share seven trial subtractors between radix-32 and radix-8 division\\\"\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  The champion's 74-cell path goes from quotient_q[31] to remainder_q[1]\n  through two dependent divider digit selections. Even the earlier split\n  at 2\"'^17 kept two radix-8 steps on the narrow feedback path. CoreMark\n  executes zero DIV/REM between markers, so this path costs clock speed on\n  every measured instruction. A single digit decision on each feedback\n  edge can improve Fmax within the existing retirement-latency bound.\nhypothesis: |\n  Use one 32-bit remainder R and one 32-bit dividend/quotient shift\n  register Q. For a nonzero divisor magnitude D below 2''^14, R fits in 14\n  bits. Resolve the top two dividend bits during setup, then consume 30\n  bits in six radix-32 digits. For D >= 2''^14, the high 14 dividend bits\n  already form a legal remainder. Seed R with them and Q with the low\n  18 dividend bits followed by 14 zeros. Six radix-8 digits then give\n  the complete quotient.\n\n  Share the trials for every fourth radix-32 candidate. Write T8 as\n  8*R + Q[31:29] and T32 as 4*T8 + Q[28:27]. For j=1..7, T32 >= 4*j*D\n  exactly when T8 >= j*D. Seven 35-bit unsigned subtractors supply these\n  fit bits to both modes. If j fits, the narrow residual for digit 4*j\n  is the wide difference with Q[28:27] appended, truncated to 14 bits.\n  The other 24 narrow candidates need only 19-bit trials. Adjacent fit\n  flags select the largest fitting digit and its residual in each mode.\n  Both banks read the shared registers directly. The registered mode\n  selects the next Q and R on the write side of the recurrence.\n\n  An isolated implementation reached 77.284, 81.254 and 81.254 MHz on\n  the three Gowin placements, versus the champion'\"'s 73.409 MHz median.\n  The same digit widths with independent remainder and quotient registers\n  reached 75.559 MHz median. The shared implementation used 4,472 logic\n  cells, 972 registers, six BSRAMs and five DSPs. At 3,234,996 bracketed\n  cycles for ten iterations, its median gives 251.17 iterations/s, a\n  10.69% gain over 226.92. Acceptance at that cycle count needs 76.79 MHz.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 11\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/alu.sv\n    description: |\n      Keep the issue, six-wait and consume schedule. On issue capture the\n      magnitudes, operation and output sign. On the first wait register\n      the mode, initial R and Q, and odd divisor multiples. Derive even\n      multiples by shifts. Use 35-bit 3D, 5D and 7D in the shared bank.\n      In the narrow bank use their low bits and form the other odd\n      multiples at 19 bits. The timed prototype used shift/add or\n      carry-save sums for these constants and constant products for\n      23D, 27D and 29D. Each trial has an extra borrow bit.\n\n      Feed wide fit[j] directly to narrow fit[4*j]. Form the associated\n      14-bit residual from wide_difference[j][11:0] and Q[28:27].\n      On each of five more wait edges and once on consume, append the\n      selected three or five quotient bits and register the corresponding\n      residual. For D=0, all trial digits fit and Q becomes all ones.\n      Retain the full dividend magnitude for the zero-divisor remainder.\n      Apply the saved sign in MEM, including INT_MIN / -1. Preserve the\n      existing ALTOPS formulas, channel-0 retirement, and completion\n      semantics when consume or MEM writeback is delayed.\n  - file: test/test_alu.py\n    description: |\n      Extend the integer-reference vectors around D=0x3fff, 0x4000 and\n      0x4001. Exercise kD-1, kD and kD+1 for all narrow digits, each of\n      the four low-bit suffixes at shared thresholds, the largest wide\n      quotient, signed variants and zero divisors. Alternate modes on\n      consecutive requests and keep the exact six-wait, delayed-consume,\n      reset and post-consume result checks.\nYAML\npython - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport json,yaml,jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261120-001-r8s0.yaml')\nd=yaml.safe_load(p.read_text())\njsonschema.validate(d,json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nprint(d['id'],d['category'],d['expected_impact'])\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
