{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"ls -la /srv/hwebench/clones/gpt-6_2-astra_xhigh-v2-rep2/cores/bench/worktrees && ls -a bench/programs | head -45\npython - <<'PY'\nimport json\nr=list(map(json.loads,open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl')))[-3]\nprint(r['hypothesis']['hypothesis'])\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"total 40\ndrwxrwx---+  5 nobody nogroup 4096 Nov 20 09:20 .\ndrwxrwx---+  8 nobody nogroup 4096 Nov 20 04:20 ..\ndrwxrwx---+ 12 nobody nogroup 4096 Nov 20 09:21 hyp-20261120-001-r9s0-hypgen\ndrwxrwx---+  9 nobody nogroup 4096 Nov 20 09:20 hyp-20261120-002-r9s1-hypgen\ndrwxrwx---+  9 nobody nogroup 4096 Nov 20 09:20 hyp-20261120-003-r9s2-hypgen\n.\n..\nMakefile\ncoremark\ncrt0.S\ngen_random_trace.py\nlink.ld\nrandom1.S\nrandom2.S\nrandom3.S\nselftest.S\nUse one 32-bit remainder R and one 32-bit dividend/quotient shift\nregister Q. For a nonzero divisor magnitude D below 2^14, R fits in 14\nbits. Resolve the top two dividend bits during setup, then consume 30\nbits in six radix-32 digits. For D >= 2^14, the high 14 dividend bits\nalready form a legal remainder. Seed R with them and Q with the low\n18 dividend bits followed by 14 zeros. Six radix-8 digits then give\nthe complete quotient.\n\nShare the trials for every fourth radix-32 candidate. Write T8 as\n8*R + Q[31:29] and T32 as 4*T8 + Q[28:27]. For j=1..7, T32 >= 4*j*D\nexactly when T8 >= j*D. Seven 35-bit unsigned subtractors supply these\nfit bits to both modes. When digit 4*j wins, its narrow residual is\nthe wide difference with Q[28:27] appended, truncated to 14 bits.\nThe other 24 narrow candidates need only 19-bit trials. Adjacent fit\nflags select the largest fitting digit and its residual in each mode.\nBoth banks read the shared registers directly. The registered mode\nselects the next Q and R on the write side of the recurrence.\n\nAn isolated implementation reached 77.284, 81.254 and 81.254 MHz on\nthe three Gowin placements, versus the champion's 73.409 MHz median.\nThe same digit widths with independent remainder and quotient registers\nreached 75.559 MHz median. The shared implementation used 4,472 logic\ncells, 972 registers, six BSRAMs and five DSPs. With both buses stalled\nby the standard generators, it passed the CoreMark CRC and UART checks\nin 3,234,996 bracketed cycles for ten iterations. Its median gives\n251.17 iterations/s, a 10.69% gain over 226.92. Acceptance at that\ncycle count needs 76.79 MHz.\n\nThe ALU integer-reference vectors and the stalled pipeline tests passed.\nSelftest and all three random ELF traces matched the reference both\nwith and without bus stalls. Preprocessing the prototype and champion\nRTL under RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS produced identical token streams.\n\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
