{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_28", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor r in map(json.loads, open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl')):\n if r['id'].endswith(('r6s0','r6s2','r5s0')):\n  print(r['id'],r['hypothesis']['hypothesis'])\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "hyp-20261120-001-r5s0 Compute the full byte address as a memory instruction enters ID/EX. Drive\nthe data bus from this register during EX. On acceptance, latch the raw\nread word for RVFI and the formatted load value in EX/MEM for ordinary EX\nforwarding. Stores use the forwarded rs2 in EX. A stalled request holds\nits address, data, enables and producer operands through the accepting edge.\n\nTo handle a newly produced base, compare the incoming rs1 against the\nyoungest writers. For ADD, ADDI and AUIPC in EX, their operands A and B\nare already available. With displacement D, compute P = A XOR B, then\n(P XOR D) + (((A AND B) OR (P AND D)) << 1) modulo 2^32. This gives\nA+B+D with one carry-propagate adder. Compute it in parallel with the normal\nbase-plus-displacement path. A preceding LUI supplies its immediate and an\naligned, accepted LW can supply the raw bus word. Use the EX/MEM value for\nolder available writers and the write-first register file otherwise.\nInterlock unavailable bases, including pending products. Suppress x0 and\ntrapped writes. Keep the multiply-use interlock for ordinary EX consumers.\n\nA scratch prototype completed ten iterations in 3,967,605 bracketed cycles\nversus 4,171,092 for the champion, with all canonical CRCs. Gowin placement\noptions 0, 1 and 2 reached 61.552, 66.658 and 66.658 MHz respectively.\nThe median gives 168.01 iterations/s, 9.44% above the champion. The\nprototype passed all 53 standard single-channel formal checks. The selftest\nand three random programs matched the reference with and without bus stalls.\n\nhyp-20261120-001-r6s0 Compute the full byte address as a load or store enters ID/EX and drive\ndmem directly from that register during EX. Capture the formatted load\ninto EX/MEM on acceptance. An immediately dependent branch can then\nresolve from a registered operand and issue its successor in one cycle.\n\nGive the decode-stage address adder two candidate bases. The ordinary\ncandidate selects the youngest available EX/MEM result or the write-first\nregister file. If the immediately pre\n…[2557 of 5629 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:adae6a2bb913c65f]…\npressure. An accepted\nload forwards from EX/MEM to the next instruction.\n\nA scratch implementation completed the ten timed iterations in 3,234,996\ncycles with both stall generators and all five canonical CRCs. Gowin\nplacement options 0, 1 and 2 reached 60.066, 61.400 and 61.400 MHz.\nThe median gives 189.80 iterations/s, 7.50% above 176.55. At that cycle\ncount, acceptance requires a median above 59.7411 MHz. All 53 standard\nsingle-channel formal checks passed. The selftest and three random ELF\ntraces matched the reference with and without stalls.\nA directed test observed one accepted store after three denied cycles\nat a repaired address and consecutive retirement of a load and its branch.\n\nA matched control with full-width address adders also issued memory\noperations in EX. It took 3,235,018 cycles at 64.020 MHz. Early load\navailability accounts for the cycle gain over the champion. These\nplacements favor full-width adders for Fmax, so they do not establish\na separate frequency gain from predicting the page.\n\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_29","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'ls -a /srv/hwebench/tmp/3c491641/d0123d24/r9-research/late/timing/gowin_p1\ncat /srv/hwebench/tmp/3c491641/d0123d24/r9-research/page12/rtl/id_stage.sv | tail -65\nls /srv/hwebench/clones/gpt-6_2-astra_xhigh-v2-rep2/bench/programs/*.elf'","aggregated_output":".\n..\n.xdg\nbuild.tcl\ngw.log\nimpl\n    ctrl_decoded.reg_write  = dec_reg_write;\n    // All eight funct3 values of OP with funct7=1 are legal M operations.\n    ctrl_decoded.late_result = in.instr[6:0] == 7'b0110011 && in.instr[31:25] == 7'b0000001;\n    ctrl_decoded.is_illegal = dec_is_illegal;\n  end\n\n  // ── ID/EX register ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n  id_ex_t reg_q;\n\n  // Only LOAD and STORE use these candidates. Bit 5 distinguishes their\n  // immediate encodings. A signed 12-bit offset can cross at most one\n  // page, so a change of bit 12 detects both carry and borrow.\n  logic [12:0] disp, rf_sum, mem_sum, lw_sum;\n  assign disp = {{1{in.instr[31]}}, in.instr[31:25],\n                 in.instr[5] ? in.instr[11:7] : in.instr[24:20]};\n  assign rf_sum  = rs1_data[12:0] + disp;\n  assign mem_sum = mem_result[12:0] + disp;\n  assign lw_sum  = lw_word[12:0] + disp;\n\n  // For an ADD/ADDI/AUIPC producer the page needs the carry from A+B.\n  // Compress A+B+disp independently so its low sum doesn't wait for A+B.\n  /* verilator lint_off UNUSEDSIGNAL */\n  logic [31:0] add_base;\n  /* verilator lint_on UNUSEDSIGNAL */\n  logic [12:0] ab_xor, carry, add_sum;\n\n  assign ab_xor   = ex_a[12:0] ^ ex_b[12:0];\n  assign carry    = ((ex_a[12:0] & ex_b[12:0]) | (ab_xor & disp)) << 1;\n  assign add_sum  = (ab_xor ^ disp) + carry;\n\n  logic [12:0] low_sum;\n  assign low_sum = ({13{use_rf}}  & rf_sum)\n                 | ({13{use_mem}} & mem_sum)\n                 | ({13{use_add}} & add_sum)\n                 | ({13{use_lui}} & (ex_b[12:0] + disp))\n                 | ({13{use_lw}}  & lw