lay annulment to the controls that authorize an operation.\\nA rejected entry can still select ALU inputs and compute a discarded\\nresult while its invalid bit and cleared enables suppress every effect.\\nThis takes the full-PC replay check off the arithmetic operand selects.\\n\\nA scratch implementation ran ten iterations in 3,234,996 bracketed cycles\\nwith both stall generators, the five expec\n…[4652 of 7724 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:5f8fe09b104dd3e2]…\n.328\n  ],\n  \"perturbations\": [\n    [\n      0,\n      75.641,\n      15\n    ],\n    [\n      1,\n      85.328,\n      13\n    ],\n    [\n      2,\n      85.328,\n      13\n    ]\n  ],\n  \"lutram\": 96,\n  \"bsram\": 6,\n  \"dsp\": 5,\n  \"critical_path\": {\n    \"from\": \"cpu/u_fwd/older_rs1_q_s0\",\n    \"to\": \"cpu/u_ex/reg_q.alu_result_23_s0\",\n    \"slack_ns\": -8.22,\n    \"arrival_ns\": 18.515,\n    \"logic_cells\": 31,\n    \"modules\": [\n      \"clock_ibuf\",\n      \"cpu/u_ex\",\n      \"cpu/u_id\",\n      \"cpu/u_ex\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"logic_levels\": 15,\n  \"formal_passed\": true,\n  \"cosim_passed\": true,\n  \"error\": null,\n  \"implementation_notes\": \"\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-20T09:28:28.870941Z\",\n  \"slot\": 1,\n  \"round_id\": 9,\n  \"lesson\": \"- 2026-11-20 hyp-20261120-002-r9s1 (improvement, +5.25%): Registering a distributed-RAM copy of replay `rs1` bypassed BSRAM delay on the path from `rs1` to the address adder, and annulling only validity and operation enables kept the replay PC check off the EX operand muxes, raising median Fmax from 81.075 to 85.328 MHz.\"\n}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
