{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_74", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"cat > cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261120-002-r10s1.yaml <<'YAML'\nid: hyp-20261120-002-r10s1\ntitle: Resolve operand sources in parallel for live and replayed instructions\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  Ten iterations take 3,234,996 cycles on the champion. Gowin's placement\n  0 path starts at older_rs1_q and ends at EX/MEM. On placement 1 both\n  WB-to-branch-PC and bypass-select-to-ALU-result paths approach the\n  85.328 MHz limit. The data-address generator also waits for the live\n  versus replay instruction choice before reading rs1 and adding the offset.\nhypothesis: |\n  Retime operand selection across ID/EX. Form the final youngest,\n  older and local grants for each source while its instruction is in ID.\n  For the ALU, group the two forwarded values on one arm of a mux and\n  the local register value and PC or immediate on the other. Capture the\n  grants alongside the consumer. This keeps the branch-selected PC out\n  of the D input of a combined local operand register.\n\n  A scratch implementation of that routing reached 85.574 MHz on\n  placement 1. The worst path then ran from imem_ready through the rs1\n  read and address adder to a data-address register. Apply the same\n  late selection to the ID address operand. Use the live rs1 tag and the\n  registered replay rs1 tag as independent asynchronous RF read addresses.\n  Form each RF-based address candidate with its own instruction's displacement.\n  Select the completed candidates with imem_ready. A denied fetch still\n  needs the existing full-PC verification before any memory side effect.\n  The two reads allow both additions to begin before bus ownership is known.\n\n  The additional RF read port costs distributed RAM and the extra\n  displacement adder costs carry cells. At the existing cycle count,\n  acceptance requires a median above 89.25 MHz. The remaining gain\n  depends on the placement of these read ports and the parallel adders.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 6\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Expose the registered replay rs1 from early_q and the replay word's\n      I/S displacement bits beside the normal selected instruction.\n      Use the existing coherent row read and stall enable for both.\n  - file: rtl/reg_file.sv\n    description: |\n      Add an asynchronous base-register read for each instruction source.\n      Share the architectural write port, x0 behavior and written bits.\n      Compute WB tag matches independently of the array data. The new\n      ports can expose raw data and separate array, bypass and zero grants.\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Form the low 13-bit sum and high page independently for the live\n      and replay RF sources, including same-edge WB writes. An unwritten\n      register or x0 contributes zero and its sum equals the displacement.\n      Select the candidates late on imem_ready. Preserve younger EX and\n      MEM base priority, page-cross detection, repair and address hold.\n      Export the decoded AUIPC and immediate-operand modes for ALU grants.\n  - file: rtl/forward_unit.sv\n    description: |\n      On consumer advance, register separate grants for raw rs1 and rs2\n      and for the ALU's forwarded, register and PC/immediate sources. A\n      younger tag match wins only if the executing producer will forward\n      after its trap checks. A suppressed writer leaves an older match\n      eligible. Hold the grants with their instruction.\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Supply trap-checked younger eligibility to ID. For each ALU input\n      use a two-level mux. The forwarded arm selects EX/MEM or WB and\n      the local arm selects raw ID/EX data or PC/immediate. Raw operands\n      retain their own grants for branches, stores, M operands and RVFI.\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: |\n      Connect both instruction-source tags and displacements to the RF\n      and address-generation logic. Wire the ALU grants, decoded modes\n      and executing producer eligibility across the existing boundary.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: |\n      Alternate live and replayed loads with different base tags and\n      displacements, including a WB collision on just one port and a\n      rejected replay carrying a store. Check accepted addresses and\n      data across repeated denials, retirement order and raw operands.\nYAML\npython - <<'PY'\nimport json,yaml,jsonschema\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261120-002-r10s1.yaml')\nd=yaml.safe_load(p.read_text());jsonschema.validate(d,json.load(open('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json')))\nassert d['id']==p.stem and d['category']=='structural'\nprint('Validated',p.name)\nPY\ndate -u\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
