{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_13", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nrows=[json.loads(l) for l in open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl')]\nfor n in [16,17,25,26,27,28,29]:\n r=rows[n]\n print(r['id'],r['cycles'],r['seeds'],r['perturbations'],r['implementation_notes'])\n print('HYP:',r['hypothesis'])\n print('PATH:',r['critical_path'])\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "hyp-20261120-001-r6s0 3320238 [65.108, 65.941, 65.941] [[0, 65.108, 18], [1, 65.941, 19], [2, 65.941, 19]] \nHYP: {'motivation': 'The champion takes 3,486,909 cycles for ten CoreMark iterations. A\\nload-use interlock discards a dependent successor even when replay\\nsupplies its instruction during a fetch stall. The previous trace\\ncounted 135,320 loads immediately followed by a branch with a matching\\nsource. On the pre-replay core, early address generation saved 203,487\\ncycles and moved the reported worst path away from the data RAM. That\\ndesign also routed EX arithmetic operands back to the decode-stage\\naddress adder. Restricting this bypass to LUI and LW trades a bubble\\non some address dependencies for a shorter clock period.\\n', 'hypothesis': \"Compute the full byte address as a load or store enters ID/EX and drive\\ndmem directly from that register during EX. Capture the formatted load\\ninto EX/MEM on acceptance. An immediately dependent branch can then\\nresolve from a registered operand and issue its successor in one cycle.\\n\\nGive the decode-stage address adder two candidate bases. The ordinary\\ncandidate selects the youngest available EX/MEM result or the write-first\\nregister file. If the immediately preceding EX instruction produces the\\nbase, bypass only a LUI immediate or the raw word of an aligned LW.\\nCalculate each candidate plus the sign-extended displacement in parallel.\\nRetry consumers of other pending bases when their producer advances. This\\nkeeps the arithmetic operands of the preceding EX instruction off the\\npath to the address register. In particular, an ADD followed by a load\\nusing its result as the base costs one bubble.\\n\\nA replayed instruction may have entered ID/EX provisionally. Qualify\\nevery early request and data wait with the resident slot's verified\\ncontrols and alignment. A rejected prediction must retry the resolved\\nPC without issuing a store, reading MMIO or blocking EX on dmemReady.\\nKeep address, store data and replay verification aligned across waits.\\n\\nA scratch pr\n…[26060 of 29132 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:9bcb7c4476ae23cd]…\n': 'Supply trap-checked younger eligibility to ID. For each ALU input\\nuse a two-level mux. The forwarded arm selects EX/MEM or WB and\\nthe local arm selects raw ID/EX data or PC/immediate. Raw operands\\nretain their own grants for branches, stores, M operands and RVFI.\\n'}, {'file': 'rtl/core.sv', 'description': 'Connect both instruction-source tags and displacements to the RF\\nand address-generation logic. Wire the ALU grants, decoded modes\\nand executing producer eligibility across the existing boundary.\\n'}, {'file': 'test/test_pipeline.py', 'description': 'Alternate live and replayed loads with different base tags and\\ndisplacements, including a WB collision on just one port and a\\nrejected replay carrying a store. Check accepted addresses and\\ndata across repeated denials, retirement order and raw operands.\\n'}]}\nPATH: {'from': 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu/triple_q_0_s0', 'to': 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu/quotient_q_1_s1', 'slack_ns': -6.934, 'arrival_ns': 17.228, 'logic_cells': 43, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu']}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
