{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_29", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,200p' formal/wrapper_si.sv; sed -n '100,225p' test/cosim/main.cpp\"", "aggregated_output": "// riscv-formal wrapper for single-issue (`nret 1`) cores. Same shape and\n// memory model as wrapper.sv, but instantiates `core` with only the\n// channel-0 RVFI port set — no `_1` ports. The single-issue path produces\n// only ch0 checks; checks_si.cfg sets `nret 1` so genchecks does not\n// emit any `_ch1` tasks (no PREUNSAT-as-pass tally needed). Selected by\n// the orchestrator when cores/<target>/core.yaml declares nret: 1.\n`include \"rvfi_macros.vh\"\n\nmodule rvfi_wrapper (\n    input clock,\n    input reset,\n    `RVFI_OUTPUTS\n);\n    // Solver picks any 32-bit instruction each cycle.\n    (* keep *) `rvformal_rand_reg [31:0] imem_data;\n\n    // 8 KiB dmem (2048 words).\n    reg [31:0] dmem [0:2047];\n\n    wire [31:0] imem_addr;\n    wire [31:0] dmem_addr;\n    wire [31:0] dmem_wdata;\n    wire [3:0]  dmem_wen;\n    wire        dmem_ren;\n\n    always @(posedge clock) begin\n        if (dmem_wen[0]) dmem[dmem_addr[12:2]][7:0]   <= dmem_wdata[7:0];\n        if (dmem_wen[1]) dmem[dmem_addr[12:2]][15:8]  <= dmem_wdata[15:8];\n        if (dmem_wen[2]) dmem[dmem_addr[12:2]][23:16] <= dmem_wdata[23:16];\n        if (dmem_wen[3]) dmem[dmem_addr[12:2]][31:24] <= dmem_wdata[31:24];\n    end\n\n    core uut (\n        .clock              (clock),\n        .reset              (reset),\n        .io_imemAddr        (imem_addr),\n        .io_imemData        (imem_data),\n        .io_imemReady       (1'b1),\n        .io_dmemAddr        (dmem_addr),\n        .io_dmemWData       (dmem_wdata),\n        .io_dmemRData       (dmem[dmem_addr[12:2]]),\n        .io_dmemWEn         (dmem_wen),\n        .io_dmemREn         (dmem_ren),\n        .io_dmemReady       (1'b1),\n        // Channel 0 — the only retirement channel. With nret=1 in\n        // checks_si.cfg, every rvfi_* signal here is sized for a single\n        // channel, so the core's `_0` ports connect directly without\n        // slicing. No `_1` ports exist on the core's IO under nret=1.\n        .io_rvfi_valid_0    (rvfi_valid),\n        .io_rvfi_order_0    (rvfi_order),\n        .io_rvfi_insn_0     (rvfi_insn),\n\n…[6363 of 9435 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:4b913ee6a30549df]…\n             \"\\\"mem_wmask\\\":%u,\\\"mem_wdata\\\":%u,\"\n                \"\\\"trap\\\":%u,\\\"halt\\\":%u,\\\"intr\\\":%u,\\\"mode\\\":%u,\\\"ixl\\\":%u}\",\n                (unsigned long long)order,\n                (unsigned long long)cycle,\n                insn, pc_rdata, pc_wdata,\n                rd_addr, rd_wdata,\n                rs1_addr, rs1_rdata,\n                rs2_addr, rs2_rdata,\n                mem_addr, mem_rmask, mem_rdata,\n                mem_wmask, mem_wdata,\n                (unsigned)trap, (unsigned)halt, (unsigned)intr,\n                (unsigned)mode, (unsigned)ixl);\n            if (bench_mode) {\n                strncpy(bench_last, buf, sizeof(bench_last)-1);\n                if (insn == 0x00100073) { hit_ebreak = true; return true; }\n            } else {\n                puts(buf);\n                fflush(stdout);\n                if (insn == 0x00100073) { hit_ebreak = true; return true; }\n            }\n            return false;\n        };\n\n        if (emit(top->io_rvfi_valid_0, top->io_rvfi_order_0, top->io_rvfi_insn_0,\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_30","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nrows=[json.loads(l) for l in open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl')]\nfor r in rows:\n if r['id'].endswith('r7s2'):\n  print(r['hypothesis']['motivation'],r['hypothesis']['hypothesis'],r['seeds'])\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_30","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nrows=[json.loads(l) for l in open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl')]\nfor r in rows:\n if r['id'].endswith('r7s2'):\n  print(r['hypothesis']['motivation'],r['hypothesis']['hypothesis'],r['seeds'])\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"A ready instruction already issues across a taken branch, and the successor\npredictor covers many denied instruction reads. The champion takes 3,234,996\ncycles with both stall generators. With data memory always ready, the same\npipeline takes 3,043,747 cycles. A load's predicted effective address is\nalready available in ID, one edge before EX needs the data.\n Use the low word index of the ID address prediction to read a synchronous\non-chip table before EX has verified the address. Each row holds the most\nrecent RAM word observed at that index, its upper address tag, and the byte\nlanes known to be current. In EX, a live ready response still supplies the\nload. On a denied read, a matching tag and complete coverage of the requested\nlanes let that load advance and forward the predicted data from EX/MEM.\nStores train the table when the data bus accepts them. An SB or SH replaces\nthe row's mask with just the lanes written. This prevents stale neighboring\nbytes from satisfying a wider load.\n\nA 512-row prototype took 3,102,126 bracketed cycles, with all five CRCs and\nthe validation banner correct. That saves 132,870 cycles over ten iterations.\nAt that cycle count a median above 65.67 MHz would clear the tournament's\n4.6 percent margin. Gowin placement option 1 reached 65.226 MHz, equivalent\nto 210.26 iterations/s or a 3.90 percent gain. The pipeline tests passed.\n [63.704, 66.28, 66.28]\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_31","type":"agent_message","text":"I tested moving older bypasses into decode. The prototype reached 77.112 MHz and added about 111,000 CoreMark cycles, so I’m testing a different pipeline split that keeps dependent instructions issuing at the champion’s rate."}}
