{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_14", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor l in open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'):\n d=json.loads(l)\n if d['id'].endswith(('r13s2','r11s2','r7s2','r12s2','r13s0')):\n  print(d['id'],d['hypothesis']['hypothesis'][:3350])\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "hyp-20261120-003-r7s2 Use the low word index of the ID address prediction to read a synchronous\non-chip table before EX has verified the address. Each row holds the most\nrecent RAM word observed at that index, its upper address tag, and the byte\nlanes known to be current. In EX, a live ready response still supplies the\nload. On a denied read, a matching tag and complete coverage of the requested\nlanes let that load advance and forward the predicted data from EX/MEM.\nStores train the table when the data bus accepts them. An SB or SH replaces\nthe row's mask with just the lanes written. This prevents stale neighboring\nbytes from satisfying a wider load.\n\nA 512-row prototype took 3,102,126 bracketed cycles, with all five CRCs and\nthe validation banner correct. That saves 132,870 cycles over ten iterations.\nAt that cycle count a median above 65.67 MHz would clear the tournament's\n4.6 percent margin. Gowin placement option 1 reached 65.226 MHz, equivalent\nto 210.26 iterations/s or a 3.90 percent gain. The pipeline tests passed.\n\nhyp-20261120-003-r11s2 Split a 32-bit integer sum at bit 16. Compute the low result and exact carry\nwith a 17-bit adder. Start the upper adder independently using a predicted\ncarry from bits 15 through 12 of the two operands. For subtraction complement\nB and use a low carry-in of one. If those four bits all propagate, use the\neffective B sign as the carry guess. This costs one short carry chain before\nthe upper sum and handles common additions of small signed displacements.\nUse the same predicted sum for the integer EX result and the ADD-produced\nbase page that ID needs for an immediately dependent load or store.\n\nVerify the carry before the producer transfers. On a mismatch hold the\nproducer, its forwarding sources and its successor for one clock, save the\nexact boundary carry, then use it for the high sum on the retry. Qualify the\ninterlock with a valid, effectful arithmetic operation so annulled slots and\nirrelevant default ALU_ADD decodes cannot hold the pipeline. The check only\ncompares on\n…[4195 of 7267 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:a9fa09a49fa6f425]…\nr can execute on\nthat cycle. Only a dependent address that missed the EX LW base\nbypass needs the existing address-repair cycle. On a tag or lane miss,\nfreeze the younger slot and both forwarding sources. Give the older\nload the external bus until its refill is accepted, capture the word\nin its resident slot, then release it through the normal bypass.\nAuthorize younger bus strobes, redirects, divider launch and pipeline\ntransfer only after the older result is verified. A refused candidate\nmust never drive a speculative JALR fetch address onto imem.\n\nThe experiment succeeds if the saved denial cycles offset MEM\nverification and refill costs. At 3.10 million bracketed cycles,\nacceptance requires more than 85.53 MHz across the median placement.\nAt 86.5 MHz that cycle count would yield 279.0 iterations/s. Measure\ndenied-load probes, verified hits, refill holds and immediate address\nrepairs alongside the three-placement median. The main timing risk\nis the path from replay RAM through a dependent branch to fetch.\n\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
