{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_9", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor d in map(json.loads,open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl')):\n if d['id'].endswith(('r9s2','r10s1','r10s2','r11s0','r14s1','r13s1')):\n  print(d['id'],d['hypothesis'],d['changes'])\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "hyp-20261120-003-r9s2 {'motivation': 'The champion takes 3,234,996 cycles for ten CoreMark iterations. Its\\nreported worst path starts at the successor instruction RAM, crosses\\nhazard and decode logic, and ends at data memory. The RAM already\\ncovers taken backedges during instruction-bus stalls. Reading it one\\ninstruction earlier would give its output a dedicated register before\\nthe instruction drives register selection, interlocks and address generation.\\n', 'hypothesis': \"Train each of the 512 predictor rows on a pair of successive control-flow\\ntransitions. For the executed sequence B, C, D, row B learns the full\\ndestination word PC and instruction of D from a ready bus fetch. While A\\nexecutes, use the existing short lookahead index for its likely successor B\\nto launch that row's synchronous read. While B executes, copy the complete\\nreturned row into a replay register. While C executes, that register can\\nsupply D on a denied fetch. A ready fetch always supplies the live word.\\nThis adds a clock boundary between the RAM read and the ID address logic\\nwhile retaining one issue per cycle on a warm stable path.\\n\\nPair the training key with consecutive admitted instructions. Invalidate\\nbroken chains across bubbles, retries or annuls. Freeze the read and replay\\npipeline together across EX holds. Carry row validity and read/write\\ncollision handling through the extra register. On a denied fetch keep the\\nexisting full-PC checks against fall-through and aligned redirect target.\\nA mismatch cancels every EX side effect and retries the resolved PC. Flush\\npending reads and training on reset or FENCE.I. The tradeoff is reduced\\nreplay coverage after unpredictable branches. With a 1% cycle penalty the\\nmedian must exceed 85.66 MHz to clear the 4.6% acceptance margin.\\n\", 'expected_impact': {'fitness_delta_pct': 6, 'confidence': 'medium'}, 'changes': [{'file': 'rtl/if_stage.sv', 'description': 'Delay the training predecessor by one advancing instruction. Read its\\ntwo-successor prediction through a synchronous \n…[28547 of 31619 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:815db66c31df7eaa]…\n, {'file': 'rtl/hazard_unit.sv', 'description': 'Interlock a dependent late integer result. Give an older correction priority over younger data holds and division, and retain precise forwarding through a denied request.'}, {'file': 'rtl/if_stage.sv', 'description': 'Use the saved successor PC for a deferred control transfer, qualify the fetched word and recover from the registered correction. Train only verified successor words and retain the predecessor across recovery.'}, {'file': 'rtl/core.sv', 'description': 'Wire the early and late execution times into one in-order stream. Qualify every younger effect with older validation. Preserve the single retirement channel, exact RVFI operand data and consecutive order.'}, {'file': 'test/test_pipeline.py', 'description': 'Exercise a load feeding a branch that changes direction, back-to-back late branches, and a forwarded JALR with a misaligned target. Check every retirement and accepted store while both buses stall and a wrong-path store or divider occupies EX.'}]\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
