{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_72","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor d in map(json.loads,open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl')):\n if d['id'].endswith('r11s2'):print(d['hypothesis']['hypothesis'])\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_72","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor d in map(json.loads,open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl')):\n if d['id'].endswith('r11s2'):print(d['hypothesis']['hypothesis'])\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"Split a 32-bit integer sum at bit 16. Compute the low result and exact carry\nwith a 17-bit adder. Start the upper adder independently using a predicted\ncarry from bits 15 through 12 of the two operands. For subtraction complement\nB and use a low carry-in of one. If those four bits all propagate, use the\neffective B sign as the carry guess. This costs one short carry chain before\nthe upper sum and handles common additions of small signed displacements.\nUse the same predicted sum for the integer EX result and the ADD-produced\nbase page that ID needs for an immediately dependent load or store.\n\nVerify the carry before the producer transfers. On a mismatch hold the\nproducer, its forwarding sources and its successor for one clock, save the\nexact boundary carry, then use it for the high sum on the retry. Qualify the\ninterlock with a valid, effectful arithmetic operation so annulled slots and\nirrelevant default ALU_ADD decodes cannot hold the pipeline. The check only\ncompares one bit and can run alongside upper-result generation. A key risk is\nmoving the limiting path to carry verification and the pipeline enables.\nMeasure repair cycles and bracketed cycles as well as the three-placement\nmedian. At a 0.5% cycle cost acceptance requires about 89.70 MHz.\n\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
