{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_5", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg -n 'structural' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl | cut -c 1-1600\"", "aggregated_output": "3:{\"id\": \"hyp-20261120-002-r1s1\", \"title\": \"Move DIV and REM off the single-cycle execute path\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The baseline retires ten CoreMark iterations in 4,491,485 cycles at a median\\n5.442 MHz. Gowin reports a 199.837 ns path through forwarding and the EX ALU.\\nThe ALU selects full-width combinational quotient and remainder results onto\\nthe same bus that feeds the data address. These operators are the strongest\\ncandidate for the reported depth of 156 cells. The RV32IM reference\\ninterpreter ran 2,922,015 instructions between the canonical -O3 binary's\\nMMIO markers, including 93,960 MULs and zero DIV, DIVU, REM or REMU\\ninstructions. The run produced all five expected CRCs.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The baseline retires ten CoreMark iterations in 4,491,485 cycles at a median\\n5.442 MHz. Gowin reports a 199.837 ns path through forwarding and the EX ALU.\\nThe ALU selects full-width combinational quotient and remainder results onto\\nthe same bus that feeds the data address. These operators are the strongest\\ncandidate for the reported depth of 156 cells. The RV32IM reference\\ninterpreter ran 2,922,015 instructions between the canonical -O3 binary's\\nMMIO markers, including 93,960 MULs and zero DIV, DIVU, REM or REMU\\ninstructions. The run produced all five expected CRCs.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Give EX one shared, fixed-latency restoring divider. At issue, register the\\nmagnitudes of the forwarded operands and the signs needed for the result.\\nProcess six quotient bits per clock for six clocks using a 36-bit dividend\\npadded with four lead\n6:{\"id\": \"hyp-20261120-002-r2s1\", \"title\": \"Resolve six quotient bits with two radix-8 divider stages\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The champion's worst Gowin path runs from divisor_q to remainder_q through\\nsix dependent trial subtractions. Eight trials per clock reached 31.094 MHz\\nand six reached 41.649 MHz. CoreMark executed zero DIV or REM instructions\\nin its 4,491,485 bracketed cycles, so the divider limits the clock even\\n\n…[1731 of 4803 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:1e6601070fcd9260]…\n38 MHz Gowin placements were multiplier-limited.\\nEX currently puts register forwarding, multiplication and result selection\\nin one cycle. EX/MEM already captures both forwarded source values, and\\na multiply leaves the data bus idle in MEM. In the reference trace, only\\n35,640 of 93,960 multiplies had an immediate consumer between the markers.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Move the four RV32M products into MEM. Feed one signed 33-by-33 multiplier\\nfrom the EX/MEM operands, extending each input by one sign or zero bit\\naccording to the instruction. Register bits 31:0 for MUL or 63:32 for\\na high-half operation in the existing MEM/WB ALU-result field. The EX/MEM\\nboundary then separates the forwarding muxes from the DSP. Independent\\ninstructions, including multiplies, can still issue on successive cycles.\\nGive loads and multiplies one late-result interlock. Compare the fetched\\nrs fields directly with the producer rd in parallel with EX branch\\nresolution. An adjacent consumer takes one bubble and receives the result\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
