{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_112", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"cat > cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261120-002-r5s1.yaml <<'PROPOSAL'\nid: hyp-20261120-002-r5s1\ntitle: Issue fall-through instructions from a replay window during fetch stalls\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  The champion resolves a branch in time to issue its target on a ready\n  bus, yet an unavailable fetch still bubbles ID/EX even when the core\n  just executed the same loop body. The prior one-entry fetch buffer\n  saved 119,419 cycles and reached 153.03 iterations/s. Reusing a longer\n  sequence offers more opportunities to keep the execution pipeline busy.\nhypothesis: |\n  Give decode two instruction sources. On a ready fetch, issue the live\n  word. On a denied fetch, issue a previously executed fall-through word\n  from a 128-word replay window when EX proves that it is the successor.\n  Capture each valid resident EX instruction in a single aligned 512-byte\n  region. Store word i in slot (i-1) modulo 128, so the registered EX PC\n  indexes its potential successor directly, in parallel with branch\n  resolution. A region change starts a fresh validity bitmap. A fence\n  clears it and requires a fresh fetch of its successor.\n\n  Accept a replay when the region tag matches, the slot is valid, the\n  successor stays inside the region and EX resolves to fall-through.\n  Latch that decision and slot alongside the existing retry PC across\n  ID/EX bubbles. Select the instruction data with imemReady. Use the hit\n  to qualify a single ID/EX valid bit so a late branch decision does\n  not fan out to the decode payload. Qualify redirects, interlocks and\n  all architectural side effects with validity. Taken branches and jumps\n  retain the champion's same-cycle bus fetch of the resolved target.\n\n  A scratch prototype completed ten iterations in 3,726,811 bracketed\n  cycles versus 4,171,092 for the champion, with both bus stalls enabled.\n  All five CRCs and the validation banner matched, and the self-test and\n  three randomized RVFI traces matched the reference under stalls.\n  Gowin placement options 0, 1 and 2 reached 56.054, 61.839 and 61.839\n  MHz. The measured median gives 165.93 iterations/s, an 8.08 percent\n  gain over 153.52.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 8\n  confidence: high\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Track one PC[31:9] region, a 128-bit valid mask and 128 instruction\n      words. When EX is valid, write ex_instr to slot ex_pc[8:2]-1 modulo\n      128. On region replacement keep only the new word valid. Give reset\n      and FENCE/FENCE.I invalidation priority. For a valid EX instruction\n      read at ex_pc[8:2]. Qualify the hit with tag equality, the slot's\n      valid bit, index \"'!= 127, no redirect and no fence. Save that index\n      and hit when EX is valid for use with retry_pc when EX is empty.\n      Feed decode the live word when ready and the replay word otherwise,\n      with fetch_valid = imem_ready || hit.\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      On each unheld edge capture the selected instruction, its PC,\n      decoded controls and register operands. Reset the ID/EX valid bit\n      and clear it on a flush. A data stall or divider wait retains the\n      resident instruction. Keep replay qualification off payload reset\n      and enable paths.\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Gate redirect with in.valid and qualify the EX/MEM register-write,\n      memory-read and memory-write controls with in.valid. Preserve\n      misalignment trap suppression, divider issue qualification and the\n      existing EX/MEM hold priority.\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: |\n      Pass the resident ID/EX instruction to IF for replay capture and\n      fence detection. Qualify the hazard unit'\"'s late-result producer\n      input with id_ex_w.valid so a bubble cannot interlock a real word.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: |\n      Warm a short loop, deny fetch on its second trip and check the\n      fall-through instruction retires once. Deny a taken target and\n      check the target retries. Exercise an offset-127 region crossing,\n      two regions with equal low PC bits, and a replayed load dependent\n      on a stalled producer. After FENCE.I, change a previously fetched\n      word and require the new instruction. Check bus strobes and RVFI PCs,\n      data and order with a store encoding on denied fetches.\nPROPOSAL\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
