 or REMU\\ninstructions. The run produced all five expected CRCs.\\n\", 'hypothesis': 'Give EX one shared, fixed-latency restoring divider. At issue, register the\\nmagnitudes of the forwarded operands and the signs needed for the result.\\nProcess six quotient bits per clock for six clocks using a 36-bit dividend\\npadded with four leading zeros. Each bit uses the borrow from a trial\\nsubt\n…[24510 of 27582 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:7cacbb224045c295]…\nation, limited to aligned addresses in the low 1 MiB.\\nSuppress training during reset, FENCE.I and invalidation. After reset\\nor FENCE.I, clear one row's valid bit per cycle with the write port\\nwhile ordinary bus fetches can proceed. Exclude stale lookups until\\nthe sweep completes and suppress prediction on a read/write collision.\\n\\nCompute the next read index with nine-bit arithmetic. Use retry_pc\\nwhen EX is empty. Hold the RAM read output on a downstream EX hold.\\nUse imemReady to select live or predicted instruction bits. Require\\na valid EX predecessor and usable row for provisional decode. Compare\\nthe zero-extended, aligned saved destination with both full-width EX\\nsuccessors. Latch the comparisons, redirect and bus-denied bit beside\\nthe candidate, holding all four across stalls. Annul only a denied\\ncandidate that fails the selected comparison. Serialize FENCE.I by\\nbubbling its successor and refetching it from the bus.\\n\"}, {'file': 'rtl/core.sv', 'description': 'Wire the ID/EX displacement, di\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
