{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor l in open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'):\n e=json.loads(l)\n if e['id'].endswith('r5s0'):\n  print(e['motivation'],e['hypothesis']['hypothesis']);print(*e['changes'],sep='\\\\n');print(e['perturbations']);print(e['seeds'])\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_9", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor l in open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'):\n e=json.loads(l)\n if e['id'].endswith('r5s0'):\n  print(e['motivation'],e['hypothesis']['hypothesis']);print(*e['changes'],sep='\\\\n');print(e['perturbations']);print(e['seeds'])\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "The champion issues data requests in MEM, one cycle too late for a dependent\ninstruction to use a load through the EX/MEM bypass. An instruction trace\nof the ten timed iterations contains 544,852 loads. A branch immediately\nfollows 135,320 loads with a matching source field. Moving address generation\none stage earlier can remove that bubble and keep the FPGA RAM address\nregistered. The latter matters because the champion's reported option-zero\ncritical path crosses the shared EX ALU on its way to data memory.\n Compute the full byte address as a memory instruction enters ID/EX. Drive\nthe data bus from this register during EX. On acceptance, latch the raw\nread word for RVFI and the formatted load value in EX/MEM for ordinary EX\nforwarding. Stores use the forwarded rs2 in EX. A stalled request holds\nits address, data, enables and producer operands through the accepting edge.\n\nTo handle a newly produced base, compare the incoming rs1 against the\nyoungest writers. For ADD, ADDI and AUIPC in EX, their operands A and B\nare already available. With displacement D, compute P = A XOR B, then\n(P XOR D) + (((A AND B) OR (P AND D)) << 1) modulo 2^32. This gives\nA+B+D with one carry-propagate adder. Compute it in parallel with the normal\nbase-plus-displacement path. A preceding LUI supplies its immediate and an\naligned, accepted LW can supply the raw bus word. Use the EX/MEM value for\nolder available writers and the write-first register file otherwise.\nInterlock unavailable bases, including pending products. Suppress x0 and\ntrapped writes. Keep the multiply-use interlock for ordinary EX consumers.\n\nA scratch prototype completed ten iterations in 3,967,605 bracketed cycles\nversus 4,171,092 for the champion, with all canonical CRCs. Gowin placement\noptions 0, 1 and 2 reached 61.552, 66.658 and 66.658 MHz respectively.\nThe median gives 168.01 iterations/s, 9.44% above the champion. The\nprototype passed all 53 standard single-channel formal checks. The selftest\nand three random programs matched the reference with and without bus stalls.\n\n{'file': 'rtl/core_pkg.sv', 'description': 'Carry the effective address in ID/EX, then carry the serviced address and raw load word in EX/MEM alongside the forwarded result.'}\n{'file': 'rtl/id_stage.sv', 'description': 'Select the youngest available base and register the address on issue. Compute the ordinary, LW/LUI-bypassed and carry-save three-input candidate addresses in parallel with the producer checks.'}\n{'file': 'rtl/ex_stage.sv', 'description': 'Drive the registered address, alignment-qualified enables and replicated store data in EX. On transfer, capture the raw read word, effective address and extended load result. Expose the forwarded arithmetic operands for address generation.'}\n{'file': 'rtl/core.sv', 'description': 'Connect the EX bus, classify eligible base producers, permit EX/MEM load forwarding and derive dmem backpressure from the resident ID/EX memory operation.'}\n{'file': 'rtl/hazard_unit.sv', 'description': 'Interlock address bases that cannot yet be bypassed and retain the multiply-use check. Hold the resident request and forwarding state on data waits, including simultaneous instruction waits.'}\n{'file': 'rtl/mem_stage.sv', 'description': 'Format the captured raw word and byte address into the existing MEM/WB read_data path for register writeback, alongside the earlier EX/MEM copy used for bypass. Use the captured access for aligned RVFI masks, memory data and traps. Preserve the MEM multiplier.'}\n{'file': 'test/test_pipeline.py', 'description': 'Assert back-to-back load-to-branch and LW-to-address timing. Check dependent ADDI addresses with carries, stale-base interlocks, misaligned requests and a stalled store accepted exactly once. Adjust stage-specific cycle expectations while retaining architectural checks.'}\n[[0, 63.004, 18], [1, 66.836, 18], [2, 66.836, 18]]\n[63.004, 66.836, 66.836]\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
