{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_78", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"git status --short --untracked-files=all && cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261120-002-r6s1.yaml && rg -n 'fitness_delta_pct' tools | head -20\"", "aggregated_output": "id: hyp-20261120-002-r6s1\ntitle: \"Move data access into EX with a separate registered load bypass\"\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  Successor replay brings ten CoreMark iterations down to 3,486,909 cycles,\n  but a replay hit immediately behind a load still encounters the MEM-stage\n  load-use interlock. The reference trace has 544,852 loads, including\n  135,320 immediately followed by a branch with a matching source field.\n  On the pre-replay core, advancing data access to EX saved 203,487 cycles\n  and reached 66.836 MHz. The replay champion's reported option-zero path\n  also runs from the register file through the EX ALU to data memory.\nhypothesis: |\n  Generate the effective address while a live or replayed memory instruction\n  enters ID/EX. Drive the data port from that register in EX. At the\n  accepting edge, clock the extended load value and the integer ALU result\n  into separate EX/MEM fields. Select between the registered values at\n  the bypass source. This takes the load mux off the ALU register input\n  and lets the next instruction consume a load, including a branch issued\n  from replay. Only the admitted EX slot owns the data port. A replay\n  address mismatch must squash both bus strobes before the edge.\n\n  Bypass available base producers into address generation. For an immediately\n  preceding ADD, ADDI or AUIPC, fold its two operands and the displacement\n  with a carry-save compressor and one final adder. An accepted aligned LW\n  can supply a pointer directly from the bus. Retry an instruction whose\n  youngest base producer is unavailable. Preserve a single registered\n  byte address on dmem across backpressure.\n\n  A scratch prototype completed ten iterations in 3,235,202 bracketed\n  cycles, saving 251,707 cycles against the champion with both stall\n  generators enabled. It passed the canonical CRC and UART checks.\n  The prototype that selected load data at the ALU register input reached\n  60.666 MHz median. Separate EX/MEM result registers reached 61.640,\n  64.712 and 64.712 MHz across Gowin placemen\n…[3413 of 6485 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:981111aad15280cd]…\nis.py:152:        \"expected_impact: {fitness_delta_pct: 5, confidence: medium}\\n\"\ntools/agents/test_hypothesis.py:210:        \"expected_impact: {fitness_delta_pct: 5, confidence: medium}\\n\"\ntools/agents/test_hypothesis.py:229:        \"expected_impact: {fitness_delta_pct: 5, confidence: medium}\\n\"\ntools/agents/test_hypothesis.py:241:    assert \"fitness_delta_pct\" in p\ntools/agents/random_agent.py:214:        \"  fitness_delta_pct: 0\\n\"\ntools/agents/static_agent.py:95:        \"  fitness_delta_pct: 0\\n\"\ntools/agents/hypothesis.py:351:  fitness_delta_pct: 5             # INTEGER (-50..+50). Schema rejects strings.\ntools/agents/hypothesis.py:362:- `expected_impact: \"free-text description\"` — schema requires an OBJECT with `fitness_delta_pct` (integer) and `confidence` (enum). Strings are rejected.\ntools/agents/hypothesis.py:363:- `expected_impact: {{fitness_delta_pct: 5.0, confidence: \"Med\"}}` — `fitness_delta_pct` must be a Python integer (not float, not \"5\"); `confidence` must be lowercase `low`/`medium`/`high`.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
