{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_42","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'tail -3 /srv/hwebench/tmp/3c491641/83938d59/divider-study.WpG0Gb/retimed/formal-proto.log && cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261120-002-r7s1.yaml && ls /srv/hwebench/tmp/3c491641/83938d59/divider-study.WpG0Gb/retimed/obj_dir/cosim_sim'","aggregated_output":"SBY  7:30:36 [causal_ch0] engine_0: Status returned by engine: pass\nSBY  7:30:36 [causal_ch0] summary: Elapsed clock time [H:MM:SS (secs)]: 0:00:17 (17)\nSBY  7:3id: hyp-20261120-002-r7s1\ntitle: Split the six-cycle divider by divisor magnitude\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  The champion's reported 75-cell Gowin path runs from triple_q to\n  remainder_q through two dependent full-width radix-8 digit selections.\n  The measured CoreMark region executes zero divides or remainders, yet\n  this path sets a clock limit for every instruction. At the champion's\n  3,234,996 cycles for ten iterations, acceptance requires a median clock\n  above 68.48 MHz. The current median is 65.467 MHz.\nhypothesis: |\n  Partition unsigned magnitude division at D = 2^17. For 0 < D < 2^17,\n  every restored remainder fits in 17 bits. Keep the two-bit prefix step\n  and five pairs of radix-8 digits, using 20-bit unsigned trials and\n  multiples in both digit selectors. For D >= 2^17, the top 17 bits of\n  the dividend A are already a legal remainder because A[31:15] < D.\n  Seed the wide remainder with those bits and process A[14:0] in five\n  single radix-8 steps. These steps produce the entire 15-bit quotient.\n  Each wide recurrence now crosses just one subtract/select stage. Keep\n  the narrow and wide feedback paths independent and select the result\n  from the completed registers using the mode captured for that request.\n\n  Both paths use one setup clock and five recurrence clocks after issue.\n  This preserves divider latency and predicts the same bracketed cycle\n  count. A median of 71 MHz would yield about 219.5 iterations/s. The\n  principal uncertainty is the delay of the next limiting path outside\n  the divider.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 8\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/alu.sv\n    description: |\n      Classify the registered divisor magnitude during setup. Register\n      the odd multiples alongside each lane's initial state. Use unsigned\n      20-bit trial differences with a separate borrow in the narrow lane\n      and 35-bit differences with a separate borrow in the wide lane.\n      Zero-extend the wide lane's quotient and the narrow lane's remainder\n      before sign correction. For D=0 return an all-ones quotient or the\n      original dividend. Preserve signed truncation, signed remainder and\n      INT_MIN / -1, the shared six-clock real and ALTOPS handshake, reset\n      cancellation and result stability until consume.\n  - file: test/test_alu.py\n    description: |\n      Extend the six-clock integer-reference tests across magnitudes\n      0x1ffff, 0x20000 and 0x20001. Exercise dividends at multiples of\n      each divisor and one to either side, 0xffffffff, and the largest\n      legal wide quotient 0x7fff. Alternate modes and signed operands\n      across consecutive requests, including zero divisors, and delay\n      consume to check the saved mode, sign and result.\n/srv/hwebench/tmp/3c491641/83938d59/divider-study.WpG0Gb/retimed/obj_dir/cosim_sim\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
