{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_8", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor l in open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'):\n d=json.loads(l)\n if d['round_id'] in [1,7] and d['slot'] in [0,1]:\n  print(d['id'],d['hypothesis'])\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "hyp-20261120-001-r1s0 {'motivation': \"The baseline's 199.837 ns path crosses operand forwarding and the EX ALU.\\nThe ALU computes signed and unsigned division and remainder combinationally.\\nA full-width divide is a plausible source of the 156-cell path. Its delay\\nlimits the clock even when executing other instructions. A reference-ISS run\\nof the canonical ten-iteration binary retired 2,922,015 instructions between\\nthe markers, including 93,960 multiplies and zero divides or remainders.\\n\", 'hypothesis': \"Replace the four DIV/REM operators with one unsigned restoring divider.\\nCapture the forwarded operand magnitudes on launch, then reuse eight\\nshift-and-trial-subtract steps over four clocks to produce the 32 quotient\\nbits and the remainder. Register the partial result after each pass. Apply\\nthe RV32M result sign at completion. Only DIV/REM occupy EX for extra clocks.\\nThe instruction count predicts zero divider stalls in the timed region.\\nAt the baseline's 4,491,485 bracketed cycles, 5.70 MHz would clear the 4.6%\\nacceptance threshold and 8.17 MHz would deliver the projected 50% gain.\\nCompare both the cycle count and median Gowin Fmax to test this prediction.\\n\", 'expected_impact': {'fitness_delta_pct': 50, 'confidence': 'medium'}, 'changes': [{'file': 'rtl/alu.sv', 'description': \"Add launch, completion and consume signals for DIV, DIVU, REM and REMU.\\nUse the trial subtraction's borrow to choose the next partial remainder\\nand quotient bit. Latch quotient/remainder selection and sign flags.\\nReturn all ones or the original dividend on division by zero, and INT_MIN\\nor zero on signed overflow, for quotient or remainder respectively.\\nUnder RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS capture the existing per-op formula at launch\\nand return it through the same four-pass control and completion handshake.\\nKeep the ordinary ALU and multiply results combinational.\\n\"}, {'file': 'rtl/ex_stage.sv', 'description': 'Launch once for a valid divide when an older MEM request can advance.\\nCapture both original forwarded operands for RVFI\n…[14144 of 17216 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:cec5c624c3087e5d]…\nerve signed truncation,\\nsigned remainder and INT_MIN / -1. Use the existing six-clock handshake\\nfor both real arithmetic and ALTOPS, including reset cancellation and\\nresult stability until consume.\\n\"}, {'file': 'test/test_alu.py', 'description': 'Extend the six-clock integer-reference tests across magnitudes\\n0x1ffff, 0x20000 and 0x20001. Exercise dividends at multiples of\\neach divisor and one to either side, 0xffffffff, and the largest\\nlegal wide quotient 0x7fff. Alternate modes and signed operands\\nacross consecutive requests, including zero divisors, and delay\\nconsume to check the saved mode, sign and result.\\n'}, {'file': 'test/test_pipeline.py', 'description': 'Issue an ADDI writing x1, a misaligned LW targeting x1, and\\nan immediate consumer of x1. Check that the load traps with zero bus\\nreads and the consumer gets the ADDI value from WB. Exercise a live\\nyounger writer to the same register as the priority counterpart.\\nVerify channel-0 operands, results and consecutive retirement orders.\\n'}]}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
