{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_48","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor l in open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'):\n d=json.loads(l)\n if d['id'].endswith('r7s2'): print(d['hypothesis']['hypothesis']); print(d['hypothesis'].get('changes'))\nPY\ndate -u\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_48","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor l in open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'):\n d=json.loads(l)\n if d['id'].endswith('r7s2'): print(d['hypothesis']['hypothesis']); print(d['hypothesis'].get('changes'))\nPY\ndate -u\"","aggregated_output":"Use the low word index of the ID address prediction to read a synchronous\non-chip table before EX has verified the address. Each row holds the most\nrecent RAM word observed at that index, its upper address tag, and the byte\nlanes known to be current. In EX, a live ready response still supplies the\nload. On a denied read, a matching tag and complete coverage of the requested\nlanes let that load advance and forward the predicted data from EX/MEM.\nStores train the table when the data bus accepts them. An SB or SH replaces\nthe row's mask with just the lanes written. This prevents stale neighboring\nbytes from satisfying a wider load.\n\nA 512-row prototype took 3,102,126 bracketed cycles, with all five CRCs and\nthe validation banner correct. That saves 132,870 cycles over ten iterations.\nAt that cycle count a median above 65.67 MHz would clear the tournament's\n4.6 percent margin. Gowin placement option 1 reached 65.226 MHz, equivalent\nto 210.26 iterations/s or a 3.90 percent gain. The pipeline tests passed.\n\n[{'file': 'rtl/id_stage.sv', 'description': 'Drive the synchronous read with bits [10:2] of the selected candidate\\naddress. In the timed prototype each existing base source had a full-width\\nsum, including a carry-save A+B+displacement candidate for an ADD writer.\\nKeep the existing base-availability and page-cross checks. The index and\\nID/EX address must belong to the same incoming instruction.\\n'}, {'file': 'rtl/ex_stage.sv', 'description': 'Infer a simple dual-port block RAM for tag, byte mask and word. Train\\nonly on accepted accesses to ordinary RAM below 1 MiB. Store the whole\\nbus word on a read and the replicated write data and accepted strobes on\\na store. Clear validity on reset and reject read/write collisions.\\nMatch the verified word address and all requested lanes before releasing\\na denied aligned load. Keep the row aligned with EX across holds and\\nre-read at the corrected index on the repair edge. Store tag [19:11] and\\nreject any EX address with nonzero bits [31:20]. Format the live and\\npredicted words in parallel, registering the predicted result and its\\nselect bit beside EX/MEM. Use the selected raw word for RVFI.\\n'}, {'file': 'rtl/core.sv', 'description': 'Connect the speculative read index and distinguish a verified local read\\nfrom a pending external request. Keep annulled, misaligned and MMIO loads\\nout of replay. An EX word load used as the next address base must supply\\nthe selected word or take the existing unavailable-base repair.\\n'}, {'file': 'test/test_pipeline.py', 'description': 'Warm a replay row. Deny a dependent load while driving unrelated bus\\ndata and check its retirement, forwarding and RVFI byte mask. Exercise\\npartial stores followed by narrow and wide reads, equal-index aliases,\\nreset, collisions and a repaired address under sustained backpressure.\\n'}]\nFri Nov 20 07:20:29 UTC 2026\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_49","type":"agent_message","text":"The radix-16 prototype matched CoreMark’s CRCs, but it reached only 72.098 MHz and the liveness check found an eleven-clock retirement gap. I’m replacing it with a reciprocal-based divider that fits the champion’s six wait clocks, then testing that design against the same gates."}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_50","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cat > cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261120-002-r8s1.yaml <<'YAML'\nid: hyp-20261120-002-r8s1\ntitle: \\\"Pipeline division through a reciprocal table and an exact remainder correction\\\"\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  The champion's 74-cell critical path runs from quotient_q to remainder_q through two serial divider digit selections. CoreMark issues zero DIV/REM between the markers, so shortening this path can raise fitness on every measured instruction. An isolated radix-16 prototype reached 72.098 MHz and its extra wait clock failed bounded liveness when a FENCE.I bubble preceded a divide and a younger store needed address repair.\nhypothesis: |\n  Replace the divider recurrence with a fixed-point reciprocal pipeline. For a nonzero divisor magnitude D, left-normalize it to V = D << s in [2\"'^31, 2''^32). Split V into a 12-bit index i = V >> 20 and the 20-bit residual x. A synchronous 2048-row constant ROM indexed by i-2048 supplies C = floor(2''^42/i) and S = ceil(2''^34/i²). Compute R = C - ceil(x*S/4096), then q0 = floor(A*R / 2''^(62-s)) for dividend magnitude A. Multiplication and shifts have separate register boundaries. Register P = q0*D, then select q0+1 and A-D-P when P <= A-D and A >= D. Otherwise select q0 and A-P.\n  \n  The tangent estimate is a lower bound on 2''^62/V. Its curvature error is below 512 reciprocal units, slope quantization contributes less than 256 and the two integer roundings contribute less than two. For D >= 4096 the scale factor A/2''^(62-s) is below 1/2048, so q0 can be short by at most one. For smaller D the normalized residual is zero and the table intercept is exact to less than one reciprocal unit. D=1 has an exact intercept. Thus one correction suffices for every RV32 operand.\n  \n  Use issue for the operand magnitudes, then six wait edges for coarse normalization, fine normalization with ROM read, interpolation, the full quotient-estimate product, quotient extraction, and the correction product respectively. The consume edge registers the corrected magnitude, ready for sign correction in MEM. This keeps the existing dependent-divide retirement interval. At 3,234,996 bracketed cycles the median must exceed 76.79 MHz for acceptance. DSP mapping and the path from instruction replay RAM through decode to the registered memory address are the main timing risks.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 8\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/alu.sv\n    description: |\n      Replace the real DIV/REM digit banks with the six registered stages and share the current controller with ALTOPS. Generate the packed intercept and slope constants from the row index at elaboration with wide unsigned arithmetic. Store a 32-bit C and a 13-bit S. Use a full-width interpolation product and subtract before shifting to implement ceiling. Retain the quotient product bits through the variable shift. Compute A-D and its borrow early so both final remainder candidates can be subtracted in parallel. Handle D=0 from saved issue operands, signed truncation, remainder sign and INT_MIN/-1. The consume edge alone commits the final magnitude. Hold it for a stalled MEM slot.\n  - file: test/test_alu.py\n    description: |\n      Keep all integer-reference, six-wait, reset and delayed-consume checks. Check the completed result on the consume edge and stability on either side of it. Exercise exact and one-short quotient estimates, the 4095/4096 transition, powers of two, both ends of normalized table bins, kD-1/kD/kD+1 and signed counterparts. Check all four DIV/REM operations against integer arithmetic.\nYAML\npython - <<'\"'PY'\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261120-002-r8s1.yaml')\njsonschema.validate(yaml.safe_load(p.read_text()),json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
