{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_10", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor r in map(json.loads,open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl')):\n if r['id'].endswith(('r8s1','r6s2','r6s1','r5s2','r7s0')):\n  print(r['id'],r['critical_path'],r['hypothesis']['hypothesis'])\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "hyp-20261120-003-r5s2 {'from': 'cpu/u_rf/regs_regs_0_0_s0', 'to': 'dmem_1_dmem_1_0_0_s', 'slack_ns': -11.091, 'arrival_ns': 21.386, 'logic_cells': 20, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_id', 'cpu/u_ex', 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu', 'cpu/u_ex']} Train a 512-entry table indexed by predecessor PC. Each row predicts the\nsuccessor PC and its instruction from the last ready external fetch.\nRead one cycle ahead using the likely next predecessor's word index.\nDirect JAL and backward branches select the direct target index.\nOther instructions select fall-through. This guess drives only the\ninternal RAM read port. EX always drives the resolved address on imem.\n\nOn a ready fetch, decode the live response. On a denied fetch, a valid\nprediction can enter ID/EX provisionally. Compare the saved destination\nagainst PC+4 and the full EX redirect target in parallel. Register both\nequality bits and the actual redirect decision. In the next cycle the\nselected equality bit admits the instruction to EX. A mismatch annuls\nthat slot and IF retries the resolved address already in retry_pc.\nThis verifies the address for indirect jumps and table aliases as well.\nVerification costs no extra cycle on a hit or a ready bus response.\n\nA scratch prototype completed ten iterations in 3,486,909 bracketed\ncycles with both stall generators, a 16.40% cycle reduction. All five\nCRCs and the UART validation banner matched. Gowin placement options\n0, 1 and 2 reached 59.777, 61.398 and 61.398 MHz. The median yields\n176.08 iterations/s, 14.70% above 153.52. At this cycle count the\nacceptance threshold requires more than 55.9935 MHz. The predictor\nadded two BSRAMs. The prototype passed all 53 standard single-channel\nformal checks. With both buses stalled, the four small ELF traces\nmatched the reference. A directed test retired 24 consecutive loop\ninstructions while the instruction bus denied every fetch, including\nthe taken backedges.\n\nhyp-20261120-002-r6s1 {'from': 'cpu/u_if/successors_successors_0_0_s', 'to': 'dmem_0_dmem_0_0_0_s', 'slack_ns': -11.065, 'arrival_ns': 2\n…[7981 of 11053 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:2a39ef6830b7204a]…\nmost 32768 units and the scale is below 1/65536. For D < 4096 the residual is zero, C has less than one unit of error, and D=1 is exact. Thus q0 is either the exact quotient or one short. Register A-D with its borrow early. On consume select q0+1 and A-D-P if A >= D and P <= A-D, otherwise q0 and A-P. Sign-correct the registered final magnitude for MEM.\n\nAn isolated prototype using a thirteen-bit residual coefficient t = ceil(x/256) passed the real-arithmetic divider tests and completed ten CoreMark iterations in 3,234,996 bracketed cycles with the five canonical CRCs. Gowin placement options 0, 1 and 2 reached 74.365, 76.550 and 76.550 MHz. The median yields 236.63 iterations/s, a 4.28% improvement. Acceptance requires more than 237.36 iterations/s or about 76.79 MHz at this cycle count. The six-bit interpolation is an unmeasured refinement targeting 78 MHz through lower logic and routing demand. The prototype timing limit runs from the successor instruction RAM through decode into the data-memory address.\n\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
