xternal fetch.\nRead one cycle ahead using the likely next predecessor's word index.\nDirect JAL and backward branches select the direct target index.\nOther instructions select fall-through. This guess drives only the\ninternal RAM read port. EX always drives the resolved address on imem.\n\nOn a ready fetch, decode the live response. On a denied fetch, a valid\nprediction can enter ID/EX provisionally. Compare the saved destination\nagainst \n…[1959 of 5031 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:0f0983ac13b29bcc]…\nwith a reciprocal table and exact residual correction\nhyp-20261120-001-r9s0 3234996 Move the M-result interlock off the replay-to-decode control path\nUse those registered matches to recognize the M-result dependency at\nthe entrance to EX. Capture a fetched candidate on the producer's\ntransfer edge. If the preceding instruction was a valid M writer and\neither captured match is set, annul the candidate in EX and fetch it\nagain from retry_pc. The producer advances to WB and the retry gets\nits result through the existing bypass. This places a register between\nthe RAM word's source fields and suppression of decoded side effects.\nA dependent pair still costs one bubble and an independent pair can\nissue on consecutive clocks. At 3,234,996 cycles per ten iterations,\nacceptance requires a median clock above 84.80 MHz.\n\nhyp-20261120-002-r9s1 3234996 Register the rs1 field separately in the successor replay table\nhyp-20261120-003-r9s2 3278387 Predict the instruction two successors ahead to register replay before decode\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
