{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_12", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor x in list(map(json.loads,open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'))):\n if '-r7s2' in x['id']: print(x)\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "{'id': 'hyp-20261120-003-r7s2', 'title': 'Predict the data word in decode and replay verified loads during bus stalls', 'category': 'predictor', 'motivation': \"A ready instruction already issues across a taken branch, and the successor\\npredictor covers many denied instruction reads. The champion takes 3,234,996\\ncycles with both stall generators. With data memory always ready, the same\\npipeline takes 3,043,747 cycles. A load's predicted effective address is\\nalready available in ID, one edge before EX needs the data.\\n\", 'hypothesis': {'motivation': \"A ready instruction already issues across a taken branch, and the successor\\npredictor covers many denied instruction reads. The champion takes 3,234,996\\ncycles with both stall generators. With data memory always ready, the same\\npipeline takes 3,043,747 cycles. A load's predicted effective address is\\nalready available in ID, one edge before EX needs the data.\\n\", 'hypothesis': \"Use the low word index of the ID address prediction to read a synchronous\\non-chip table before EX has verified the address. Each row holds the most\\nrecent RAM word observed at that index, its upper address tag, and the byte\\nlanes known to be current. In EX, a live ready response still supplies the\\nload. On a denied read, a matching tag and complete coverage of the requested\\nlanes let that load advance and forward the predicted data from EX/MEM.\\nStores train the table when the data bus accepts them. An SB or SH replaces\\nthe row's mask with just the lanes written. This prevents stale neighboring\\nbytes from satisfying a wider load.\\n\\nA 512-row prototype took 3,102,126 bracketed cycles, with all five CRCs and\\nthe validation banner correct. That saves 132,870 cycles over ten iterations.\\nAt that cycle count a median above 65.67 MHz would clear the tournament's\\n4.6 percent margin. Gowin placement option 1 reached 65.226 MHz, equivalent\\nto 210.26 iterations/s or a 3.90 percent gain. The pipeline tests passed.\\n\", 'expected_impact': {'fitness_delta_pct': 4, 'confidence': 'medium'}, 'c\n…[3808 of 6880 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:a29ffb853297ccda]…\n_pct': 6.03, 'vs_baseline': 1670.46, 'fmax_mhz': 66.28, 'ipc_coremark': 3e-06, 'cycles': 3088894, 'iterations': 10, 'lut4': 4221, 'ff': 904, 'seeds': [63.704, 66.28, 66.28], 'perturbations': [[0, 63.704, 18], [1, 66.28, 18], [2, 66.28, 18]], 'lutram': 32, 'bsram': 8, 'dsp': 2, 'critical_path': {'from': 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu/remainder_q_0_s0', 'to': 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu/remainder_q_15_s0', 'slack_ns': -10.698, 'arrival_ns': 20.992, 'logic_cells': 60, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu']}, 'logic_levels': 18, 'formal_passed': True, 'cosim_passed': True, 'error': None, 'implementation_notes': '', 'timestamp': '2026-11-20T07:10:16.583476Z', 'slot': 2, 'round_id': 7, 'lesson': '- 2026-11-20 hyp-20261120-003-r7s2 (regression, +6.03%): Reading a 512-row table in ID let EX replay denied RAM loads when the tag matched and all requested byte lanes were valid, saving 132,870 cycles over ten CoreMark iterations, too few to offset the higher Fmax of the retimed divider and forwarding design (214.58 vs 226.92 iterations/s).'}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
