{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_18", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor l in open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'):\n r=json.loads(l)\n if r['id'].endswith(('r5s2','r6s2','r7s2','r9s2')):print(r['id'],r['critical_path'],r['seeds'],r['lut4'],r['bsram'], r['hypothesis']['hypothesis'][:4000])\nPY\ncat \\\"\"'$TMPDIR/r11-alu/bench.log\" | tail -c 900\ntail -10 \"$TMPDIR/r11-alu/p1/gw.log\"'", "aggregated_output": "hyp-20261120-003-r5s2 {'from': 'cpu/u_rf/regs_regs_0_0_s0', 'to': 'dmem_1_dmem_1_0_0_s', 'slack_ns': -11.091, 'arrival_ns': 21.386, 'logic_cells': 20, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_id', 'cpu/u_ex', 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu', 'cpu/u_ex']} [62.145, 61.563, 61.563] 3540 8 Train a 512-entry table indexed by predecessor PC. Each row predicts the\nsuccessor PC and its instruction from the last ready external fetch.\nRead one cycle ahead using the likely next predecessor's word index.\nDirect JAL and backward branches select the direct target index.\nOther instructions select fall-through. This guess drives only the\ninternal RAM read port. EX always drives the resolved address on imem.\n\nOn a ready fetch, decode the live response. On a denied fetch, a valid\nprediction can enter ID/EX provisionally. Compare the saved destination\nagainst PC+4 and the full EX redirect target in parallel. Register both\nequality bits and the actual redirect decision. In the next cycle the\nselected equality bit admits the instruction to EX. A mismatch annuls\nthat slot and IF retries the resolved address already in retry_pc.\nThis verifies the address for indirect jumps and table aliases as well.\nVerification costs no extra cycle on a hit or a ready bus response.\n\nA scratch prototype completed ten iterations in 3,486,909 bracketed\ncycles with both stall generators, a 16.40% cycle reduction. All five\nCRCs and the UART validation banner matched. Gowin placement options\n0, 1 and 2 reached 59.777, 61.398 and 61.39