{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_6", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg '\\\"category\\\" *: *\\\"predictor\\\"' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl | python3 -c 'import sys,json\nfor l in sys.stdin:\n d=json.loads(l); print(str(d.keys()) if not d.get(\\\"id\\\") else d[\\\"id\\\"], str(d.get(\\\"title\\\",\\\"\\\")),str(d.get(\\\"hypothesis\\\",\\\"\\\"))[:450])'\"", "aggregated_output": "hyp-20261120-003-r1s2 Predict direct control flow with a displacement-biased agree predictor {'motivation': 'Fetch advances to PC+4 even at a hot loop backedge or a direct call. Because\\nIF/ID is combinational, a correct next-PC prediction saves one fetch opportunity\\non a ready cycle. Backward loop branches and forward exit branches can share\\nthe same counter constructively if it records agreement with their respective\\ndisplacement biases.\\n', 'hypothesis': 'Predict backward conditional branches taken and forward branches fall-through\nhyp-20261120-003-r2s2 Predict direct branches and JAL in fetch on the six-step divider core {'motivation': 'The champion still fetches PC+4 after every branch. Its combinational IF/ID\\nboundary makes each correctly predicted taken transfer worth one fetch\\nopportunity. On the previous parent, the displacement-biased agree predictor\\ncut the ten-iteration CoreMark interval from 4,491,485 to 4,188,667 cycles.\\nThe champion takes the same 4,491,485 cycles, and its reported critical path\\nruns from divisor_q to remainder_q inside the divide\nhyp-20261120-003-r3s2 Predict direct branches and jumps on the radix-8 core with recovery at ID/EX {'motivation': 'The champion fetches PC+4 after every instruction. Its combinational IF/ID\\nboundary costs one fetch opportunity on each taken transfer resolved in EX.\\nThe two prior predictor runs both saved 302,818 of 4,491,485 bracketed\\nCoreMark cycles. The latest reached 102.72 iterations/s on a parent whose\\ndivider limited median Fmax to 43.026 MHz. The radix