{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_75","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cat > cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261120-003-r12s2.yaml <<'YAML'\nid: hyp-20261120-003-r12s2\ntitle: Forward a verified replay word into a dependent load or store address\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  A previous load-word predictor recovered 132,870 CoreMark cycles by supplying\n  denied RAM reads. The current core also uses an accepted LW response to form\n  the next instruction's address. Selecting between live and replay data ahead\n  of that adder would put two memory outputs on its timing path.\nhypothesis: |\n  Launch a synchronous read of a 512-entry word table using the index bits of\n  ID's predicted effective address. In EX, check the recorded read index and\n  upper tag against the checked byte address, restrict hits to ordinary RAM\n  and require validity for every requested byte. A hit supplies the load even\n  during external backpressure. Feed the raw replay word straight into ID's\n  LW-based address adder. A verified, aligned LW hit authorizes that candidate\n  if the load is the youngest writer of the next base. A live miss still\n  completes through the bus, and an immediately dependent address takes its\n  existing one-cycle repair from the forwarded architectural value.\n  \n  Train on accepted RAM reads with all lanes valid. An accepted store replaces\n  the row with its tag, replicated data and actual lane mask. Scrub validity\n  at reset, freeze lookup metadata with the consumer and reject read/write\n  collisions. An unavailable or misaligned address cannot authorize a request.\n  Carry the selected raw load word through RVFI and the usual EX/MEM forwarding.\n  \n  A scratch implementation passed the five canonical CRCs with both stall\n  generators in 3,089,744 bracketed cycles, saving 145,252 against the champion.\n  At that cycle count the required median is 85.25 MHz. Placement option 1\n  reached 80.119 MHz, with successor RAM feeding the ID address path. The\n  placement result leaves frequency recovery as the implementation risk.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/load_replay.sv\n    description: Implement the tagged word table, byte validity, reset scrub and collision exclusion.\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: Expose the predicted word index to launch the synchronous read alongside ID/EX.\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: Connect verified load hits to EX and the LW address candidate, and route a missing load to the bus.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: Exercise warm load replay and a cold denied read. Check every retirement, accepted bus transfer and partial-store overwrite.\nYAML\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
