{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_64", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor r in map(json.loads,open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl')):\n if r['id'].endswith(('r11s2','r13s1')):\n  for k in ('hypothesis','changes'):print(r['hypothesis'][k])\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "Split a 32-bit integer sum at bit 16. Compute the low result and exact carry\nwith a 17-bit adder. Start the upper adder independently using a predicted\ncarry from bits 15 through 12 of the two operands. For subtraction complement\nB and use a low carry-in of one. If those four bits all propagate, use the\neffective B sign as the carry guess. This costs one short carry chain before\nthe upper sum and handles common additions of small signed displacements.\nUse the same predicted sum for the integer EX result and the ADD-produced\nbase page that ID needs for an immediately dependent load or store.\n\nVerify the carry before the producer transfers. On a mismatch hold the\nproducer, its forwarding sources and its successor for one clock, save the\nexact boundary carry, then use it for the high sum on the retry. Qualify the\ninterlock with a valid, effectful arithmetic operation so annulled slots and\nirrelevant default ALU_ADD decodes cannot hold the pipeline. The check only\ncompares one bit and can run alongside upper-result generation. A key risk is\nmoving the limiting path to carry verification and the pipeline enables.\nMeasure repair cycles and bracketed cycles as well as the three-placement\nmedian. At a 0.5% cycle cost acceptance requires about 89.70 MHz.\n\n[{'file': 'rtl/alu.sv', 'description': 'Form predicted split ADD and SUB results, export the predicted and exact middle carry, and accept a registered carry override for the repair cycle.'}, {'file': 'rtl/ex_stage.sv', 'description': 'Register the exact carry on a miss, qualify misses for valid integer ADD, ADDI, AUIPC and SUB writers to nonzero rd, and expose the selected arithmetic sum for the ID base-page bypass. Hold repair state through any concurrent backpressure.'}, {'file': 'rtl/id_stage.sv', 'description': \"Source the ADD producer's base page from the shared split sum. Keep the independent low displacement sum and existing effective-address repair.\"}, {'file': 'rtl/hazard_unit.sv', 'description': 'Hold ID/EX and EX/MEM on the initial carry miss and retain MEM/WB\n…[2220 of 5292 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:5aa0840b178f4681]…\npkg.sv', 'description': 'Extend EX/MEM with an alternate upper result and carry select, and ID/EX with the corresponding upper-address fields.'}, {'file': 'rtl/ex_stage.sv', 'description': 'Capture split arithmetic results at EX/MEM and select the upper request address from the resident ID/EX fields. Make the split ADD base available to ID on the same cycle as its current operands.'}, {'file': 'rtl/id_stage.sv', 'description': \"Replace the full-width add_base with the producer's slices, carry the candidate pages across issue, and install an exact address on repair. Hold all address fields together on a denied request.\"}, {'file': 'rtl/core.sv', 'description': \"Reconstruct the exact EX/MEM result once for both EX forwarding inputs and ID's MEM-base candidate. Wire the independent EX sum slices to ID.\"}, {'file': 'rtl/mem_stage.sv', 'description': 'Feed the reconstructed integer result to MEM/WB alongside the existing multiply and divide result choices. Preserve the exact value for register writes and RVFI.'}]\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
