{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_92", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"cat > cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261120-003-r14s2.yaml <<'EOF'\nid: hyp-20261120-003-r14s2\ntitle: \\\"Predict a load's 64-byte sector two instructions ahead\\\"\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  Earlier load replay designs saved over 130,000 cycles, but deriving the\n  RAM read address from the load's operands or reading on the falling edge\n  cost clock speed. The data sector is predictable earlier than the word.\n  On the champion's CoreMark retirement trace, a 512-entry last-sector\n  table indexed by the PC two retirements before each load predicted\n  address[10:6] correctly for 315,227 of 544,852 bracketed loads (57.9%).\n  This measures set prediction alone. It excludes pipeline bubbles, RAM\n  conflicts, byte validity and bus readiness.\nhypothesis: |\n  While A executes and B decodes, use A's registered PC[10:2] to read a\n  five-bit sector hint from distributed RAM. At the edge that admits B,\n  launch a rising-edge read of the hinted sector from a 2 KiB load replay\n  store. While B executes and C decodes, all sixteen candidate words are\n  available. Select C's word with the existing ID address candidate[5:2]\n  and latch its raw data, word-valid bit, physical sector tag and predicted\n  index beside C in ID/EX. This puts a full clock boundary between the\n  replay RAM output and EX load forwarding. The final ID address selects\n  a word from the returned sector without driving a RAM read port.\n  Learn A's hint from C's checked physical address when C completes a\n  real RAM load. Track A through two actual admissions and discard broken\n  chains on bubbles, annuls and redirects that discard an instruction.\n\n  A ready load uses the live response. A denied load can complete locally\n  only if its exact, checked, naturally aligned RAM word address agrees\n  with all saved address bits and the word is valid. Check alignment and\n  MMIO independently. A miss falls back to the ordinary bus. Freeze a\n  pending external request until acceptance. Select live versus registered\n  raw data using readiness, with tag validation qualifying advancement.\n  Preserve the existing accepting-LW base bypass. A dependent address\n  following a local LW can use the normal repair cycle.\n\n  A same-cycle sector-directory prototype took 3,146,750 cycles for ten\n  iterations with canonical CRCs. Reading the entire predicted sector\n  ahead of decode is the unmeasured timing change. At 3.16 million cycles\n  the median must exceed 87.19 MHz to clear the tournament margin.\n  Count verified denied-load hits, conflicting writes and extra address\n  repairs, then compare bracketed cycles times clock period across the\n  three Gowin placements. The main risk is the 16-way word select in ID.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/load_replay.sv\n    description: |\n      Implement the hint table and 32 direct-mapped sectors of sixteen\n      banked words each. Hold one physical tag, a sector-valid bit and a\n      16-bit word-valid mask per sector. Fill on accepted ordinary RAM\n      reads and full-word stores. Invalidate a partially stored word.\n      Replacing a tag discards every old valid word. Clear sector validity\n      on reset. Reject same-sector writes from launch through admission,\n      including updates while a candidate is held, so stale data cannot hit.\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: |\n      Launch the lookahead from registered EX PC, track training keys on\n      actual advances, and connect accepted RAM transactions and local hits.\n      Keep exactly one owner for a stalled demand transaction.\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: Carry the predicted physical word address, raw word and usable bit with each ID/EX slot.\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: Select the candidate by low_sum[5:2] during decode and register data, tag, set, offset and validity together. Clear eligibility on address repair or squash.\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: Check the candidate against the resident load and feed the selected raw word to both the existing subword formatter and RVFI.\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: Release a denied load on a verified local hit. Preserve holds for address repair and outstanding external accesses.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: Exercise changing sectors at one load PC, same-set tag aliases, byte stores between prediction and use, and held or annulled consumers. Check bus acceptances, forwarded values and RVFI order.\nEOF\npython - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport json,jsonschema,yaml\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261120-003-r14s2.yaml');v=yaml.safe_load(p.read_text());jsonschema.validate(v,json.load(open('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json')));assert v['id']==p.stem;print(v['title'],263.77*1.046*.316)\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
