{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_14", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor e in map(json.loads, open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl')):\n if e['id'].endswith(('r12s1','r13s2','r14s2')):print(e['id'], e['hypothesis']['hypothesis'], e.get('implementation_notes')[:1200])\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "hyp-20261120-002-r12s1 Move the synchronous lookup one stage later. Compute the exact byte address\nonce in EX from forwarded rs1 and the signed displacement. On EX transfer,\nlaunch a 512-entry word RAM read with that address and capture the full\naddress, access width, store lanes and instruction in EX/MEM. The RAM\noutput and its requesting instruction arrive in MEM together. This removes\nthe ID address candidates, producer-specific page arithmetic and repair\ncycle. It also removes the tag check from the issuing load's EX stage.\n\nGive a resident RAM load the returned word as its provisional forwarding\nvalue. In parallel, check the full word tag and valid lanes and format the\nselected bytes for the consumer. On a hit the next EX instruction can use\nthe value on the normal EX/MEM bypass. Keep the tag comparator off that\ndata bus. On a miss hold the resident load and its younger consumer, refill\nfrom an accepted external read, and resume from the registered refill.\nGate younger transfers, divide launch and fetch redirection until the\nolder load can complete. Hold a known fetch PC during a miss. A load used\nimmediately as another memory operation's base waits one cycle for its\nregistered WB value, cutting the RAM-output-to-address-adder recurrence.\n\nMEM also owns a one-entry external command register. An aligned RAM store\nmay retire once its command is buffered in order. Hold its pins until\nacceptance and allow drain and replacement on one edge. Update the local\nrow when ownership transfers. A partial store may invalidate neighboring\nlanes. Clear row validity on reset and hold the read result with its MEM\nslot across stalls. A same-index RAM read/write collision forces a miss,\nand a refill waits behind any older buffered store. Give each command exactly one\ntransfer. Bypass local service for MMIO, drain older writes at fences and\ntermination, and preserve alignment traps before issuing any command.\n\nThe scratch result measures the service mechanism. The EX lookup and\nremoval of ID address generation are the unmeasured\n…[2994 of 6066 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:a696690706ca2944]…\nad uses the live response. A denied load can complete locally\nonly if its exact, checked, naturally aligned RAM word address agrees\nwith all saved address bits and the word is valid. Check alignment and\nMMIO independently. A miss falls back to the ordinary bus. Freeze a\npending external request until acceptance. Select live versus registered\nraw data using readiness, with tag validation qualifying advancement.\nPreserve the existing accepting-LW base bypass. A dependent address\nfollowing a local LW can use the normal repair cycle.\n\nA same-cycle sector-directory prototype took 3,146,750 cycles for ten\niterations with canonical CRCs. Reading the entire predicted sector\nahead of decode is the unmeasured timing change. At 3.16 million cycles\nthe median must exceed 87.19 MHz to clear the tournament margin.\nCount verified denied-load hits, conflicting writes and extra address\nrepairs, then compare bracketed cycles times clock period across the\nthree Gowin placements. The main risk is the 16-way word select in ID.\n \n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
