{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_43","type":"agent_message","text":"The first prototype saved 304,147 bracketed cycles, but its 56.501 MHz median missed the threshold. Registering the correction decision and address preserved the cycle saving and raised the median to 61.218 MHz, enough for 144.94 iterations/s. I’m checking the stall and wrong-path cases before finalizing the proposal."}}
{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_44", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"cat > cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261120-003-r4s2.yaml <<'YAML'\nid: hyp-20261120-003-r4s2\ntitle: \\\"Register branch recovery to preserve fetch prediction throughput\\\"\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  The champion takes 4,527,760 cycles for ten CoreMark iterations. Predicting\n  direct transfers saved 302,818 cycles on the preceding radix-8 core. On the\n  current champion a scratch implementation saved 304,147 cycles, but driving\n  the ID/EX control flush directly from the EX comparison limited median Fmax\n  to 56.501 MHz. At this cycle count acceptance requires more than 60.574 MHz.\nhypothesis: |\n  Predict legal direct branches and JAL in fetch with a 256-entry\n  displacement-biased agree predictor. Register the EX miss bit and its\n  recovery address in parallel. After the edge, that bit both selects the\n  recovery address on imemAddr and annuls the one younger instruction in\n  ID/EX. This keeps the forwarded branch comparison off the wide ID/EX\n  reset and PC-input mux paths while retaining one-cycle miss recovery.\n\n  On a scratch copy of the champion the registered version completed ten\n  iterations in 4,223,613 marker-to-marker cycles with both bus stalls and\n  all five canonical CRCs. Gowin placement options 0, 1 and 2 reached\n  62.082, 61.218 and 61.218 MHz. That median gives 144.94 iterations/s,\n  5.71% above 137.11. The median placement's worst path runs from the\n  register file through EX to data RAM. The frequency margin is 0.64 MHz.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 6\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Read a 256 x 2 distributed RAM at effective PC[9:2], initialized to\n      01, with one synchronous EX training write. For the six legal B\n      encodings predict taken when instr[31] XOR counter[1] is set. Predict\n      JAL taken. Use a shared B/J displacement adder and allow prediction\n      only to aligned instruction RAM below 0x00100000. Feed ID raw imem_data.\n      Keep separate speculative-PC, repair-PC and miss registers. Capture\n      the alternative successor every edge and the miss for one cycle.\n      Mux the two registered PCs with the registered miss. On acceptance\n      advance from that effective PC. If the corrected fetch stalls, retain\n      its address in the speculative-PC register as the miss pulse clears.\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: Carry the effective predicted-taken bit and the two-bit counter snapshot in if_id_t and id_ex_t.\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Capture, hold and bubble the prediction metadata with its instruction.\n      Hold the payload on downstream stalls. Clear valid and ctrl on reset\n      or an interlock bubble. Use the registered EX miss to mask the valid\n      output of the one younger ID/EX slot during the recovery cycle.\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Compare effective predicted and resolved direction once per valid EX\n      transfer. Compute the repair value in parallel from the saved choice:\n      PC+4 for a predicted-taken transfer, otherwise the architectural target.\n      JALR uses forwarded rs1 and clears target bit zero. A taken misaligned\n      transfer traps and continues at PC+4. Drive RVFI pc_next from the actual\n      outcome. Gate divide issue, miss and training on effective validity.\n      Clear EX/MEM controls for an invalid slot to suppress bus requests and\n      forwarding. Train an advancing legal conditional branch once, using its\n      saved counter. Increment on disagreement with the displacement sign and\n      decrement on agreement, saturating both ways. Skip reset, holds and faults.\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: |\n      Wire EX's miss, alternative successor and training signals to IF. Send\n      IF's registered miss to ID to annul the younger slot. Disconnect the\n      same-cycle redirect from the hazard-unit flush. Qualify the late-result\n      interlock with effective ID/EX validity so a killed load or multiply\n      cannot hold the corrected fetch. Keep data-bus and divider holds intact.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: |\n      Check consecutive fetches at a predicted backedge and direct JAL, and\n      check exit recovery, aliasing, misalignment and JALR. Use an unpredicted\n      JALR in the existing unready wrong-path store test so it still exercises\n      a correction. Hold a branch behind an older stalled load, release it\n      with imemReady low, and keep the corrected address stalled across the\n      following edge. Assert the fetch PCs, absence of wrong-path bus strobes\n      and consecutive channel-0 retirement orders.\nYAML\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
