{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_5", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg -in 'predict|r4s[012]' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl | python3 -c 'import sys,json; rows=[json.loads(s.split(\\\":\\\",1)[1]) for s in sys.stdin]; print(rows[-1].keys()); print(json.dumps(rows[-1],indent=2)[:24000]); print(\\\"\\\\n\\\".join(str((r.get(\\\"id\\\"), r.get(\\\"title\\\"),r.get(\\\"category\\\"))) for r in rows))'\"", "aggregated_output": "dict_keys(['id', 'title', 'category', 'motivation', 'hypothesis', 'expected_impact', 'changes', 'outcome', 'fitness', 'delta_pct', 'vs_baseline', 'fmax_mhz', 'ipc_coremark', 'cycles', 'iterations', 'lut4', 'ff', 'seeds', 'perturbations', 'lutram', 'bsram', 'dsp', 'critical_path', 'logic_levels', 'formal_passed', 'cosim_passed', 'error', 'implementation_notes', 'timestamp', 'slot', 'round_id', 'lesson'])\n{\n  \"id\": \"hyp-20261120-003-r4s2\",\n  \"title\": \"Carry the unchosen fetch address into registered branch recovery\",\n  \"category\": \"predictor\",\n  \"motivation\": \"The champion takes 4,527,760 cycles for ten CoreMark iterations. Predicting\\ndirect transfers saved 302,818 cycles on the preceding radix-8 core. On the\\ncurrent champion a scratch implementation saved 304,147 cycles, but driving\\nthe ID/EX control flush directly from the EX comparison limited median Fmax\\nto 56.501 MHz. At this cycle count acceptance requires more than 60.574 MHz.\\n\",\n  \"hypothesis\": {\n    \"motivation\": \"The champion takes 4,527,760 cycles for ten CoreMark iterations. Predicting\\ndirect transfers saved 302,818 cycles on the preceding radix-8 core. On the\\ncurrent champion a scratch implementation saved 304,147 cycles, but driving\\nthe ID/EX control flush directly from the EX comparison limited median Fmax\\nto 56.501 MHz. At this cycle count acceptance requires more than 60.574 MHz.\\n\",\n    \"hypothesis\": \"Predict legal direct branches and JAL in fetch with a 256-entry\\ndisplacement-biased agree predictor. At fetch, compute both the target\\nand PC+4. Follow the prediction and latch the unchosen address alongside\\nthe instruction. At the end of EX, register that recovery address and\\nthe miss bit in parallel. After the edge, the bit selects the recovery\\naddress on imemAddr and annuls the one younger instruction in ID/EX.\\nThe two fetch addresses are ready before the forwarded branch comparison\\nfinishes. A miss costs one fetch opportunity.\\n\\nOn a scratch copy of the champion the registered version completed ten\\niterations in 4,223,613 marker\n…[8601 of 11673 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:780a59cbb05b9457]…\nd same-cycle EX target fetch (147.00 vs 153.52 CoreMark iterations/s).\"\n}\n('hyp-20261120-001-r1s0', 'Compute eight quotient bits per clock in a shared DIV/REM unit', 'micro_opt')\n('hyp-20261120-002-r1s1', 'Move DIV and REM off the single-cycle execute path', 'structural')\n('hyp-20261120-003-r1s2', 'Predict direct control flow with a displacement-biased agree predictor', 'predictor')\n('hyp-20261120-002-r2s1', 'Resolve six quotient bits with two radix-8 divider stages', 'structural')\n('hyp-20261120-003-r2s2', 'Predict direct branches and JAL in fetch on the six-step divider core', 'predictor')\n('hyp-20261120-003-r3s2', 'Predict direct branches and jumps on the radix-8 core with recovery at ID/EX', 'predictor')\n('hyp-20261120-001-r4s0', 'Fetch the resolved target in the EX redirect cycle', 'micro_opt')\n('hyp-20261120-002-r4s1', 'Issue resolved branch targets through a one-entry fetch buffer', 'structural')\n('hyp-20261120-003-r4s2', 'Carry the unchosen fetch address into registered branch recovery', 'predictor')\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
