{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_15", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python -c 'import json\nr=list(map(json.loads, open(\\\"cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\\\")))[-1]; print(r.keys()); print(json.dumps(r,indent=2)[-8800:])'\"", "aggregated_output": "dict_keys(['id', 'title', 'category', 'motivation', 'hypothesis', 'expected_impact', 'changes', 'outcome', 'fitness', 'delta_pct', 'vs_baseline', 'fmax_mhz', 'ipc_coremark', 'cycles', 'iterations', 'lut4', 'ff', 'seeds', 'perturbations', 'lutram', 'bsram', 'dsp', 'critical_path', 'logic_levels', 'formal_passed', 'cosim_passed', 'error', 'implementation_notes', 'timestamp', 'slot', 'round_id', 'lesson'])\nenied fetches\",\n  \"category\": \"predictor\",\n  \"motivation\": \"The champion already issues a ready branch or JALR target as its\\npredecessor leaves EX. Its ten CoreMark iterations take 4,171,092\\ncycles. The previous direction predictor took 4,223,613 cycles because\\neach miss cost a fetch opportunity. A predictor that remembers the\\ninstruction at the successor can recover fetch opportunities during\\ninstruction-bus stalls, even in straight-line code.\\n\",\n  \"hypothesis\": {\n    \"motivation\": \"The champion already issues a ready branch or JALR target as its\\npredecessor leaves EX. Its ten CoreMark iterations take 4,171,092\\ncycles. The previous direction predictor took 4,223,613 cycles because\\neach miss cost a fetch opportunity. A predictor that remembers the\\ninstruction at the successor can recover fetch opportunities during\\ninstruction-bus stalls, even in straight-line code.\\n\",\n    \"hypothesis\": \"Train a 512-entry table indexed by predecessor PC. Each row predicts the\\nsuccessor PC and its instruction from the last ready external fetch.\\nRead one cycle ahead using the likely next predecessor's word index.\\nDirect JAL and backward branches select the direct target index.\\nOther instructions select fall-through. This guess drives only the\\ninternal RAM read port. EX always drives the resolved address on imem.\\n\\nOn a ready fetch, decode the live response. On a denied fetch, a valid\\nprediction can enter ID/EX provisionally. Compare the saved destination\\nagainst PC+4 and the full EX redirect target in parallel. Register both\\nequality bits and the actual redirect decision. In the next cycle the\\nselected equality \n…[6136 of 9208 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:7bc1b0823e0d3123]…\nations\": [\n    [\n      0,\n      62.145,\n      15\n    ],\n    [\n      1,\n      61.563,\n      15\n    ],\n    [\n      2,\n      61.563,\n      15\n    ]\n  ],\n  \"lutram\": 8,\n  \"bsram\": 8,\n  \"dsp\": 2,\n  \"critical_path\": {\n    \"from\": \"cpu/u_rf/regs_regs_0_0_s0\",\n    \"to\": \"dmem_1_dmem_1_0_0_s\",\n    \"slack_ns\": -11.091,\n    \"arrival_ns\": 21.386,\n    \"logic_cells\": 20,\n    \"modules\": [\n      \"clock_ibuf\",\n      \"cpu/u_id\",\n      \"cpu/u_ex\",\n      \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu\",\n      \"cpu/u_ex\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"logic_levels\": 15,\n  \"formal_passed\": true,\n  \"cosim_passed\": true,\n  \"error\": null,\n  \"implementation_notes\": \"\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-20T05:02:04.433223Z\",\n  \"slot\": 2,\n  \"round_id\": 5,\n  \"lesson\": \"- 2026-11-20 hyp-20261120-003-r5s2 (improvement, +15.00%): Replaying the successor instruction from a table indexed by predecessor PC kept CoreMark issuing across taken loop backedges with `io_imemReady` low, while parallel checks of the saved successor PC against `fallthrough_pc` and `redirect_target` let EX annul mismatches.\"\n}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
