{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_40", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python -c 'import json; rows=[r for r in map(json.loads,open(\\\"cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\\\")) if r[\\\"id\\\"].endswith(\\\"r5s0\\\")];print(json.dumps(rows[-1][\\\"hypothesis\\\"],indent=1)); print(rows[-1][\\\"implementation_notes\\\"])'\"", "aggregated_output": "{\n \"motivation\": \"The champion issues data requests in MEM, one cycle too late for a dependent\\ninstruction to use a load through the EX/MEM bypass. An instruction trace\\nof the ten timed iterations contains 544,852 loads. A branch immediately\\nfollows 135,320 loads with a matching source field. Moving address generation\\none stage earlier can remove that bubble and keep the FPGA RAM address\\nregistered. The latter matters because the champion's reported option-zero\\ncritical path crosses the shared EX ALU on its way to data memory.\\n\",\n \"hypothesis\": \"Compute the full byte address as a memory instruction enters ID/EX. Drive\\nthe data bus from this register during EX. On acceptance, latch the raw\\nread word for RVFI and the formatted load value in EX/MEM for ordinary EX\\nforwarding. Stores use the forwarded rs2 in EX. A stalled request holds\\nits address, data, enables and producer operands through the accepting edge.\\n\\nTo handle a newly produced base, compare the incoming rs1 against the\\nyoungest writers. For ADD, ADDI and AUIPC in EX, their operands A and B\\nare already available. With displacement D, compute P = A XOR B, then\\n(P XOR D) + (((A AND B) OR (P AND D)) << 1) modulo 2^32. This gives\\nA+B+D with one carry-propagate adder. Compute it in parallel with the normal\\nbase-plus-displacement path. A preceding LUI supplies its immediate and an\\naligned, accepted LW can supply the raw bus word. Use the EX/MEM value for\\nolder available writers and the write-first register file otherwise.\\nInterlock unavailable bases, including pending products. Suppress x0 and\\ntrapped writes. Keep the multiply-use interlock for ordinary EX consumers.\\n\\nA scratch prototype completed ten iterations in 3,967,605 bracketed cycles\\nversus 4,171,092 for the champion, with all canonical CRCs. Gowin placement\\noptions 0, 1 and 2 reached 61.552, 66.658 and 66.658 MHz respectively.\\nThe median gives 168.01 iterations/s, 9.44% above the champion. The\\nprototype passed all 53 standard single-channel formal checks. The selftest\\nand three random programs matched the reference with and without bus stalls.\\n\",\n \"expected_impact\": {\n  \"fitness_delta_pct\": 9,\n  \"confidence\": \"high\"\n },\n \"changes\": [\n  {\n   \"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\",\n   \"description\": \"Carry the effective address in ID/EX, then carry the serviced address and raw load word in EX/MEM alongside the forwarded result.\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\",\n   \"description\": \"Select the youngest available base and register the address on issue. Compute the ordinary, LW/LUI-bypassed and carry-save three-input candidate addresses in parallel with the producer checks.\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\",\n   \"description\": \"Drive the registered address, alignment-qualified enables and replicated store data in EX. On transfer, capture the raw read word, effective address and extended load result. Expose the forwarded arithmetic operands for address generation.\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\",\n   \"description\": \"Connect the EX bus, classify eligible base producers, permit EX/MEM load forwarding and derive dmem backpressure from the resident ID/EX memory operation.\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\",\n   \"description\": \"Interlock address bases that cannot yet be bypassed and retain the multiply-use check. Hold the resident request and forwarding state on data waits, including simultaneous instruction waits.\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"file\": \"rtl/mem_stage.sv\",\n   \"description\": \"Format the captured raw word and byte address into the existing MEM/WB read_data path for register writeback, alongside the earlier EX/MEM copy used for bypass. Use the captured access for aligned RVFI masks, memory data and traps. Preserve the MEM multiplier.\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\",\n   \"description\": \"Assert back-to-back load-to-branch and LW-to-address timing. Check dependent ADDI addresses with carries, stale-base interlocks, misaligned requests and a stalled store accepted exactly once. Adjust stage-specific cycle expectations while retaining architectural checks.\"\n  }\n ]\n}\n\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
