{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_116", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261120-003-r6s2.yaml')\ns=\\\"id: hyp-20261120-003-r6s2\\\\ntitle: Predict same-page data addresses to forward loads from EX/MEM\\\\ncategory: predictor\\\\nmotivation: |\\\\n  The champion already replays instructions across taken backedges. Ten\\\\n  iterations took 3,486,909 cycles with both stalls and 3,353,265 with\\\\n  instruction stalls disabled, a 4.0% throughput difference at equal Fmax.\\\\n  The acceptance margin is 4.6%. A prior trace counted 135,320 loads\\\\n  immediately followed by a branch with a matching source field. An\\\\n  address predictor can make those load values available a cycle earlier.\\\\nhypothesis: |\\\\n  Predict that adding a load or store's signed 12-bit displacement preserves\\\\n  its base register's 4 KiB page. In decode, take bits [31:12] from the\\\\n  selected base and compute only (base + displacement) modulo 8192.\\\\n  Concatenate the page with the low 12 sum bits. Comparing sum bit 12 with\\\\n  base bit 12 detects every crossing, including borrow and 32-bit wrap,\\\\n  because one displacement can cross at most one page. Register the\\\\n  candidate address, the crossing bit and whether the base source was\\\\n  available. This puts the check beside the memory instruction before it\\\\n  can assert a bus strobe.\\\\n  \\\\n  An in-page hit issues in EX from a single address register. A crossing\\\\n  or unavailable base costs one repair cycle. Suppress the request, hold\\\\n  the instruction, and overwrite the same register with forwarded rs1\\\\n  plus the full signed displacement. The repaired instruction can issue\\\\n  on the next cycle and holds its request through backpressure. An accepted\\\\n  load forwards from EX/MEM to the next instruction.\\\\n  \\\\n  A scratch implementation completed the ten timed iterations in 3,234,996\\\\n  cycles with both stall generators and all five canonical CRCs. Gowin\\\\n  placement options 0, 1 and 2 reached 60.066, 61.400 and 61.400 MHz.\\\\n  The median gives 189.80 iterations/s, 7.50% above 176.55. At that cycle\\\\n  count, acceptance requires a median above 59.74 MHz.\\\\nexpected_impact:\\\\n  fitness_delta_pct: 8\\\\n  confidence: medium\\\\nchanges:\\\\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\\\\n    description: |\\\\n      Calculate the 13-bit sums for the available bases in parallel.\\\\n      For an immediately preceding ADD, ADDI or AUIPC with operands A\\\\n      and B, get the base page from A+B. Form the low 13 bits of A+B+D\\\\n      with a three-input carry-save compressor and one short adder,\\\\n      in parallel with A+B. Select the LUI immediate or accepted aligned\\\\n      LW raw word for those producers. Otherwise use an available EX/MEM\\\\n      result or the write-first register file. Register the selected page\\\\n      and low 12 bits in the address register. Give a repair write priority\\\\n      over its ordinary enable. Drive the bus directly from its Q output.\\\\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\\\\n    description: |\\\\n      Compare the incoming rs1 against in-flight writers with youngest\\\\n      priority and x0 exclusion. Mark unsupported immediate producers and\\\\n      outstanding products unavailable. Qualify the LW base bypass by\\\\n      alignment and pipeline transfer. Route the EX memory port and\\\\n      EX/MEM load bypass. Apply the existing successor annul to all decoded\\\\n      controls before the resident slot can repair, redirect or access memory.\\\\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\\\\n    description: |\\\\n      Carry the predicted address, crossing flag and base-source status\\\\n      with ID/EX. Carry the serviced byte address and raw accepted read\\\\n      word alongside the normal result in EX/MEM.\\\\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\\\\n    description: |\\\\n      Gate bus enables with the registered prediction status and alignment.\\\\n      On a miss, latch a repaired flag while writing the corrected address\\\\n      back into the address register. Clear that flag when the slot leaves.\\\\n      Format accepted loads for the EX/MEM result bypass. Use forwarded\\\\n      store data and preserve misalignment traps and suppressed writes.\\\\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\\\\n    description: |\\\\n      Hold ID/EX, EX/MEM and forwarding data during a repair or an EX\\\\n      memory request denied by dmemReady. Clear MEM/WB valid on a hold.\\\\n      Interlock products and allow a dependent successor to advance with\\\\n      an accepted load. Apply the same hold to successor replay metadata.\\\\n  - file: rtl/mem_stage.sv\\\\n    description: |\\\\n      Build RVFI memory fields and writeback from the registered serviced\\\\n      address, raw word, width and store data. Preserve the MEM multiplier\\\\n      and the single-channel retirement boundary.\\\\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\\\\n    description: |\\\\n      Check back-to-back load-to-branch retirement on a hit. Exercise\\\\n      0x0ffc + 4 and 0x1000 - 4, an unsupported base producer, a misaligned\\\\n      corrected address and a denied repaired store. Check all accepted\\\\n      bus transactions, masks and RVFI order. Update stage-specific stall\\\\n      expectations for EX memory issue while retaining the wrong-path store,\\\\n      JALR, FENCE.I, multiply and divide checks.\\\"\np.write_text('\\\\n'.join(line.rstrip() for line in s.splitlines())+'\\\\n')\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_116", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261120-003-r6s2.yaml')\ns=\\\"id: hyp-20261120-003-r6s2\\\\ntitle: Predict same-page data addresses to forward loads from EX/MEM\\\\ncategory: predictor\\\\nmotivation: |\\\\n  The champion already replays instructions across taken backedges. Ten\\\\n  iterations took 3,486,909 cycles with both stalls and 3,353,265 with\\\\n  instruction stalls disabled, a 4.0% throughput difference at equal Fmax.\\\\n  The acceptance margin is 4.6%. A prior trace counted 135,320 loads\\\\n  immediately followed by a branch with a matching source field. An\\\\n  address predictor can make those load values available a cycle earlier.\\\\nhypothesis: |\\\\n  Predict that adding a load or store's signed 12-bit displacement preserves\\\\n  its base register's 4 KiB page. In decode, take bits [31:12] from the\\\\n  selected base and compute only (base + displacement) modulo 8192.\\\\n  Concatenate the page with the low 12 sum bits. Comparing sum bit 12 with\\\\n  base bit 12 detects every crossing, including borrow and 32-bit wrap,\\\\n  because one displacement can cross at most one page. Register the\\\\n  candidate address, the crossing bit and whether the base source was\\\\n  available. This puts the check beside the memory instruction before it\\\\n  can assert a bus strobe.\\\\n  \\\\n  An in-page hit issues in EX from a single address register. A crossing\\\\n  or unavailable base costs one repair cycle. Suppress the request, hold\\\\n  the instruction, and overwrite the same register with forwarded rs1\\\\n  plus the full signed displacement. The repaired instruction can issue\\\\n  on the next cycle and holds its request through backpressure. An accepted\\\\n  load forwards from EX/MEM to the next instruction.\\\\n  \\\\n  A scratch implementation completed the ten timed iterations in 3,234,996\\\\n  cycles with both stall generators and all five canonical CRCs. Gowin\\\\n  placement options 0, 1 and 2 reached 60.066, 61.400 and 61.400 MHz.\\\\n  The median gives 189.80 iterations/s, 7.50% above 176.55. At that cycle\\\\n  count, acceptance requires a median above 59.74 MHz.\\\\nexpected_impact:\\\\n  fitness_delta_pct: 8\\\\n  confidence: medium\\\\nchanges:\\\\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\\\\n    description: |\\\\n      Calculate the 13-bit sums for the available bases in parallel.\\\\n      For an immediately preceding ADD, ADDI or AUIPC with operands A\\\\n      and B, get the base page from A+B. Form the low 13 bits of A+B+D\\\\n      with a three-input carry-save compressor and one short adder,\\\\n      in parallel with A+B. Select the LUI immediate or accepted aligned\\\\n      LW raw word for those producers. Otherwise use an available EX/MEM\\\\n      result or the write-first register file. Register the selected page\\\\n      and low 12 bits in the address register. Give a repair write priority\\\\n      over its ordinary enable. Drive the bus directly from its Q output.\\\\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\\\\n    description: |\\\\n      Compare the incoming rs1 against in-flight writers with youngest\\\\n      priority and x0 exclusion. Mark unsupported immediate producers and\\\\n      outstanding products unavailable. Qualify the LW base bypass by\\\\n      alignment and pipeline transfer. Route the EX memory port and\\\\n      EX/MEM load bypass. Apply the existing successor annul to all decoded\\\\n      controls before the resident slot can repair, redirect or access memory.\\\\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\\\\n    description: |\\\\n      Carry the predicted address, crossing flag and base-source status\\\\n      with ID/EX. Carry the serviced byte address and raw accepted read\\\\n      word alongside the normal result in EX/MEM.\\\\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\\\\n    description: |\\\\n      Gate bus enables with the registered prediction status and alignment.\\\\n      On a miss, latch a repaired flag while writing the corrected address\\\\n      back into the address register. Clear that flag when the slot leaves.\\\\n      Format accepted loads for the EX/MEM result bypass. Use forwarded\\\\n      store data and preserve misalignment traps and suppressed writes.\\\\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\\\\n    description: |\\\\n      Hold ID/EX, EX/MEM and forwarding data during a repair or an EX\\\\n      memory request denied by dmemReady. Clear MEM/WB valid on a hold.\\\\n      Interlock products and allow a dependent successor to advance with\\\\n      an accepted load. Apply the same hold to successor replay metadata.\\\\n  - file: rtl/mem_stage.sv\\\\n    description: |\\\\n      Build RVFI memory fields and writeback from the registered serviced\\\\n      address, raw word, width and store data. Preserve the MEM multiplier\\\\n      and the single-channel retirement boundary.\\\\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\\\\n    description: |\\\\n      Check back-to-back load-to-branch retirement on a hit. Exercise\\\\n      0x0ffc + 4 and 0x1000 - 4, an unsupported base producer, a misaligned\\\\n      corrected address and a denied repaired store. Check all accepted\\\\n      bus transactions, masks and RVFI order. Update stage-specific stall\\\\n      expectations for EX memory issue while retaining the wrong-path store,\\\\n      JALR, FENCE.I, multiply and divide checks.\\\"\np.write_text('\\\\n'.join(line.rstrip() for line in s.splitlines())+'\\\\n')\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
