{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_4", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/LESSONS.md schemas/hypothesis.schema.json'", "aggregated_output": "- 2026-11-20 hyp-20261120-001-r1s0 (regression, +471.20%): Eight serial trial subtractions on the `partial_q` feedback path limited median Fmax to 31.094 MHz versus 41.649 MHz for six steps per clock, while CoreMark executed no DIV/REM between markers to benefit from the shorter divide latency.\n- 2026-11-20 hyp-20261120-002-r1s1 (improvement, +665.10%): Moving combinational `/` and `%` off the shared EX result path into a six-cycle restoring divider raised median Fmax from 5.442 to 41.649 MHz without adding divider stalls because CoreMark issued no DIV/REM between its markers.\n- 2026-11-20 hyp-20261120-003-r1s2 (regression, +6.19%): Predicting branches by displacement bias and taking JAL in fetch saved 302,818 CoreMark cycles by avoiding EX redirects, while the combinational DIV/REM path still limited median Fmax to 5.392 MHz.\n- 2026-11-20 hyp-20261120-001-r2s0 (regression, +10.91%): Replacing six serial trials with three radix-4 stages that test divisor multiples in parallel raised median Fmax from 41.649 to 46.194 MHz, exposing the path from the register file through hazard logic to ID/EX as the new timing limit.\n- 2026-11-20 hyp-20261120-002-r2s1 (improvement, +12.46%): Registering 3D, 5D and 7D let two radix-8 stages replace six serial trial subtractions, raising median Fmax from 41.649 to 46.838 MHz at the same 4,491,485 CoreMark cycles, with the single-cycle multiplier limiting both median-frequency placements.\n- 2026-11-20 hyp-20261120-003-r2s2 (regression, +10.77%): Predicting branches and JAL in fetch avoided EX redirects and saved 302,818 CoreMark cycles, but the six-step divider’s `remainder_q` feedback path limited median Fmax to 43.026 MHz, leaving throughput below the radix-8 core (102.72 vs 104.28 iterations/s).\n- 2026-11-20 hyp-20261120-001-r3s0 (regression, +18.45%): Registering four multiply partial products at EX/MEM raised median Fmax from 46.838 to 55.927 MHz, while registering the forwarded operands and doing the full multiply in MEM reached 62.078 MHz with the same 0.81% CoreMark cycle pena\n…[3689 of 6761 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:0ed21d4faf178ca1]…\nnLength\": 5},\n    \"category\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"enum\": [\"micro_opt\",\"structural\",\"extension\",\"predictor\",\"memory\"]},\n    \"motivation\":  {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 20},\n    \"hypothesis\":  {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 20},\n    \"expected_impact\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\",\n      \"required\": [\"fitness_delta_pct\",\"confidence\"],\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"fitness_delta_pct\": {\"type\": \"integer\"},\n        \"confidence\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"enum\": [\"low\",\"medium\",\"high\"]}\n      }\n    },\n    \"changes\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\", \"minItems\": 1,\n      \"items\": {\n        \"type\": \"object\",\n        \"required\": [\"file\",\"description\"],\n        \"properties\": {\n          \"file\":        {\n            \"type\": \"string\",\n            \"description\": \"Must be under rtl/ (any extension) or be a test/test_*.py cocotb suite. Anything else is rejected by the runtime sandbox check.\",\n            \"pattern\": \"^(rtl/[^.].*|test/test_[^/]+\\\\.py)$\"\n          },\n          \"description\": {\"type\": \"string\"}\n        }\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_5", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg -i 'predictor|successor|predicting' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl | python -c 'import sys,json; rows=[json.loads(l) for l in sys.stdin]; print(list(rows[-1])); print(*[(r.get(\\\"id\\\"),str(r.get(\\\"hypothesis\\\",\\\"\\\"))[:1800]) for r in rows],sep=\\\"\\\\n\\\")'\"", "aggregated_output": "['id', 'title', 'category', 'motivation', 'hypothesis', 'expected_impact', 'changes', 'outcome', 'fitness', 'delta_pct', 'vs_baseline', 'fmax_mhz', 'ipc_coremark', 'cycles', 'iterations', 'lut4', 'ff', 'seeds', 'perturbations', 'lutram', 'bsram', 'dsp', 'critical_path', 'logic_levels', 'formal_passed', 'cosim_passed', 'error', 'implementation_notes', 'timestamp', 'slot', 'round_id', 'lesson']\n('hyp-20261120-003-r1s2', \"{'motivation': 'Fetch advances to PC+4 even at a hot loop backedge or a direct call. Because\\\\nIF/ID is combinational, a correct next-PC prediction saves one fetch opportunity\\\\non a ready cycle. Backward loop branches and forward exit branches can share\\\\nthe same counter constructively if it records agreement with their respective\\\\ndisplacement biases.\\\\n', 'hypothesis': 'Predict backward conditional branches taken and forward branches fall-through.\\\\nUse the high bit of a 256-entry table of two-bit saturating counters to invert\\\\nthat prediction at sites that repeatedly disagree with the bias. Predict JAL\\\\ntaken and leave JALR sequential until EX. Decode direct targets from the\\\\ncurrent instruction, so aliases affect direction alone. On the prototype,\\\\nstalled CoreMark took 4,188,667 bracketed cycles versus 4,491,485 at baseline\\\\nand passed all five CRCs. Gowin reported 5.236, 5.528 and 5.528 MHz. The\\\\nmedian gives 13.20 iterations/s versus 12.12. The cycle improvement alone\\\\ngives 7.23% more iterations per cycle. The prototype used 16 additional\\\\nLUTRAMs and three additional flip-flops. It passed all 53 single-retire\\\\nfast formal checks.\\\\n', 'expected_impact': {'fitness_delta_pct': 9, 'confidence': 'medium'}, 'changes': [{'file': 'rtl/if_stage.sv', 'description': 'Implement a 256 x 2 distributed RAM indexed by PC[9:2], with one\\\\nasynchronous fetch read and one synchronous EX update. Initialize words\\\\nto 01 (weak agreement) at FPGA configuration and retain them on warm\\\\nreset. On update, increment the saved count on disagreement and decrement\\\\non agreement, saturating at 3 and 0. F\n…[17824 of 20896 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:9c2a983388ad1425]…\nw and 32-bit wrap,\\\\nbecause one displacement can cross at most one page. Register the\\\\ncandidate address, the crossing bit and whether the base source was\\\\navailable. This puts the check beside the memory instruction before it\\\\ncan assert a bus strobe.\\\\n\\\\nAn in-page hit issues in EX from a single address register. A crossing\\\\nor unavailable base costs one repair cycle. Suppress the request, hold\\\\nthe instruction, and overwrite the same register with forwarded rs1\\\\nplus the full signed displacement. The repaired instruction can issue\\\\non the next cycle and holds its request through backpressure. An accepted\\\\nload forwards from EX/MEM to the next instruction.\\\\n\\\\nA scratch implementation completed the ten timed iterations in 3,234,996\\\\ncycles with both stall generators and all five canonical CRCs. Gowin\\\\nplacement options 0, 1 and 2 reached 60.066, 61.400 and 61.400 MHz.\\\\nThe median gives 189.80 iterations/s, 7.50% above 176.55. At that cycle\\\\ncount, acceptance requires a median above 59.7411')\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
