{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"rg -n 'GOWIN|gw_sh|def run_|env\\\\[' tools/eval/gowin.py && cat bench/programs/Makefile | head -90 && ls /opt && ls /srv/hwebench/toolchain\"","aggregated_output":"22:GOWIN_HOME = Path(os.environ.get(\"GOWIN_HOME\", \"/opt/gowin\"))\n23:GOWIN_VERSION = \"1.9.11.03 Education\"\n35:    libs = [GOWIN_HOME / \"deps/root/usr/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu\", GOWIN_HOME / \"IDE/lib\"]\n36:    env[\"LD_LIBRARY_PATH\"] = \":\".join(map(str, libs))\n37:    env[\"QT_QPA_PLATFORM\"] = \"offscreen\"\n41:    env[\"XDG_RUNTIME_DIR\"] = str(xdg)\n128:def _run_gw_sh(outdir: Path, log: Path, env: dict) -> bool:\n133:        proc = subprocess.Popen([str(GOWIN_HOME / \"IDE/bin/gw_sh\"), \"build.tcl\"], cwd=outdir,\n158:    timed_out = _run_gw_sh(outdir, log, gowin_env(env, outdir))\nCROSS   := riscv32-unknown-elf\nCC      := $(CROSS)-gcc\n\n# CoreMark build knobs. Defaults are the canonical EEMBC reporting config\n# (2K data size, -O3); tools/eval/fpga.py's COREMARK_EXPECTED CRCs assume\n# exactly these defaults.\n# - COREMARK_SIZE: TOTAL_DATA_SIZE in coremark.h (#ifndef-guarded). 2000 is\n#   the EEMBC canonical reporting config (used by VexRiscv et al.); 6000\n#   makes the matrix/list/state working sets ~3x larger so the score is\n#   harder to inflate via register-resident working sets.\n# - COREMARK_OPT: gcc optimization. -O3 is the standard CoreMark publication\n#   flag; -O2 is what the V0 baseline used.\n# Defaults match VexRiscv's published CoreMark methodology so the\n# orchestrator's fitness number is directly comparable to public CoreMark\n# results. To override (e.g. for the prior 6K -O2 V0 baseline):\n#     make bench/programs/coremark.elf COREMARK_SIZE=6000 COREMARK_OPT=-O2\nCOREMARK_SIZE ?= 2000\nCOREMARK_OPT  ?= -O3\n\nCFLAGS  := -march=rv32im -mabi=ilp32 $(COREMARK_OPT) -static -nostartfiles \\\n           -specs=nano.specs -specs=nosys.specs \\\n           -T bench/programs/link.ld -Ibench/programs/coremark \\\n           -Ibench/programs/coremark/baremetal \\\n           -DTOTAL_DATA_SIZE=$(COREMARK_SIZE)\n\nSRCS := bench/programs/coremark/core_list_join.c \\\n        bench/programs/coremark/core_main.c \\\n        bench/programs/coremark/core_matrix.c \\\n        bench/programs/coremark/core_state.c \\\n        bench/programs/coremark/core_util.c \\\n        bench/programs/coremark/baremetal/core_portme.c \\\n        bench/programs/crt0.S\n\nbench/programs/coremark.elf: $(SRCS)\n\t$(CC) $(CFLAGS) $^ -o $@\n\nbench/programs/selftest.elf: bench/programs/selftest.S\n\t$(CC) -march=rv32im -mabi=ilp32 -static -nostartfiles \\\n\t  -T bench/programs/link.ld $< -o $@\n\n# Random full-trace programs (V2). The .S files are generated once by\n# gen_random_trace.py <seed> and committed, so every candidate runs the\n# same programs.\nRANDOM_ELFS := bench/programs/random1.elf bench/programs/random2.elf bench/programs/random3.elf\n\nbench/programs/random%.elf: bench/programs/random%.S\n\t$(CC) -march=rv32im -mabi=ilp32 -static -nostartfiles \\\n\t  -T bench/programs/link.ld $< -o $@\n\n.PHONY: all clean\nall: bench/programs/coremark.elf bench/programs/selftest.elf $(RANDOM_ELFS)\nclean:\n\trm -f bench/programs/*.elf\ngowin\nhwe-python\nhwe-toolchain\nbin\noss-cad-suite\nxpack-riscv-none-elf-gcc-15.2.0-1\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nr=[json.loads(l) for l in open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl')]\nprint(r[-1]['hypothesis']['hypothesis'])\nPY\nls cores/bench/test && ls /srv/hwebench/clones/gpt-6_2-astra_xhigh-v2-rep2/bench/programs/*.elf\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nr=[json.loads(l) for l in open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl')]\nprint(r[-1]['hypothesis']['hypothesis'])\nPY\nls cores/bench/test && ls /srv/hwebench/clones/gpt-6_2-astra_xhigh-v2-rep2/bench/programs/*.elf\"","aggregated_output":"Predict that adding a load or store's signed 12-bit displacement preserves\nits base register's 4 KiB page. In decode, take bits [31:12] from the\nselected base and compute only (base + displacement) modulo 8192.\nConcatenate the page with the low 12 sum bits. Comparing sum bit 12 with\nbase bit 12 detects every crossing, including borrow and 32-bit wrap,\nbecause one displacement can cross at most one page. Register the\ncandidate address, the crossing bit and whether the base source was\navailable. This puts the check beside the memory instruction before it\ncan assert a bus strobe.\n\nAn in-page hit issues in EX from a single address register. A crossing\nor unavailable base costs one repair cycle. Suppress the request, hold\nthe instruction, and overwrite the same register with forwarded rs1\nplus the full signed displacement. The repaired instruction can issue\non the next cycle and holds its request through backpressure. An accepted\nload forwards from EX/MEM to the next instruction.\n\nA scratch implementation completed the ten timed iterations in 3,234,996\ncycles with both stall generators and all five canonical CRCs. Gowin\nplacement options 0, 1 and 2 reached 60.066, 61.400 and 61.400 MHz.\nThe median gives 189.80 iterations/s, 7.50% above 176.55. At that cycle\ncount, acceptance requires a median above 59.7411 MHz. All 53 standard\nsingle-channel formal checks passed. The selftest and three random ELF\ntraces matched the reference with and without stalls.\nA directed test observed one accepted store after three denied cycles\nat a repaired address and consecutive retirement of a load and its branch.\n\nA matched control with full-width address adders also issued memory\noperations in EX. It took 3,235,018 cycles at 64.020 MHz. Early load\navailability accounts for the cycle gain over the champion. These\nplacements favor full-width adders for Fmax, so they do not establish\na separate frequency gain from predicting the page.\n\n_helpers.py\nconftest.py\ntest_alu.py\ntest_decoder.py\ntest_imm_gen.py\ntest_mul_product.py\ntest_pipeline.py\ntest_reg_file.py\n/srv/hwebench/clones/gpt-6_2-astra_xhigh-v2-rep2/bench/programs/coremark.elf\n/srv/hwebench/clones/gpt-6_2-astra_xhigh-v2-rep2/bench/programs/random1.elf\n/srv/hwebench/clones/gpt-6_2-astra_xhigh-v2-rep2/bench/programs/random2.elf\n/srv/hwebench/clones/gpt-6_2-astra_xhigh-v2-rep2/bench/programs/random3.elf\n/srv/hwebench/clones/gpt-6_2-astra_xhigh-v2-rep2/bench/programs/selftest.elf\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
