{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_10", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor l in open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'):\n a=json.loads(l)\n if a['id'] in ('hyp-20261120-002-r7s1','hyp-20261120-001-r7s0','hyp-20261120-003-r7s2'):\n  print(a['id'],a['hypothesis']['hypothesis'],a['hypothesis']['changes'])\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "hyp-20261120-001-r7s0 Retime the M-extension result bypass. Forward DIV/REM from MEM/WB like\nMUL, and compare consumer source tags with both potential producers one\nstage earlier. Moving the divide result past EX/MEM frees the EX transfer\nedge for arithmetic. Seed with two dividend bits on the first wait clock\nwhile registering 3D, 5D and 7D. Take five bits on each of the next five\nwait clocks and on the transfer edge. Within each five-bit group take a\nradix-4 digit first and a radix-8 digit second. This covers all 32 bits\nwith ten trial subtractors across the two stages, down from fourteen.\nMEM selects and sign-corrects the registered quotient or remainder.\n\nIn parallel with decoding each consumer, register the younger rd match\nand the older writer match for each source. In EX, qualify the younger\nmatch with the actual EX/MEM write enable and late-result flag, then give\nit priority. This retains trap suppression and takes both five-bit tag\ncomparisons off the path through the EX operand and result muxes.\n\nA scratch build reached 74.626, 76.825 and 76.825 MHz across the three\nGowin placements. The matched champion reproduced its 65.467 MHz median.\nMoving division to MEM/WB with the same five-bit groups and the original\ntag comparisons reached 68.274 MHz. With both bus stall generators enabled,\nthe full prototype completed ten iterations in 3,234,996 bracketed cycles\nwith all five canonical CRCs and the CoreMark validation message. Its median\ngives 237.48 iterations/s, a 17.35% gain over 202.37. Acceptance requires\nover 68.478 MHz at that cycle count. Selftest and all three random ELF\nretirement traces matched the reference both with and without bus stalls.\nA directed test confirmed that a younger trapping JAL with a matching rd\nlets the older writer supply both operands, and that a store retains its\nforwarded value through four denied bus cycles. The scratch cocotb suite\npassed, including the divider reference vectors and a pair of independent\ndivides that retired eight cycles apart.\n [{'file': 'rtl/alu.sv', 'des\n…[8501 of 11573 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:ef17424f930b0c20]…\na denied aligned load. Keep the row aligned with EX across holds and\\nre-read at the corrected index on the repair edge. Store tag [19:11] and\\nreject any EX address with nonzero bits [31:20]. Format the live and\\npredicted words in parallel, registering the predicted result and its\\nselect bit beside EX/MEM. Use the selected raw word for RVFI.\\n'}, {'file': 'rtl/core.sv', 'description': 'Connect the speculative read index and distinguish a verified local read\\nfrom a pending external request. Keep annulled, misaligned and MMIO loads\\nout of replay. An EX word load used as the next address base must supply\\nthe selected word or take the existing unavailable-base repair.\\n'}, {'file': 'test/test_pipeline.py', 'description': 'Warm a replay row. Deny a dependent load while driving unrelated bus\\ndata and check its retirement, forwarding and RVFI byte mask. Exercise\\npartial stores followed by narrow and wide reads, equal-index aliases,\\nreset, collisions and a repaired address under sustained backpressure.\\n'}]\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
